#. type: Title =
#: src/drivers/pmx485.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Powermax Modbus Driver"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pmx485.adoc:14
msgid ""
"This is a non-realtime HAL program, written in python, to control Hypetherm "
"Powermax plasma cutters using the Modbus ASCII protocol over RS485."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pmx485.adoc:16
msgid ""
"Since this is a non-realtime program it can be affected by computer loading "
"and latency. It is possible to lose communications which will be indicated "
"by a change in the status output. One should always have an Estop circuit "
"that kills the power to the unit in case of emergency."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/pmx485.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "loadusr -Wn pmx485 pmx485 /dev/ttyUSB0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pmx485.adoc:26
msgid ""
"This will load the pmx485 component using the /dev/ttyUSB0 port and wait for "
"it to become ready."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pmx485.adoc:28
msgid "It is necessary to name the port to use for communications."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pmx485.adoc:32
