#. type: Title =
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Servo To Go Driver"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:18
msgid ""
"The Servo-To-Go (STG) is one of the first PC motion control cards supported "
"by LinuxCNC. It is an ISA card and it exists in different flavors (all "
"supported by this driver). The board includes up to 8 channels of quadrature "
"encoder input, 8 channels of analog input and output, 32 bits digital I/O, "
"an interval timer with interrupt and a watchdog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:25
msgid ""
"We have had reports that the opamps on the Servo To Go card do not work with "
"newer ATX power supplies that use modern switch mode DC-DC converters.  The "
"failure mode is that STG card outputs a constant voltage regardless of what "
"the driver is commanding it to do.  Older ATX power supplies with linear "
"voltage regulators do not have this problem, and work fine with the STG "
"cards."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"loadrt hal_stg [base=<address>] [num_chan=<nr>] [dio=\"<dio-string>\"] \\\n"
"                 [model=<model>]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:46
msgid ""
"The base address field is optional; if it's not provided the driver attempts "
"to autodetect the board. The num_chan field is used to specify the number of "
"channels available on the card, if not used the 8 axis version is assumed. "
"The digital inputs/outputs configuration is determined by a config string "
"passed to insmod when loading the module.  The format consists of a four "
"character string that sets the direction of each group of pins. Each "
"character of the direction string is either \"I\" or \"O\". The first "
"character sets the direction of port A (Port A - DIO.0-7), the next sets "
"port B (Port B - DIO.8-15), the next sets port C (Port C - DIO.16-23), and "
"the fourth sets port D (Port D - DIO.24-31). The model field can be used in "
"case the driver doesn't autodetect the right card version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:50
msgid ""
"HINT: after starting up the driver, 'dmesg' can be consulted for messages "
"relevant to the driver (e.g. autodetected version number and base address). "
"For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "loadrt hal_stg base=0x300 num_chan=4 dio=\"IOIO\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:62
msgid ""
"This example installs the STG driver for a card found at the base address of "
"0x300, 4 channels of encoder feedback, DACs and ADCs, along with 32 bits of "
"I/O configured like this: the first 8 (Port A)  configured as Input, the "
"next 8 (Port B) configured as Output, the next 8 (Port C) configured as "
"Input, and the last 8 (Port D) configured as Output"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "loadrt hal_stg\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:72
msgid ""
"This example installs the driver and attempts to autodetect the board "
"address and board model, it installs 8 axes by default along with a standard "
"I/O setup: Port A & B configured as Input, Port C & D configured as Output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:76
msgid "'stg.<channel>.counts' - (s32) Tracks the counted encoder ticks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:77
msgid "'stg.<channel>.position' - (float) Outputs a converted position."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:79
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.dac-value' - (float) Drives the voltage for the corresponding "
"DAC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:81
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.adc-value' - (float) Tracks the measured voltage from the "
"corresponding ADC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:82
msgid "'stg.in-<pinnum>' - (bit) Tracks a physical input pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:84
msgid ""
"'stg.in-<pinnum>-not' - (bit) Tracks a physical input pin, but inverted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:85
msgid "'stg.out-<pinnum>' - (bit) Drives a physical output pin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:90
msgid ""
"For each pin, <channel> is the axis number, and <pinnum> is the logic pin "
"number of the STG if `IIOO` is defined, there are 16 input pins (in-00 .. "
"in-15) and 16 output pins (out-00 .. out-15), and they correspond to PORTs "
"ABCD (in-00 is PORTA.0, out-15 is PORTD.7)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:95
msgid ""
"The in-<pinnum> HAL pin is TRUE if the physical pin is high, and FALSE if "
"the physical pin is low. The in-<pinnum>-not HAL pin is inverted -- it is "
"FALSE if the physical pin is high. By connecting a signal to one or the "
"other, the user can determine the state of the input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:100
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.position-scale' - (float) The number of counts / user unit "
"(to convert from counts to units)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:102
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.dac-offset' - (float) Sets the offset for the corresponding "
"DAC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:104
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.dac-gain' - (float) Sets the gain of the corresponding DAC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:106
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.adc-offset' - (float) Sets the offset of the corresponding "
"ADC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:108
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.adc-gain' - (float) Sets the gain of the corresponding ADC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:109
msgid "'stg.out-<pinnum>-invert' - (bit) Inverts an output pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:115
msgid ""
"The -invert parameter determines whether an output pin is active high or "
"active low. If -invert is FALSE, setting the HAL out- pin TRUE drives the "
"physical pin high, and FALSE drives it low. If -invert is TRUE, then setting "
"the HAL out- pin TRUE will drive the physical pin low."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:120
msgid ""
"'stg.capture-position' - Reads the encoder counters from the axis <channel>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:121
msgid "'stg.write-dacs' - Writes the voltages to the DACs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:122
msgid "'stg.read-adcs' - Reads the voltages from the ADCs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:124
msgid ""
"'stg.di-read' - Reads physical in- pins of all ports and updates all HAL in-"
"<pinnum> and in-<pinnum>-not pins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:126
msgid ""
"'stg.do-write' - Reads all HAL out-<pinnum> pins and updates all physical "
"output pins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shuttle"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:10 src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:16
msgid ""
"Shuttle is a non-realtime HAL component that interfaces Contour Design's "
"ShuttleXpress, ShuttlePRO, and ShuttlePRO2 devices with LinuxCNC's HAL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:14 src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:20
msgid ""
"If the driver is started without command-line arguments, it will probe all /"
"dev/hidraw* device files for Shuttle devices, and use all devices found.  If "
"it is started with command-line arguments, it will only probe the devices "
"specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:17 src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:23
msgid ""
"The ShuttleXpress has five momentary buttons, a 10 counts/revolution jog "
"wheel with detents, and a 15-position spring-loaded outer wheel that returns "
"to center when released."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:20 src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:26
msgid ""
"The ShuttlePRO has 13 momentary buttons, a 10 counts/revolution jog wheel "
"with detents, and a 15-position spring-loaded outer wheel that returns to "
"center when released."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:23 src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:29
msgid ""
"The ShuttlePRO2 has 15 momentary buttons, a 10 counts/revolution jog wheel "
"with detents, and a 15-position spring-loaded outer wheel that returns to "
"center when released."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:29
msgid ""
"The Shuttle devices have an internal 8-bit counter for the current jog-wheel "
"position.  The shuttle driver can not know this value until the Shuttles "
"device sends its first event.  When the first event comes into the driver, "
"the driver uses the device's reported jog-wheel position to initialize "
"counts to 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:31
msgid ""
"This means that if the first event is generated by a jog-wheel move, that "
"first move will be lost."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:34 src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:59
msgid ""
"Any user interaction with the Shuttle device will generate an event, "
"informing the driver of the jog-wheel position.  So if you (for example) "
"push one of the buttons at startup, the jog-wheel will work fine and notice "
"the first click."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:37 src/gui/touchy.adoc:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup"
msgstr "მორგება"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:42
msgid ""
"The shuttle driver needs read permission to the /dev/hidraw* device files. "
"This can be accomplished by adding a file /etc/udev/rules.d/99-"
"shuttle.rules, with the following contents:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SUBSYSTEM==\"hidraw\", ATTRS{idVendor}==\"0b33\", ATTRS{idProduct}==\"0020\", MODE=\"0444\"\n"
"SUBSYSTEM==\"hidraw\", ATTRS{idVendor}==\"05f3\", ATTRS{idProduct}==\"0240\", MODE=\"0444\"\n"
"SUBSYSTEM==\"hidraw\", ATTRS{idVendor}==\"0b33\", ATTRS{idProduct}==\"0030\", MODE=\"0444\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:52
msgid ""
"The LinuxCNC Debian package installs an appropriate udev file automatically, "
"but if you are building LinuxCNC from source and are not using the Debian "
"packaging you'll need to install this file by hand.  If you install the file "
"by hand you'll need to tell udev to reload its rules files by running "
"`udevadm control --reload-rules`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:57
msgid ""
"All HAL pin names are prefixed with `shuttle` followed by the index of the "
"device (the order in which the driver found them), for example `shuttle.0` "
"or `shuttle.2`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<Prefix>_`.button-<ButtonNumber>` (bit out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:60
msgid "These pins are True (1) when the button is pressed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<Prefix>_`.button-<ButtonNumber>-not` (bit out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:62
msgid ""
"These pins have the inverse of the button state, so they're True (1) when "
"the button is not pressed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<Prefix>_`.counts` (s32 out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:64 src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:71
msgid "Accumulated counts from the jog wheel (the inner wheel)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<Prefix>_`.spring-wheel-s32` (s32 out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:67 src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:74
msgid ""
"The current deflection of the spring-wheel (the outer wheel).  It's 0 at "
"rest, and ranges from -7 at the counter-clockwise extreme to +7 at the "
"clockwise extreme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<Prefix>_`.spring-wheel-f` (float out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/shuttle.adoc:71
msgid ""
"The current deflection of the spring-wheel (the outer wheel).  It's 0.0 at "
"rest, -1.0 at the counter-clockwise extreme, and +1.0 at the clockwise "
"extreme.  The Shuttle devices report the spring-wheel position as an integer "
"from -7 to +7, so this pin reports only 15 discrete values in it's range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "VFS11 VFD Driver"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:12
msgid ""
"This is a non-realtime HAL program to control the S11 series of VFDs from "
"Toshiba."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:16
msgid ""
"vfs11_vfd supports serial and TCP connections.  Serial connections may be "
"RS232 or RS485. RS485 is supported in full- and half-duplex mode.  TCP "
"connections may be passive (wait for incoming connection), or active "
"outgoing connections, which may be useful to connect to TCP-based devices or "
"through a terminal server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:18
msgid ""
"Regardless of the connection type, vfs11_vfd operates as a Modbus master."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "loadusr -Wn spindle-vfd vfs11_vfd -n spindle-vfd\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:27
msgid ""
"The above command says: loadusr, wait for named to load, component "
"vfs11_vfd, named spindle-vfd"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:31
msgid ""
"'vfs11_vfd' is mostly configured through INI file options. The command line "
"options are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:33
msgid "'-n or --name <halname>' : set the HAL component name"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:35
msgid ""
"'-I or --ini <inifilename>' : take configuration from this INI file.  "
"Defaults to environment variable INI_FILE_NAME."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:36
msgid ""
"'-S or --section <section name>' : take configuration from this section in "
"the INI file. Defaults to 'VFS11'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:37
msgid "'-d or --debug' enable debug messages on console output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:38
msgid "'-m or --modbus-debug' enable modbus messages on console output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:39
msgid "'-r or --report-device' report device properties on console at startup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:42
msgid ""
"Debugging can be toggled by sending a USR1 signal to the vfs11_vfd process.  "
"Modbus debugging can be toggled by sending a USR2 signal to vfs11_vfd "
"process (example: +kill -USR1 \\`pidof vfs11_vfd`+)."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:49 src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:125
msgid ""
"Where <n> is +vfs11_vfd+ or the name given during loading with the -n option."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:51
msgid ""
"'<n>.acceleration-pattern' (bit, in) when true, set acceleration and "
"deceleration times as defined in registers F500 and F501 respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:52
msgid "Used in PID loops to choose shorter ramp times to avoid oscillation."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:55
msgid ""
"'<n>.alarm-code' (s32, out) non-zero if drive is in alarmed state.  Bitmap "
"describing alarm information (see register FC91 description).  Use err-reset "
"(see below) to clear the alarm."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:57
msgid ""
"'<n>.at-speed' (bit, out)  when drive is at commanded speed (see speed-"
"tolerance below)"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:59
msgid "'<n>.current-load-percentage' (float, out)  reported from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:61
msgid ""
"'<n>.dc-brake' (bit, in)  engage the DC brake. Also turns off spindle-on."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:64
msgid ""
"'<n>.enable' (bit, in)  enable the VFD.  If false, all operating parameters "
"are still read but control is released and panel control is enabled (subject "
"to VFD setup)."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:67
msgid ""
"'<n>.err-reset' (bit, in)  reset errors (alarms a.k.a Trip and e-stop "
"status).  Resetting the VFD may cause a 2-second delay until it's rebooted "
"and Modbus is up again."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:70
msgid ""
"'<n>.estop' (bit, in)  put the VFD into emergency-stopped status.  No "
"operation possible until cleared with err-reset or powercycling."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:72
msgid ""
"'<n>.frequency-command' (float, out)  current target frequency in Hz as set "
"through speed-command (which is in RPM), from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:74
msgid "'<n>.frequency-out' (float, out)  current output frequency of the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:76
msgid ""
"'<n>.inverter-load-percentage' (float, out)  current load report from VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:79
msgid ""
"'<n>.is-e-stopped' (bit, out)  the VFD is in emergency stop status (blinking "
"\"E\" on panel).  Use err-reset to reboot the VFD and clear the e- stop "
"status."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:81
msgid "'<n>.is-stopped' (bit, out)  true when the VFD reports 0 Hz output"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:88
msgid ""
"'<n>.max-rpm' (float, R)  actual RPM limit based on maximum frequency the "
"VFD may generate, and the motors nameplate values.  For instance, if "
"nameplate-HZ is 50, and nameplate-RPM_ is 1410, but the VFD may generate up "
"to 80 Hz, then max-rpm would read as 2256 (80*1410/50).  The frequency limit "
"is read from the VFD at startup.  To increase the upper frequency limit, the "
"UL and FH parameters must be changed on the panel.  See the VF-S11 manual "
"for instructions how to set the maximum frequency."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:90
msgid ""
"'<n>.modbus-ok' (bit, out)  true when the Modbus session is successfully "
"established and the last 10 transactions returned without error."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:92
msgid "'<n>.motor-RPM' (float, out)  estimated current RPM value, from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:94
msgid "'<n>.output-current-percentage' (float, out)  from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:96
msgid "'<n>.output-voltage-percentage' (float, out)  from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:98
msgid "'<n>.output-voltage' (float, out)  from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:100
msgid ""
"'<n>.speed-command' (float, in)  speed sent to VFD in RPM. It is an error to "
"send a speed faster than the Motor Max RPM as set in the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:102
msgid "'<n>.spindle-fwd' (bit, in)  1 for FWD and 0 for REV, sent to VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:104
msgid ""
"'<n>.spindle-on' (bit, in)  1 for ON and 0 for OFF sent to VFD, only on when "
"running"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:106
msgid ""
"'<n>.spindle-rev' (bit, in)  1 for ON and 0 for OFF, only on when running"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:111
msgid ""
"'<n>.jog-mode' (bit, in)  1 for ON and 0 for OFF, enables the VF-S11 'jog "
"mode'.  Speed control is disabled, and the output frequency is determined by "
"register F262 (preset to 5 Hz).  This might be useful for spindle "
"orientation.  In normal mode, the VFD shuts off if the frequency drops below "
"12 Hz."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:114
msgid ""
"'<n>.status' (s32, out)  Drive Status of the VFD (see the TOSVERT VF-S11 "
"Communications Function Instruction Manual, register FD01).  A bitmap."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:116
msgid "'<n>.trip-code' (s32, out)  trip code if VF-S11 is in tripped state."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:118
msgid ""
"'<n>.error-count' (s32, out)  number of Modbus transactions which returned "
"an error"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:121
msgid ""
"'<n>.max-speed' (bit, in)  ignore the loop-time parameter and run Modbus at "
"maximum speed, at the expense of higher CPU usage.  Suggested use during "
"spindle positioning."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:128
msgid "'<n>.frequency-limit' (float, RO)  upper limit read from VFD setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:130
msgid ""
"'<n>.loop-time' (float, RW)  how often the Modbus is polled (default "
"interval 0.1 seconds)"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:132
msgid ""
"'<n>.nameplate-HZ' (float, RW)  Nameplate Hz of motor (default 50). Used to "
"calculate target frequency (together with nameplate-RPM ) for a target RPM "
"value as given by speed-command."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:134
msgid "'<n>.nameplate-RPM' (float, RW)  Nameplate RPM of motor (default 1410)"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:136
msgid ""
"'<n>.rpm-limit' (float, RW)  do-not-exceed soft limit for motor RPM "
"(defaults to nameplate-RPM )."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:139
msgid ""
"'<n>.tolerance' (float, RW)  speed tolerance (default 0.01) for determining "
"whether spindle is at speed (0.01 meaning: Output frequency is within 1% of "
"target frequency)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:140
#, no-wrap
msgid "INI file configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:144
msgid ""
"This lists all options understood by vfs11_vfd.  Typical setups for RS-232, "
"RS-485 and TCP can be found in 'src/hal/user_comps/vfs11_vfd/*.ini'."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[VFS11]\n"
"# serial connection\n"
"TYPE=rtu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:153
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# serial port\n"
"DEVICE=/dev/ttyS0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:156
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# TCP server - wait for incoming connection\n"
"TYPE=tcpserver\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:159
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# tcp portnumber for TYPE=tcpserver or tcpclient\n"
"PORT=1502\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:162
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# TCP client - active outgoing connection\n"
"TYPE=tcpclient\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:165
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# destination to connect to if TYPE=tcpclient\n"
"TCPDEST=192.168.1.1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:170
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#---------- meaningful only if TYPE=rtu -------\n"
"# serial device detail\n"
"# 5 6 7 8\n"
"BITS= 5\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:173
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# even odd none\n"
"PARITY=none\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:176
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# 110, 300, 600, 1200, 2400, 4800, 9600, 19200, 38400, 57600, 115200\n"
"BAUD=19200\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:179
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# 1 2\n"
"STOPBITS=1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:182
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#rs232 rs485\n"
"SERIAL_MODE=rs485\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:189
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# up down none\n"
"# this feature might not work with a stock Ubuntu\n"
"# libmodbus5/libmodbus-dev package, and generate a warning\n"
"# execution will continue as if RTS_MODE=up were given.\n"
"RTS_MODE=up\n"
"#---------------------\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:195
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# modbus timers in seconds\n"
"# inter-character timer\n"
"BYTE_TIMEOUT=0.5\n"
"# packet timer\n"
"RESPONSE_TIMEOUT=0.5\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:198
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# target modbus ID\n"
"TARGET=1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:202
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# on I/O failure, try to reconnect after sleeping\n"
"# for RECONNECT_DELAY seconds\n"
"RECONNECT_DELAY=1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:207
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# misc. parameters\n"
"DEBUG=10\n"
"MODBUS_DEBUG=0\n"
"POLLCYCLES=10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:218
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#\n"
"# example usage of the VF-S11 VFD driver\n"
"#\n"
"#\n"
"loadusr -Wn spindle-vfd vfs11_vfd -n spindle-vfd\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:222
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the spindle direction pins to the VFD\n"
"net vfs11-fwd spindle-vfd.spindle-fwd <= spindle.0.forward\n"
"net vfs11-rev spindle-vfd.spindle-rev <= spindle.0.reverse\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:225
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the spindle on pin to the VF-S11\n"
"net vfs11-run spindle-vfd.spindle-on <= spindle.0.on\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:228
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the VF-S11 at speed to the motion at speed\n"
"net vfs11-at-speed spindle.0.at-speed <= spindle-vfd.at-speed\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:231
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the spindle RPM to the VF-S11\n"
"net vfs11-RPM spindle-vfd.speed-command <= spindle.0.speed-out\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:236
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the VF-S11 DC brake\n"
"# since this draws power during spindle off, the dc-brake pin would\n"
"# better be driven by a monoflop which triggers on spindle-on falling edge\n"
"#net vfs11-spindle-brake spindle.N.brake => spindle-vfd.dc-brake\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:240
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# to use the VFS11 jog mode for spindle orient\n"
"# see orient.9 and motion.9\n"
"net spindle-orient spindle.0.orient spindle-vfd.max-speed spindle-vfd.jog-mode\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:243
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# take precedence over control panel\n"
"setp spindle-vfd.enable 1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:245
#, no-wrap
msgid "Panel operation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:252
msgid ""
"The vfs11_vfd driver takes precedence over panel control while it is enabled "
"(see 'enable' pin), effectively disabling the panel.  Clearing the 'enable' "
"pin re-enables the panel.  Pins and parameters can still be set, but will "
"not be written to the VFD untile the 'enable' pin is set.  Operating "
"parameters are still read while bus control is disabled.  Exiting the "
"vfs11_vfd driver in a controlled way will release the VFD from the bus and "
"restore panel control."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:255
msgid ""
"See the LinuxCNC Integrators Manual for more information.  For a detailed "
"register description of the Toshiba VFDs, see the \"TOSVERT VF-S11 "
"Communications Function Instruction Manual\" (Toshiba document number "
"E6581222) and the \"TOSVERT VF-S11 Instruction manual\" (Toshiba document "
"number E6581158)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:256
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error Recovery"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:259
msgid ""
"+vfs11_vfd+ recovers from I/O errors as follows: First, all HAL pins are set "
"to default values, and the driver will sleep for +RECONNECT_DELAY+ seconds "
"(default 1 second)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:261
msgid "Serial (+TYPE=rtu+) mode: on error, close and reopen the serial port."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:262
msgid ""
"TCP server (+TYPE=tcpserver+) mode: on losing the TCP connection, the driver "
"will go back to listen for incoming connections."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:263
msgid ""
"TCP client (+TYPE=tcpclient+) mode: on losing the TCP connection, the driver "
"will reconnect to 'TCPDEST:PORTNO'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:264
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuring the VFS11 VFD for Modbus usage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:274
msgid ""
"The VF-S11 has an RJ-45 jack for serial communication.  Unfortunately, it "
"does not have a standard RS-232 plug and logic levels.  The Toshiba-"
"recommended way is: connect the USB001Z USB-to-serial conversion unit to the "
"drive, and plug the USB port into the PC.  A cheaper alternative is a "
"homebrew interface ( https://git.mah.priv.at/gitweb/vfs11-vfd.git/blob_plain/"
"refs/heads/f12-prod:/VFS11-RJ45_e.pdf[hints from Toshiba support], https://"
"git.mah.priv.at/gitweb/vfs11-vfd.git/blob_plain/refs/heads/f12-prod:/vfs11-"
"rs232.pdf[circuit diagram])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:276
msgid "Note: the 24V output from the VFD has no short-circuit protection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:278
msgid ""
"Serial port factory defaults are 9600/8/1/even, the protocol defaults to the "
"proprietary \"Toshiba Inverter Protocol\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:285
msgid ""
"Several parameters need setting before the VF-S11 will talk to this module.  "
"This can either be done manually with the control panel, or over the serial "
"link - Toshiba supplies a Windows application called 'PCM001Z' which can "
"read/set parameters in the VFD.  Note - PCM001Z only talks the Toshiba "
"inverter protocol.  So the last parameter which you'd want to change is the "
"protocol - set from Toshiba Inverter Protocol to Modbus; thereafter, the "
"Windows app is useless."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:288
msgid ""
"To increase the upper frequency limit, the UL and FH parameters must be "
"changed on the panel.  I increased them from 50 to 80."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:292
msgid ""
"See dump-params.mio for a description of non-standard VF-S11 parameters of "
"my setup.  This file is for the https://git.mah.priv.at/gitweb/"
"modio.git[modio Modbus interactive utility]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:293
#, no-wrap
msgid "Programming Note"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:296
msgid ""
"The vfs11_vfd driver uses the https://www.libmodbus.org[libmodbus version 3] "
"library which is more recent than the version 2 code used in +gs2_vfd+."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:300
msgid ""
"The Ubuntu +libmodbus5+ and +libmodbus-dev+ packages are only available "
"starting from Ubuntu 12 ('Precise Pengolin').  Moreover, these packages lack "
"support for the MODBUS_RTS_MODE_* flags.  Therefore, building vfs11_vfd "
"using this library might generate a warning if RTS_MODE= is specified in the "
"INI file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:302
msgid "To use the full functionality on lucid and precise:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:304
msgid ""
"remove the libmodbus packages: `sudo apt-get remove libmodbus5 libmodbus-dev`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:306
msgid ""
"build and install libmodbus version 3 from source as outlined https://"
"github.com/stephane/libmodbus/blob/master/README.rst[here]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:308
msgid ""
"Libmodbus does not build on Ubuntu Hardy, hence vfs11_vfd is not available "
"on Hardy."
msgstr ""

