#. type: Title ===
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normal Download"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:44
msgid ""
"Software for LinuxCNC to download is presented on the project's https://"
"linuxcnc.org/downloads/[Downloads page].  Most users will aim for the disk "
"image for Intel/AMD PCs, the URL will resemble https://www.linuxcnc.org/iso/"
"linuxcnc_2.9.8-amd64.hybrid.iso."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:47
msgid ""
"For the Raspberry Pi, multiple images are provided to address differences "
"between the RPi4 and RPi5."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:51
msgid ""
"Do not use the regular Raspbian distribution for LinuxCNC that may have "
"shipped with your RPi starter kit - that will not have the real-time kernel "
"and you cannot migrate from Raspbian to Debian's kernel image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download using zsync"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:60
msgid ""
"zsync is a download application that efficiently resumes interrupted "
"downloads and efficiently transfers large files with small modifications (if "
"you have an older local copy). Please note, it needs to use the http "
"protocol, not https. Use zsync if your download of the image using the "
"<<_normal_download,Normal Download>> method is frequently interrupted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "zsync in Linux"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:64
msgid ""
"Install zsync using Synaptic or, by running the following in a "
"<<faq:terminal,terminal>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo apt-get install zsync\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:69
msgid "Then run this command to download the iso to your computer"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "zsync https://www.linuxcnc.org/iso/linuxcnc_2.9.8-amd64.hybrid.iso\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/getting-linuxcnc.adoc:77
msgid ""
"Please remember to confirm the checksum of the downloaded iso as described "
"below, since the authenticity of the server is not guaranteed with the http "
"protocol."
msgstr ""

