#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/system-requirements.adoc:68
#: src/getting-started/updating-linuxcnc.adoc:67
msgid ""
"If you see (as above) `-rt-` in the kernel name then you are running the "
"preempt-rt kernel and should install the \"uspace\" version of LinuxCNC.  "
"You should also install uspace for \"sim\" configs on non-realtime kernels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/system-requirements.adoc:71
msgid ""
"If you see `-rtai-` in the kernel name then you are running RTAI realtime. "
"See below for the LinuxCNC version to install."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/getting-started/system-requirements.adoc:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preempt-RT with 'linuxcnc-uspace' package"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/system-requirements.adoc:83
msgid ""
"Preempt-RT is the newest of the realtime systems, and is also the version "
"that is closest to a mainline kernel. Preempt-RT kernels are available as "
"precompiled packages from the main repositories. The search term "
"\"PREEMPT_RT\" will find them, and one can be downloaded and installed just "
"like any other package.  Preempt-RT will generally have the best driver "
"support and is the only option for systems using the Mesa ethernet-connected "
"hardware driver cards. In general preempt-rt has the worst latency of the "
"available systems, but there are exceptions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/getting-started/system-requirements.adoc:84
#, no-wrap
msgid "RTAI with 'linuxcnc' package"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/system-requirements.adoc:92
msgid ""
"RTAI has been the mainstay of LinuxCNC distributions for many years. It will "
"generally give the best realtime performance in terms of low latency, but "
"might have poorer peripheral support and not as many screen resolutions. An "
"RTAI kernel is available from the LinuxCNC package repository. If you "
"installed from the Live/Install image then switching kernel and LinuxCNC "
"flavour is described in [Installing-RTAI]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/getting-started/system-requirements.adoc:93
#, no-wrap
msgid "Xenomai with 'linuxcnc-uspace' package"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/system-requirements.adoc:97
msgid ""
"Xenomai is also supported, but you will have to find or build the kernel and "
"compile LinuxCNC from source to utilise it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/getting-started/system-requirements.adoc:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "RTAI with 'linuxcnc-uspace' package"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/system-requirements.adoc:102
msgid ""
"It is also possible to run LinuxCNC with RTAI in user-space mode.  As with "
"Xenomai you will need to compile from source to do this."
msgstr ""

