#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:25 src/gui/mdro.adoc:29 src/gui/tklinuxcnc.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr "საერთო ინფორმაცია"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:30
msgid ""
"If your configuration is not currently set up to use AXIS, you can change it "
"by editing the .ini file (INI file). In the section `[DISPLAY]` change the "
"`[DISPLAY]` line to read `DISPLAY = axis`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:32
msgid ""
"The sample configuration 'sim/axis.ini' is already configured to use AXIS as "
"its front-end."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:35
msgid ""
"When AXIS starts, a window like the one in the figure <<fig:axis-window>> "
"above opens."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:42
msgid ""
"For more information on INI file settings that can change how AXIS works see "
"the <<sub:ini:sec:display,Display Section>> and the <<sub:ini:sec:axis-"
"letter,Axis Section>> of the INI Configuration Chapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'CYCLE_TIME' - Adjust the response rate of the GUI in milliseconds. Typical 100, useable range 50 - 200\n"
"(will accept time in seconds (.05 -.2) for legacy reasons - milliseconds preferred to match other screens)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:59
msgid ""
"'PREVIEW_TIMEOUT' - Set timeout in seconds for loading G-code preview.  If "
"parsing the G-code lasts longer than this, a notice is shown and only the "
"initial part of the program is drawn in the graphical display. Specifying 0 "
"or leaving the setting out results in no timeout."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"PREVIEW_TIMEOUT = 5\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Typical Session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:69
msgid "Launch LinuxCNC and select a configuration file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:70
msgid "Release the E-STOP button (F1) and turn the Machine Power on (F2)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:71
msgid "Home all axes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:72
msgid "Load the G-code file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:73
msgid "Use the preview plot to verify that the program is correct."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:74
msgid "Load the material."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:76
msgid ""
"Set the proper offset for each axis by jogging and using the `Touch Off` "
"button as needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:77 src/gui/tklinuxcnc.adoc:56
msgid "Run the program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:79
msgid ""
"To machine the same file again, return to step 6.  To machine a different "
"file, return to step 4."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:80
msgid "When the job is complete, exit AXIS."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:87
msgid ""
"To run the same program again depends on your setup and requirements.  You "
"might need to load more material and set offsets or move over and set an "
"offset then run the program again. If your material is fixtured then you "
"might need to only run the program again. See the <<sub:axis-machine-"
"menu,Machine Menu>> for more information on the run command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "AXIS Window"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:91
msgid "The AXIS window contains the following elements:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:93
msgid "A display area that shows one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:97
msgid ""
"A preview of the loaded file (in this case, 'axis.ngc'), as well as the "
"current location of the CNC machine's 'controlled point'. Later, this area "
"will display the path the CNC machine has moved through, called the "
"'backplot'."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:98
msgid "A large readout showing the current position and all offsets."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:99
msgid "A menu bar and toolbar that allow you to perform various actions"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:102
msgid ""
"'Manual Control Tab' - which allows you to make the machine move, turn the "
"spindle on or off, and turn the coolant on or off if included in the INI "
"file."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:105
msgid ""
"'MDI Tab' - where G-code programs can be entered manually, one line at a "
"time. This also shows the 'Active G-codes' which shows which modal G-codes "
"are in effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:109
msgid ""
"'Feed Override' - which allows you to scale the speed of programmed "
"motions.  The default maximum is 120% and can be set to a different value in "
"the INI file. See the <<sub:ini:sec:display,Display Section>> of the INI "
"file for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:110
msgid ""
"'Spindle Override' - which allows you to scale the spindle speed up or down."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:112
msgid ""
"'Jog Speed' - which allows you to set the jog speed within the limits set in "
"the INI file.  See the <<sub:ini:sec:display,Display Section>> of the INI "
"file for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:114
msgid ""
"'Max Velocity' - which allows you to restrict the maximum velocity of all "
"programmed motions (except spindle synchronized motion)."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:115
msgid "A text display area that shows the loaded G-code."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:119
msgid ""
"A status bar which shows the state of the machine. In this screen shot, the "
"machine is turned on, does not have a tool inserted, and the displayed "
"position is 'Relative' (showing all offsets), and 'Actual' (showing feedback "
"position)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu Items"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:125
msgid ""
"Some menu items might be grayed out depending on how you have your INI file "
"configured. For more information on configuration see the <<cha:ini-"
"configuration,INI Chapter>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:126
#, no-wrap
msgid "File Menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:132
msgid ""
"'Open...' - Opens a standard dialog box to open a G-code file to load in "
"AXIS. If you have configured LinuxCNC to use a filter program you can also "
"open it up. See the <<sub:ini:sec:filter,FILTER Section>> of the INI "
"configuration for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:133
msgid "'Recent Files' - Displays a list of recently opened files."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:136
msgid ""
"'Edit...' - Open the current G-code file for editing if you have an editor "
"configured in your INI file. See the <<sub:ini:sec:display,DISPLAY Section>> "
"for more information on specifying an editor to use."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:140
msgid ""
"'Reload' - Reload the current G-code file. If you edited it you must reload "
"it for the changes to take affect. If you stop a file and want to start from "
"the beginning then reload the file. The toolbar reload is the same as the "
"menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:141
msgid "'Save G-code as...' - Save the current file with a new name."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:144
msgid ""
"'Properties' - The sum of the rapid and feed moves. Does not factor in "
"acceleration, blending or path mode so time reported will never be less than "
"the actual run time."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:146
msgid ""
"'Edit tool table...' - Same as Edit if you have defined an editor you can "
"open the tool table and edit it."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:147
msgid "'Reload tool table' - After editing the tool table you must reload it."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:149
msgid ""
"'Ladder editor' - If you have loaded ClassicLadder you can edit it from "
"here. See the <<cha:classicladder,ClassicLadder chapter>> for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:150
msgid "'Quit' - Terminates the current LinuxCNC session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:152
#, no-wrap
msgid "Machine Menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:155
msgid "'Toggle Emergency Stop F1' - Change the state of the Emergency Stop."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:156
msgid ""
"'Toggle Machine Power F2' - Change the state of the Machine Power if the "
"Emergency Stop is not on."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:157
msgid "'Run Program' - Run the currently loaded program from the beginning."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:160
msgid ""
"'Run From Selected Line' - Select the line you want to start from first.  "
"Use with caution as this will move the tool to the expected position before "
"the line first then it will execute the rest of the code."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:163
msgid ""
"Do not use 'Run From Selected Line' if your G-code program contains "
"subroutines."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:165
msgid "'Step' - Single step through a program."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:166
msgid "'Pause' - Pause a program."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:167
msgid "'Resume' - Resume running from a pause."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:168
msgid ""
"'Stop' - Stop a running program. When run is selected after a stop the "
"program will start from the beginning."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:169
msgid ""
"'Stop at M1' - If an M1 is reached, and this is checked, program execution "
"will stop on the M1 line. Press Resume to continue."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:170
msgid ""
"'Skip lines with \"/\"' - If a line begins with '/' and this is checked, the "
"line will be skipped."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:171
msgid "'Clear MDI history' - Clears the MDI history window."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:172
msgid "'Copy from MDI history' - Copies the MDI history to the clipboard"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:173
msgid ""
"'Paste to MDI history' - Paste from the clipboard to the MDI history window"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:177
msgid ""
"'Calibration' - Starts the Calibration assistant (emccalib.tcl).  "
"Calibration reads the HAL file and for every 'setp' that uses a variable "
"from the INI file that is in an [AXIS_L],[JOINT_N],[SPINDLE_S], or [TUNE] "
"section it creates an entry that can be edited and tested."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:179
msgid ""
"'Show HAL Configuration' - Opens the HAL Configuration window where you can "
"monitor HAL Components, Pins, Parameters, Signals, Functions, and Threads."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:180
msgid ""
"'HAL Meter' - Opens a window where you can monitor a single HAL Pin, Signal, "
"or Parameter."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:181
msgid ""
"'HAL Scope' - Opens a virtual oscilloscope that allows plotting HAL values "
"vs. time."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:182
msgid "'Show LinuxCNC Status' - Opens a window showing LinuxCNC's status."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:183
msgid ""
"'Set Debug Level' - Opens a window where debug levels can be viewed and some "
"can be set."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:184
msgid "'Homing' - Home one or all axes."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:185
msgid "'Unhoming' - Unhome one or all axes."
msgstr ""

#. [[sub:axis:tool-touch-off]]
#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:186
msgid ""
"'Zero Coordinate System' - Set all offsets to zero in the coordinate system "
"chosen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:188 src/gui/axis.adoc:522 src/lathe/lathe-user.adoc:92
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool Touch Off"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:193
msgid ""
"'Tool touch off to workpiece' - When performing Touch Off, the value entered "
"is relative to the current workpiece ('G5x') coordinate system, as modified "
"by the axis offset ('G92').  When the Touch Off is complete, the Relative "
"coordinate for the chosen axis will become the value entered.  See "
"<<gcode:g10-l10,G10 L10>> in the G-code chapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:199
msgid ""
"'Tool touch off to fixture' - When performing Touch Off, the value entered "
"is relative to the ninth ('G59.3') coordinate system, with the axis offset "
"('G92') ignored.  This is useful when there is a tool touch-off fixture at a "
"fixed location on the machine, with the ninth ('G59.3') coordinate system "
"set such that the tip of a zero-length tool is at the fixture's origin when "
"the Relative coordinates are 0.  See <<gcode:g10-l11,G10 L11>> in the G-code "
"chapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "View Menu"
msgstr "ხედის მენიუ"

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:204
msgid ""
"'Top View' - The Top View (or Z view) displays the G-code looking along the "
"Z axis from positive to negative. This view is best for looking at X & Y."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:208
msgid ""
"'Rotated Top View' - The Rotated Top View (or rotated Z view) also displays "
"the G-code looking along the Z axis from positive to negative. But sometimes "
"it's convenient to display the X & Y axes rotated 90 degrees to fit the "
"display better. This view is also best for looking at X & Y."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:210
msgid ""
"'Side View' - The Side View (or X view) displays the G-code looking along "
"the X axis from positive to negative. This view is best for looking at Y & Z."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:212
msgid ""
"'Front View' - The Front View (or Y view) displays the G-code looking along "
"the Y axis from negative to positive. This view is best for looking at X & Z."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:219
msgid ""
"'Perspective View' - The Perspective View (or P view) displays the G-code "
"looking at the part from an adjustable point of view, defaulting to X+, Y-, "
"Z+. The position is adjustable using the mouse and the drag/rotate "
"selector.  This view is a compromise view, and while it does do a good job "
"of trying to show three (to nine!) axes on a two-dimensional display, there "
"will often be some feature that is hard to see, requiring a change in "
"viewpoint. This view is best when you would like to see all three (to nine) "
"axes at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:220
#, no-wrap
msgid "Point of View"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:227
msgid ""
"The AXIS display pick menu 'View' refers to 'Top', 'Front', and 'Side' "
"views.  These terms are correct if the CNC machine has its Z axis vertical, "
"with positive Z up. This is true for vertical mills, which is probably the "
"most popular application, and also true for almost all EDM machines, and "
"even vertical turret lathes, where the part is turning below the tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:233
msgid ""
"The terms 'Top', 'Front', and 'Side' might be confusing in other CNC "
"machines, such as a standard lathe, where the Z axis is horizontal, or a "
"horizontal mill, again where the Z axis is horizontal, or even an inverted "
"vertical turret lathe, where the part is turning above the tool, and the Z "
"axis positive direction is down!"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block *
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:236
msgid ""
"Just remember that positive Z axis is (almost) always away from the part.  "
"So be familiar with your machine's design and interpret the display as "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:239
msgid "'Display Inches' - Set the AXIS display scaling for inches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:240
msgid "'Display MM' - Set the AXIS display scaling for millimeters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:241
msgid ""
"'Show Program' - The preview display of the loaded G-code program can be "
"entirely disabled if desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:244
msgid ""
"'Show Program Rapids' - The preview display of the loaded G-code program "
"will always show the feed rate moves (G1,G2,G3) in white.  But the display "
"of rapid moves (G0) in cyan can be disabled if desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:246
msgid ""
"'Alpha-blend Program' - This option makes the preview of complex programs "
"easier to see, but may cause the preview to display more slowly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:247
msgid ""
"'Show Live Plot' - The highlighting of the feedrate paths (G1,G2,G3) as the "
"tool moves can be disabled if desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:248
msgid ""
"'Show Tool' - The display of the tool cone/cylinder can be disabled if "
"desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:249
msgid ""
"'Show Extents' - The display of the extents (maximum travel in each axis "
"direction) of the loaded G-code program can be disabled if desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:252
msgid ""
"'Show Offsets' - The selected fixture offset (G54-G59.3) origin location can "
"be shown as a set of three orthogonal lines, one each of red, blue, and "
"green.  This offset origin (or fixture zero) display can be disabled if "
"desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:257
msgid ""
"'Show Machine Limits' - The machine's maximum travel limits for each axis, "
"as set in the INI file, are shown as a rectangular box drawn in red dashed "
"lines. This is useful when loading a new G-code program, or when checking "
"for how much fixture offset would be needed to bring the G-code program "
"within the travel limits of your machine. It can be shut off if not needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:259
msgid ""
"'Show Velocity' - A display of velocity is sometimes useful to see how close "
"your machine is running to its design velocities. It can be disabled if "
"desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:263
msgid ""
"'Show Distance to Go' - Distance to go is a very handy item to know when "
"running an unknown G-code program for the first time. In combination with "
"the rapid override and feedrate override controls, unwanted tool and machine "
"damage can be avoided.  Once the G-code program has been debugged and is "
"running smoothly, the Distance to Go display can be disabled if desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:265
msgid ""
"'Coordinates in large font...' - The coordinates of the axes and the speed "
"in advance, will display in large font in the toolpath view."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:268
msgid ""
"'Clear Live Plot' - As the tool travels in the AXIS display, the G-code path "
"is highlighted.  To repeat the program, or to better see an area of "
"interest, the previously highlighted paths can be cleared."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:270
msgid ""
"'Show Commanded Position' - This is the position that LinuxCNC will try to "
"go to. Once motion has stopped, this is the position LinuxCNC will try to "
"hold."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:274
msgid ""
"'Show Actual Position' - Actual Position is the measured position as read "
"back from the system's encoders or simulated by step generators. This may "
"differ slightly from the Commanded Position for many reasons including PID "
"tuning, physical constraints, or position quantization."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:275
msgid ""
"'Show Machine Position' - This is the position in unoffset coordinates, as "
"established by Homing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:276
msgid ""
"'Show Relative Position' - This is the Machine Position modified by 'G5x', "
"'G92', and 'G43' offsets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:277
#, no-wrap
msgid "Help Menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:280
msgid "'About AXIS' - We all know what this is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:281
msgid "'Quick Reference' - Shows the keyboard shortcut keys."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:282
#, no-wrap
msgid "Toolbar buttons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:285
msgid ""
"From left to right in the AXIS display, the toolbar buttons (keyboard "
"shortcuts shown [in brackets]) are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:287
msgid ""
"image:images/tool_estop.png[\"Toggle Emergency Stop\"] Toggle Emergency Stop "
"[F1] (also called E-Stop)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:288
msgid ""
"image:images/tool_power.png[\"Toggle Machine Power\"] Toggle Machine Power "
"[F2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:289
msgid "image:images/tool_open.png[\"Open G Code file\"] Open G Code file [O]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:290
msgid ""
"image:images/tool_reload.png[\"Reload current file\"] Reload current file "
"[Ctrl-R]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:291
msgid ""
"image:images/tool_run.png[\"Begin executing the current file\"] Begin "
"executing the current file [R]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:292
msgid "image:images/tool_step.png[\"Execute next line\"] Execute next line [T]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:293
msgid ""
"image:images/tool_pause.png[\"Pause Execution - Resume Execution\"] Pause "
"Execution [P] Resume Execution [S]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:294
msgid ""
"image:images/tool_stop.png[\"Stop Program Execution\"] Stop Program "
"Execution [ESC]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:295
msgid ""
"image:images/tool_blockdelete.png[\"Toggle Skip lines\"] Toggle Skip lines "
"with \"/\" [Alt-M-/]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:296
msgid ""
"image:images/tool_optpause.png[\"Toggle Optional Pause\"] Toggle Optional "
"Pause [Alt-M-1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:297
msgid "image:images/tool_zoomin.png[\"Zoom In\"] Zoom In"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:298
msgid "image:images/tool_zoomout.png[\"Zoom Out\"] Zoom Out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:299
msgid "image:images/tool_axis_z.png[\"Top view\"] Top view"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:300
msgid "image:images/tool_axis_z2.png[\"Rotated Top view\"] Rotated Top view"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:301
msgid "image:images/tool_axis_x.png[\"Side view\"] Side view"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:302
msgid "image:images/tool_axis_y.png[\"Front view\"] Front view"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:303
msgid "image:images/tool_axis_p.png[\"Perspective view\"] Perspective view"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:304
msgid ""
"image:images/tool_rotate.png[\"Toggle between Drag and Rotate Mode\"] Toggle "
"between Drag and Rotate Mode [D]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:305
msgid ""
"image:images/tool_clear.png[\"Clear live backplot\"] Clear live backplot "
"[Ctrl-K]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:306
#, no-wrap
msgid "Graphical Display Area"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:308
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coordinate Display"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:312
msgid ""
"In the upper-left corner of the program display is the coordinate position "
"display for each axis. To the right of the number an origin symbol "
"image:images/axis-homed.png[\"origin symbol is shown if the axis has been "
"homed\"] is shown if the axis has been homed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:315
msgid ""
"A limit symbol image:images/axis-limit.png[\"limit symbol\"] is shown on the "
"right side of the coordinate position number if the axis is on one of its "
"limit switches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:323
msgid ""
"To properly interpret the coordinate position numbers, refer to the "
"'Position:' indicator in the status bar. If the position is 'Machine "
"Actual', then the displayed number is in the machine coordinate system. If "
"it is 'Relative Actual', then the displayed number is in the offset "
"coordinate system. When the coordinates displayed are relative and an offset "
"has been set, the display will include a cyan <<sec:machine-coordinate-"
"system,'machine origin'>> image:images/axis-machineorigin.png[\"cyan machine "
"origin\"] marker."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:331
msgid ""
"If the position is 'Commanded', then the exact coordinate given in a G-code "
"command is displayed. If it is 'Actual', then it is the position the machine "
"has actually moved to. These values can be different from commanded position "
"due to following error, dead band, encoder resolution, or step size. For "
"instance, if you command a movement to X 0.0033 on your mill, but one step "
"of your stepper motor or one encoder count is 0.00125, then the 'Commanded' "
"position might be 0.0033, but the 'Actual' position will be 0.0025 (2 steps) "
"or 0.00375 (3 steps)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:332
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preview Plot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:341
msgid ""
"When a file is loaded, a preview of it is shown in the display area.  Fast "
"moves (such as those produced by the 'G0' command) are shown as cyan lines. "
"Moves at a feed rate (such as those produced by the 'G1' command) are shown "
"as solid white lines. Dwells (such as those produced by the 'G4' command)  "
"are shown as small pink 'X' marks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:348
msgid ""
"G0 (Rapid) moves prior to a feed move will not show on the preview plot.  "
"Rapid moves after a T<n> (Tool Change) will not show on the preview until "
"after the first feed move.  To turn either of these features off program a "
"G1 without any moves prior to the G0 moves."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:349
#, no-wrap
msgid "Program Extents"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:353
msgid ""
"The 'extents' of the program in each axis are shown.  At the ends, the least "
"and greatest coordinate values are indicated.  In the middle, the difference "
"between the coordinates is shown."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:363
msgid ""
"When some coordinates exceed the 'soft limits' in the INI file, the relevant "
"dimension is shown in a different color and enclosed by a box.  In figure "
"below the maximum soft limit is exceeded on the X axis as indicated by the "
"box surrounding the coordinate value.  The minimum X travel of the program "
"is -1.95, the maximum X travel is 1.88, and the program requires 3.83 inches "
"of X travel.  To move the program so it's within the machine's travel in "
"this case, jog to the left and Touch Off X again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:365
#, no-wrap
msgid "Soft Limits(((Soft Limits)))"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:366 src/motion/external-offsets.adoc:111
#, no-wrap
msgid "Soft Limits"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:366
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/axis-outofrange.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:368
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool Cone"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:372
msgid ""
"When no tool is loaded, the location of the tip of the tool is indicated by "
"the 'tool cone'.  The 'tool cone' does not provide guidance on the form, "
"length, or radius of the tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:376
msgid ""
"When a tool is loaded (for instance, with the MDI command 'T1 M6' ), the "
"cone changes to a cylinder which shows the diameter of the tool given in the "
"tool table file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:377 src/gui/tklinuxcnc.adoc:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backplot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:383
msgid ""
"When the machine moves, it leaves a trail called the backplot.  The color of "
"the line indicates the type of motion: Yellow for jogs, faint green for "
"rapid movements, red for straight moves at a feed rate, and magenta for "
"circular moves at a feed rate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:384
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grid"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:391
msgid ""
"AXIS can optionally display a grid when in orthogonal views.  Enable or "
"disable the grid using the 'Grid' menu under 'View'.  When enabled, the grid "
"is shown in the top and rotated top views; when coordinate system is not "
"rotated, the grid is shown in the front and side views as well.  The presets "
"in the 'Grid' menu are controlled by the INI file item `[DISPLAY]GRIDS`.  If "
"unspecified, the default is `10mm 20mm 50mm 100mm 1in 2in 5in 10in`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:393
msgid "Specifying a very small grid may decrease performance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:394
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interacting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:397
msgid ""
"By left-clicking on a portion of the preview plot, the line will be "
"highlighted in both the graphical and text displays.  By left-clicking on an "
"empty area, the highlighting will be removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:400
msgid ""
"By dragging with the left mouse button pressed, the preview plot will be "
"shifted (panned)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:408
msgid ""
"By dragging with shift and the left mouse button pressed, or by dragging "
"with the mouse wheel pressed, the preview plot will be rotated.  When a line "
"is highlighted, the center of rotation is the center of the line.  "
"Otherwise, the center of rotation is the center of the entire program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:412
msgid ""
"By rotating the mouse wheel, or by dragging with the right mouse button "
"pressed, or by dragging with control and the left mouse button pressed, the "
"preview plot will be zoomed in or out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:415
msgid ""
"By clicking one of the 'Preset View' icons, or by pressing 'V', several "
"preset views may be selected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:416
#, no-wrap
msgid "Text Display Area"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:420
msgid ""
"By left-clicking a line of the program, the line will be highlighted in both "
"the graphical and text displays."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:424
msgid ""
"When the program is running, the line currently being executed is "
"highlighted in red. If no line has been selected by the user, the text "
"display will automatically scroll to show the current line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:425 src/gui/axis.adoc:426
#, no-wrap
msgid "Current and Selected Lines"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:426
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/axis-currentandselected.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:428 src/gui/tklinuxcnc.adoc:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manual Control"
msgstr "ხელით კონტროლი"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:433
msgid ""
"While the machine is turned on but not running a program, the items in the "
"'Manual Control' tab can be used to move the machine or control its spindle "
"and coolant."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:436
msgid ""
"When the machine is not turned on, or when a program is running, the manual "
"controls are unavailable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:444
msgid ""
"Many of the items described below are not useful on all machines.  When AXIS "
"detects that a particular pin is not connected in HAL, the corresponding "
"item in the Manual Control tab is removed.  For instance, if the HAL pin "
"'spindle.0.brake' is not connected, then the 'Brake' button will not appear "
"on the screen.  If the environment variable 'AXIS_NO_AUTOCONFIGURE' is set, "
"this behavior is disabled and all the items will appear."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:445
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Axis group"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:455
msgid ""
"'AXIS' allows you to manually move the machine.  This action is known as "
"'jogging'.  First, select the axis to be moved by clicking it.  Then, click "
"and hold the '+' or '-' button depending on the desired direction of "
"motion.  The first four axes can also be moved by the arrow keys (X and Y), "
"PAGE UP and PAGE DOWN keys (Z), and the [ and ] keys (A)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:462
msgid ""
"If 'Continuous' is selected, the motion will continue as long as the button "
"or key is pressed.  If another value is selected, the machine will move "
"exactly the displayed distance each time the button is clicked or the key is "
"pressed.  By default, the available values are '0.1000, 0.0100, 0.0010, "
"0.0001'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:465
msgid ""
"See the <<sub:ini:sec:display,DISPLAY Section>> for more information on "
"setting the increments."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:466
#, no-wrap
msgid "Homing (Identity Kinematics)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:472
msgid ""
"The INI file setting [KINS]JOINTS defines the total number of joints for the "
"system.  A joint may be configured with a home switch or for 'immediate' "
"homing.  Joints may specify a home sequence that organizes the order for "
"homing groups of joints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:479
msgid ""
"If *all* joints are configured for homing and have valid home sequences, the "
"homing button will show 'Home All'. Pressing the 'Home All' button (or the "
"Ctrl-HOME key) will initiate homing for all joints using their defined home "
"sequences. Pressing the HOME key will home the joint corresponding to the "
"currently selected axis even if no homing sequence is defined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:484
msgid ""
"If not all axes have valid home sequences, the homing button will show 'Home "
"Axis' and will home the joint for the currently selected axis only.  Each "
"axis must be selected and homed separately."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:488
msgid ""
"The dropdown menu Machine/Homing provides an alternate method to home axes. "
"The dropdown menu Machine/Unhoming provides means to unhome axes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:492
msgid ""
"If your machine does not have home switches defined in the configuration, "
"the 'Home' button will set the current position of the selected axis as the "
"absolute position 0 for that axis and will set the 'is-homed' bit for that "
"axis."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:494 src/gui/axis.adoc:503
msgid ""
"See the <<cha:homing-configuration,Homing Configuration Chapter>> for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:495
#, no-wrap
msgid "Homing (Non-Identity Kinematics)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:501
msgid ""
"Operation is similar to that for Identity Kinematics but, prior to homing, "
"the selection radio buttons select joints by number. The homing button will "
"show 'Home All' if all joints are configured for homing and have valid home "
"sequences.  Otherwise, the homing button will show 'Home Joint'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:511
msgid ""
"By pressing 'Touch Off' or the END key, the 'G5x offset' for the current "
"axis is changed so that the current axis value will be the specified value. "
"Expressions may be entered using the rules for rs274ngc programs, except "
"that variables may not be referred to. The resulting value is shown as a "
"number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:512 src/gui/axis.adoc:513
#, no-wrap
msgid "Touch Off Window"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:513
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/touchoff.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:516
msgid ""
"See also the Machine menu options: 'Touch part' and 'Touch part holder'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:517
#, no-wrap
msgid "Actual Position Touch Off"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:519
msgid ""
"An axis may be configured in the .INI file to incorporate the actual "
"position value for an axis into the touch off calculation, either adding or "
"subtracting this value.  This is primarily useful for machines which have a "
"non-motorized axis such as a quill with an encoder.  When this feature is "
"enabled for an axis, the title bar of the touch off window will indicate "
"*(system ACTUAL)*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:521
msgid "See <<axis:touchoff-actual>> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:526
msgid ""
"By pressing the 'Tool Touch Off' button the tool length and offsets of the "
"currently loaded tool will be changed so that the current tool tip position "
"matches the entered coordinate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:528 src/gui/axis.adoc:529
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool Touch Off Window"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:529
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/tooltouchoff.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:533
msgid ""
"See also the 'Tool touch off to workpiece' and 'Tool touch off to fixture' "
"options in the Machine menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:535 src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1177
#, no-wrap
msgid "Override Limits"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:543
msgid ""
"By pressing Override Limits, the machine will temporarily be allowed to jog "
"off of a physical limit switch. This check box is only available when a "
"limit switch is tripped.  The override is reset after one jog.  If the axis "
"is configured with separate positive and negative limit switches, LinuxCNC "
"will allow the jog only in the correct direction.  _Override Limits will not "
"allow a jog past a soft limit.  The only way to disable a soft limit on an "
"axis is to Unhome it._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:544 src/gui/tklinuxcnc.adoc:188
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Spindle group"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:554
msgid ""
"The buttons on the first row select the direction for the spindle to rotate: "
"Counterclockwise, Stopped, Clockwise. Counterclockwise will only show up if "
"the pin 'spindle.0.reverse' is in the HAL file (it can be 'net trick-axis "
"spindle.0.reverse' ). The buttons on the next row increase or decrease the "
"rotation speed. The checkbox on the third row allows the spindle brake to be "
"engaged or released. Depending on your machine configuration, not all the "
"items in this group may appear. Pressing the spindle start button sets the "
"'S' speed to 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:555 src/gui/tklinuxcnc.adoc:197
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Coolant group"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:558
msgid ""
"The two buttons allow the 'Mist' and 'Flood' coolants to be turned on and "
"off.  Depending on your machine configuration, not all the items in this "
"group may appear."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:564
msgid ""
"MDI allows G-code commands to be entered manually.  When the machine is not "
"turned on, or when a program is running, the MDI controls are unavailable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:565
#, no-wrap
msgid "The MDI tab"
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:566
#, no-wrap
msgid "MDI tab"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:566
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/axis-mdi.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:569
msgid ""
"'History' - This shows MDI commands that have been typed earlier in this "
"session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:571
msgid ""
"'MDI Command' - This allows you to enter a G-code command to be executed. "
"Execute the command by pressing Enter or by clicking 'Go'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:575
msgid ""
"'Active G-codes' - This shows the 'modal codes' that are active in the "
"interpreter. For instance, 'G54' indicates that the 'G54 offset' is applied "
"to all coordinates that are entered. When in Auto the Active G-codes "
"represent the codes after any read ahead by the interpreter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:576 src/gui/halui.adoc:114 src/gui/tklinuxcnc.adoc:226
#: src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc:378
#, no-wrap
msgid "Feed Override"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:581
msgid ""
"By moving this slider, the programmed feed rate can be modified. For "
"instance, if a program requests 'F60' and the slider is set to 120%, then "
"the resulting feed rate will be 72."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:588
msgid ""
"By moving this slider, the programmed spindle speed can be modified. For "
"instance, if a program requests S8000 and the slider is set to 80%, then the "
"resulting spindle speed will be 6400. This item only appears when the HAL "
"pin 'spindle.0.speed-out' is connected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:589 src/gui/tklinuxcnc.adoc:219
#, no-wrap
msgid "Jog Speed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:597
msgid ""
"By moving this slider, the speed of jogs can be modified. For instance, if "
"the slider is set to 1 in/min, then a .01 inch jog will complete in about .6 "
"seconds, or 1/100 of a minute. Near the left side (slow jogs) the values are "
"spaced closely together, while near the right side (fast jogs) they are "
"spaced much further apart, allowing a wide range of jog speeds with fine "
"control when it is most important."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:600
msgid ""
"On machines with a rotary axis, a second jog speed slider is shown.  This "
"slider sets the jog rate for the rotary axes (A, B and C)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:601 src/gui/halui.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "Max Velocity"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:606
msgid ""
"By moving this slider, the maximum velocity can be set. This caps the "
"maximum velocity for all programmed moves except spindle-synchronized moves."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:607 src/gui/tklinuxcnc.adoc:245
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keyboard Controls"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:613
msgid ""
"Almost all actions in AXIS can be accomplished with the keyboard. A full "
"list of keyboard shortcuts can be found in the AXIS Quick Reference, which "
"can be displayed by choosing Help > Quick Reference.  Many of the shortcuts "
"are unavailable when in MDI mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:614
#, no-wrap
msgid "Feed Override Keys"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:618
msgid ""
"For details on the Spanish keyboard layout please inspect the translated "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/axis.adoc:625
msgid ""
"The Feed Override keys behave differently when in Manual Mode.  The keys "
"'12345678 will select an axis if it is programmed. If you have 3 axis then ' "
"will select axis 0, 1 will select axis 1, and 2 will select axis 2. The "
"remainder of the number keys will still set the Feed Override. When running "
"a program '1234567890 will set the Feed Override to 0% - 100%."
msgstr ""

