#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:374
#, no-wrap
msgid "User Created Messages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:377
msgid ""
"GMOCCAPY has the ability to create HAL driven user messages.  To use them "
"you need to introduce some lines in the [DISPLAY] section of the INI file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:379
msgid "These three lines are needed to define a user pop up message dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:384
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"MESSAGE_TEXT    = The text to be displayed, may be pango markup formatted\n"
"MESSAGE_TYPE    = \"status\" , \"okdialog\" , \"yesnodialog\"\n"
"MESSAGE_PINNAME = is the name of the HAL pin group to be created\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:388
msgid ""
"The messages support pango markup language. Detailed information about the "
"markup language can be found at https://developer.gnome.org/pango/stable/"
"PangoMarkupFormat.html[Pango Markup]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:390
msgid "The following three dialog types are available:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:392
msgid ""
"*status* - Will just display a message as pop up window, using the messaging "
"system of GMOCCAPY."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:393
msgid ""
"*okdialog* - Will hold focus on the message dialog and will activate a `-"
"waiting` HAL pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:394
msgid ""
"*yesnodialog* - Will hold focus on the message dialog and will activate a `-"
"waiting` HAL pin and provide a `-response` HAL pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:396
msgid ""
"For more detailed information of the pins see <<gmoccapy:user-created-"
"message,User Created Message HAL Pins>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:397
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example of User Message Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:403
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"MESSAGE_TEXT = This is a <span background=\"#ff0000\" foreground=\"#ffffff\">info-message</span> test\n"
"MESSAGE_TYPE = status\n"
"MESSAGE_PINNAME = statustest\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:407
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"MESSAGE_TEXT = This is a yes no dialog test\n"
"MESSAGE_TYPE = yesnodialog\n"
"MESSAGE_PINNAME = yesnodialog\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:411
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"MESSAGE_TEXT = Text can be <small>small</small>, <big>big</big>, <b>bold</b <i>italic</i>, and even be <span color=\"red\">colored</span>.\n"
"MESSAGE_TYPE = okdialog\n"
"MESSAGE_PINNAME = okdialog\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:415
msgid "Currently the formatting doesn't work."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:421
msgid ""
"Magic comments can be used to control the G-code preview.  On very large "
"programs the preview can take a long time to load.  You can control what is "
"shown and what is hidden on the graphics screen by adding the appropriate "
"comments from this list into your G-code:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:426
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(PREVIEW,hide)\n"
"<G-code to be hidden>\n"
"(PREVIEW,show)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:428
#, no-wrap
msgid "User Command File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:433
msgid ""
"If a file `~/.gmoccapyrc` exists, its contents are executed as Python source "
"code just after the GUI is displayed. The details of what may be written in "
"the `~/.gmoccapyrc` are subject to change during the development cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:435
msgid ""
"A configuration-specific Python file may be specified with an INI file "
"setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:439
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"USER_COMMAND_FILE=filename.py\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:442
msgid ""
"If this file is specified, this file is sourced just after the GMOCCAPY GUI "
"is displayed *instead* of `~/.gmoccapyrc`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:446
msgid ""
"The following example changes the size of the vertical buttons: .Example "
"of .gmoccapyrc file"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:458
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"self.widgets.vbtb_main.set_size_request(85,-1)\n"
"BB_SIZE = (70, 70) # default = (90, 56)\n"
"self.widgets.tbtn_estop.set_size_request(*BB_SIZE)\n"
"self.widgets.tbtn_on.set_size_request(*BB_SIZE)\n"
"self.widgets.rbt_manual.set_size_request(*BB_SIZE)\n"
"self.widgets.rbt_mdi.set_size_request(*BB_SIZE)\n"
"self.widgets.rbt_auto.set_size_request(*BB_SIZE)\n"
"self.widgets.tbtn_setup.set_size_request(*BB_SIZE)\n"
"self.widgets.tbtn_user_tabs.set_size_request(*BB_SIZE)\n"
"self.widgets.btn_exit.set_size_request(*BB_SIZE)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:461
msgid ""
"The widget names can the looked up in the /usr/share/gmoccapy.glade file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:462
#, no-wrap
msgid "User CSS File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:466
msgid ""
"Similar to the User command file it's possible to influence the appearance "
"by cascading style sheets (CSS).  If a file `~/.gmoccapy_css` exists, its "
"contents are loaded into the stylesheet provider and are so being applied to "
"the GUI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:468
msgid ""
"A configuration-specific CSS file may be specified with an INI file setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:472
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"USER_CSS_FILE=filename.css\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:474
msgid ""
"If this file is specified, this file is used *instead* of `~/.gmoccapy_css`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:476
msgid ""
"Information what can be controlled by CSS can be found here: link:https://"
"docs.gtk.org/gtk3/css-overview.html[Overview of CSS in GTK]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:479
msgid ""
"Here an example how the color of checked buttons can be set to "
"yellow: .Example Yellow color for checked buttons"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:484
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"button:checked {\n"
"    background: rgba(250,230,0,0.8);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:490
msgid ""
"GMOCCAPY supports specifying the level of information (log level) that will "
"be printed to the console and to the log file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:493
msgid ""
"The order is _VERBOSE_, _DEBUG_, _INFO_, _WARNING_, _ERROR_, _CRITICAL_.  "
"Default is _WARNING_, that means _WARNING_, _ERROR_ and _CRITICAL_ are "
"printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:495
msgid "You can specify the log level in the INI file like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:499
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"DISPLAY = gmoccapy <log_level_param>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:501
msgid "using these parameters:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:507
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Log level   <log_level_param>\n"
"DEBUG       -d\n"
"INFO        -i\n"
"VERBOSE     -v\n"
"ERROR       -q\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:509
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: Configure logging to print only errors"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:514
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"DISPLAY = gmoccapy -q\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:517
msgid "You can specify where to save the log file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:521
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"LOG_FILE = gmoccapy.log\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:523
msgid ""
"If `LOG_FILE` is not set, logging happens to `$HOME/<base_log_name>.log`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:529
msgid ""
"GMOCCAPY exports several HAL pins to be able to react to hardware devices.  "
"The goal is to get a GUI that may be operated in a tool shop, completely/"
"mostly without mouse or keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:534
msgid ""
"You will have to do all connections to GMOCCAPY pins in your postgui.hal "
"file.  When GMOCCAPY is started, it creates the HAL pins for the GUI then it "
"executes the post-GUI HAL file named in the INI file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:538
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[HAL]\n"
"POSTGUI_HALFILE=<filename>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:543
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Typically `<filename>` would be the configs base name + `_postgui.hal`, e.g. `lathe_postgui.hal`, but can be any legal filename.\n"
"These commands are executed after the screen is built, guaranteeing the widget's HAL pins are available.\n"
"You can have multiple line of `POSTGUI_HALFILE=<filename>` in the INI file. Each will be run one after the other in the order they appear."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:545
#, no-wrap
msgid "Right and Bottom Button Lists"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:550
