"The screen has two main button lists, one on the right side an one on the "
"bottom.  The right handed buttons will not change during operation, but the "
"bottom button list will change very often.  The buttons are count from up to "
"down and from left to right beginning with 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:553
msgid "The pin names have changed in GMOCCAPY 2 to order them in a better way."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:555
msgid "The pins for the right (vertical) buttons are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:557
msgid "*gmoccapy.v-button.button-0* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:558
msgid "*gmoccapy.v-button.button-1* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:559
msgid "*gmoccapy.v-button.button-2* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:560
msgid "*gmoccapy.v-button.button-3* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:561
msgid "*gmoccapy.v-button.button-4* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:562
msgid "*gmoccapy.v-button.button-5* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:563
msgid "*gmoccapy.v-button.button-6* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:565
msgid "For the bottom (horizontal) buttons they are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:567
msgid "*gmoccapy.h-button.button-0* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:568
msgid "*gmoccapy.h-button.button-1* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:569
msgid "*gmoccapy.h-button.button-2* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:570
msgid "*gmoccapy.h-button.button-3* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:571
msgid "*gmoccapy.h-button.button-4* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:572
msgid "*gmoccapy.h-button.button-5* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:573
msgid "*gmoccapy.h-button.button-6* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:574
msgid "*gmoccapy.h-button.button-7* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:575
msgid "*gmoccapy.h-button.button-8* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:576
msgid "*gmoccapy.h-button.button-9* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:580
msgid ""
"As the buttons in the bottom list will change according to the mode and "
"other influences, the hardware buttons will activate the displayed "
"functions.  So you don't have to take care about switching functions around "
"in HAL, because that is done completely by GMOCCAPY!"
