#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:745
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.axis.jog-y-plus* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:746
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.axis.jog-y-minus* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:747
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.axis.jog-z-plus* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:748
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.axis.jog-z-minus* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:750
msgid "If you use a 4 axes configuration, there will be two additional pins:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:752
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.jog-<your fourth axis letter >-plus* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:753
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.jog-<your fourth axis letter >-minus* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:755
msgid "For a C-axis you will see:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:757
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.axis.jog-c-plus* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:758
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.axis.jog-c-minus* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:760
#, no-wrap
msgid "Jog Velocities and Turtle-Jog HAL Pin"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:768
msgid ""
"The jog velocity can be selected with the corresponding slider.  The scale "
"of the slider will be modified if the turtle button (the one showing a "
"rabbit or a turtle) has been toggled.  If the button is not visible, it "
"might have been disabled on the <<gmoccapy:turtle-jog,settings page>>.  If "
"the button shows the rabbit-icon, the scale is from min to max machine "
"velocity.  If it shows the turtle, the scale will reach only 1/20 of max "
"velocity by default.  The used divider can be set on the <<gmoccapy:turtle-"
"jog,settings page>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:770
msgid "So using a touch screen it is much easier to select smaller velocities."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:772
msgid ""
"GMOCCAPY offers this HAL pin to toggle between turtle and rabbit jogging:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:774
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.turtle-jog* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:775
#, no-wrap
msgid "Jog Increment HAL Pins"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:778
msgid "The jog increments given in the INI file like"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:782
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"INCREMENTS = 5mm 1mm .5mm .1mm .05mm .01mm\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:786
msgid ""
"are selectable through HAL pins, so a selection hardware switch can be used "
"to select the increment to use.  There will be a maximum of 10 HAL pins for "
"the increments given in the INI file.  If you give more increments in your "
"INI file, they will be not reachable from the GUI as they will not be "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:788
msgid ""
"If you have 6 increments in your INI file like in the example above, you "
"will get *7* pins:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:790
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.jog.jog-inc-0* _(bit IN)_ - This one is fixed and will represent "
"continuous jogging."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:791
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.jog.jog-inc-1* _(bit IN)_ - First increment given in the INI file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:792
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.jog-inc-2* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:793
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.jog-inc-3* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:794
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.jog-inc-4* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:795
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.jog-inc-5* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:796
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.jog-inc-6* _(bit IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:798
msgid "GMOCCAPY offers also a HAL pin to output the selected jog increment:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:800
msgid "*gmoccapy.jog.jog-increment* _(float OUT)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:802
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardware Unlock Pin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:806
msgid ""
"To be able to use a key switch to unlock the settings page, the following "
"pin is exported:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:809
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.unlock-settings* _(bit IN)_ - The settings page is unlocked if the "
"pin is high.  To use this pin, you need to activate it on the settings page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:810
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error/Warning Pins"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:813
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.error* _(bit OUT)_ - Indicates an error, so a light can lit or "
"even the machine may be stopped. It will be reset with the pin "
"`gmoccapy.delete-message`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:814
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.delete-message* _(bit IN)_ - Will delete the first error and reset "
"the `gmoccapy.error` pin to false after the last error has been cleared."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:815
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.warning-confirm* _(bit IN)_ - Confirms warning dialog like click "
"on OK"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:820
msgid ""
"Messages or user infos will not affect the `gmoccapy.error` pin, but the "
"`gmoccapy.delete-message` pin will delete the last message if no error is "
"shown!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:823
#, no-wrap
msgid "User Created Message HAL Pins"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:826
msgid ""
"GMOCCAPY may be configured to react to external errors, using 3 different "
"user messages:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:827
#, no-wrap
msgid "status"
msgstr "სტატუსი"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:830
msgid "*gmoccapy.messages.status* _(bit IN)_ - Triggers the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:831
#, no-wrap
msgid "okdialog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:834
msgid "*gmoccapy.messages.okdialog* _(bit IN)_ - Triggers the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:835
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.messages.okdialog-waiting* _(bit OUT)_ - Will be '1' as long as "
"the dialog is open. Closing the message will reset the this pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:836
#, no-wrap
msgid "yesnodialog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:839
msgid "*gmoccapy.messages.yesnodialog* _(bit IN)_ - Triggers the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:840
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.messages.yesnodialog-waiting* _(bit OUT)_ - Will be '1' as long as "
"the dialog is open. Closing the message will reset the this pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:842
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.messages.yesnodialog-response* _(bit OUT)_ - This pin will change "
"to '1' if the user clicks OK and in all other cases it will be '0'.  This "
"pin will remain '1' until the dialog is called again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:845
msgid ""
"To add a user created message you need to add the message to the INI file in "
"the DISPLAY section.  See <<sub:gmocccapy-configuration-user-"
"messages,Configuration of User Created Messages>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:846
#, no-wrap
msgid "User Message Example (INI file)"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:852
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"MESSAGE_TEXT = LUBE FAULT\n"
"MESSAGE_TYPE = okdialog\n"
"MESSAGE_PINNAME = lube-fault\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:856
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"MESSAGE_TEXT = X SHEAR PIN BROKEN\n"
"MESSAGE_TYPE = status\n"
"MESSAGE_PINNAME = pin\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:860
msgid ""
"To connect these new pins you need to do this in the postgui HAL file.  Here "
"are some example connections which connect the message signals to some place "
"else in the HAL file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:861
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example Connection of User Messages (HAL file)"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:867
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"net gmoccapy-lube-fault gmoccapy.messages.lube-fault\n"
"net gmoccapy-lube-fault-waiting gmoccapy.messages.lube-fault-waiting\n"
"net gmoccapy-pin gmoccapy.messages.pin\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:871
msgid ""
"For more information about HAL files and the net command see the <<cha:basic-"
"hal-reference,HAL Basics>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:872
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spindle Feedback Pins"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:875
msgid "There are two pins for spindle feedback:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:877
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.spindle_feedback_bar* _(float IN)_ - Pin to show the spindle speed "
"on the spindle bar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:878
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.spindle_at_speed_led* _(bit IN)_ - Pin to lit the is-at-speed-led."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:880
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pins to Indicate Program Progress Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:883
msgid "There are three pins giving information about the program progress:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:885
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.program.length* _(s32 OUT)_ - Shows the total number of lines of "
"the program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:886
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.program.current-line* _(s32 OUT)_ - Indicates the current working "
"line of the program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:887
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.program.progress* _(float OUT)_ - Gives the program progress in "
"percentage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:890
msgid ""
"The values may not be very accurate if you are working with subroutines or "
"large remap procedures.  Also loops will cause different values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:891
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool Related Pins"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:893
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool Change Pins"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:897
msgid ""
"These pins are provided to use GMOCCAPY's internal tool change dialog, "
"similar to the one known from AXIS, but with several modifications.  So you "
"will not only get the message to change to 'tool number 3', but also the "
"description of that tool like '7.5 mm 3 flute cutter'.  The information is "
"taken from the tool table, so it is up to you what to display."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:898
#, no-wrap
msgid "GMOCCAPY tool change dialog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:899
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manual tool change"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:899
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/gmoccapy_manual_toolchange.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:902
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.toolchange-number* _(s32 IN)_ - The number of the tool to be "
"changed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:903
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.toolchange-change* _(bit IN)_ - Indicates that a tool has to be "
"changed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:904
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.toolchange-changed* _(bit OUT)_ - Indicates tool has been changed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:905
msgid "*gmoccapy.toolchange-confirm* _(bit IN)_ - Confirms tool change"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:907
msgid "Usually they are connected like this for a manual tool change:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:914
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"net tool-change gmoccapy.toolchange-change <= iocontrol.0.tool-change\n"
"net tool-changed gmoccapy.toolchange-changed <= iocontrol.0.tool-changed\n"
"net tool-prep-number gmoccapy.toolchange-number <= iocontrol.0.tool-prep-number\n"
"net tool-prep-loop iocontrol.0.tool-prepare <= iocontrol.0.tool-prepared\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:918
msgid ""
"Please take care, that this connections have to be done in the postgui HAL "
"file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:919
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool Offset Pins"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:922
msgid ""
"These pins allow you to show the active tool offset values for X and Z in "
"the tool information frame.  You should know that they are only active after "
"G43 has been sent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:923
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool information area"
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:924
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool information"
msgstr "ინფორმაცია ხელსაწყოზე"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:924
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/gmoccapy_tool_info.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:927
msgid "*gmoccapy.tooloffset-x* _(float IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:928
msgid "*gmoccapy.tooloffset-z* _(float IN)_"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:931
msgid ""
"The tooloffset-x line is not needed on a mill, and will not be displayed on "
"a mill with trivial kinematics."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:933
msgid ""
"To display the current offsets, the pins have to be connected like this in "
"the postgui HAL file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:938
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"net tooloffset-x gmoccapy.tooloffset-x <= motion.tooloffset.x\n"
"net tooloffset-z gmoccapy.tooloffset-z <= motion.tooloffset.z\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:943
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please note, that GMOCCAPY takes care of its own to update the offsets, sending an G43 after any tool change, *but not in auto mode!*\n"
"So writing a program makes you responsible to include an G43 after each tool change!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:945 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1042
#, no-wrap
msgid "Auto Tool Measurement"
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:949
msgid ""
"GMOCCAPY offers an integrated auto tool measurement.  To use this feature, "
"you will need to do some additional settings and you may want to use the "
"offered HAL pin to get values in your own NGC remap procedure."
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:953
msgid ""
"Before starting the first test, do not forget to enter the probe height and "
"probe velocities on the settings page! See <<gmoccapy:tool-"
"measurement,Settings Page Tool Measurement>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:956
msgid ""
"It might be also a good idea to take a look at the tool measurement video, "
"see <<gmoccapy:tool-measurement-videos,tool measurement related videos>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:959
msgid ""
"Tool Measurement in GMOCCAPY is done a little bit different to many other "
"GUIs.  You should follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:961 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1080
msgid "Touch off your workpiece in X and Y."
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:962
msgid ""
"Measure the height of your block from the base where your tool switch is "
"located, to the upper face of the block (including chuck etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:963
msgid "Push the button block height and enter the measured value."
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:964 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1083
msgid "Go to auto mode and start your program."
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:966
msgid "Here is a small sketch:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:967
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool measurement data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:968 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1085
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/sketch_auto_tool_measurement.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: IMPORTANT
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:972
msgid ""
"With the first given tool change the tool will be measured and the offset "
"will be set automatically to fit the block height.  The advantage of the "
"GMOCCAPY way is, that you do not need a reference tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:978
msgid ""
"Your program must contain a tool change at the beginning! The tool will be "
"measured, even it has been used before, so there is no danger, if the block "
"height has changed.  There are several videos showing the way to do that on "
"YouTube."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:981
#, no-wrap
msgid "Provided Pins"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:985
msgid ""
"GMOCCAPY offers five pins for tool measurement purposes.  These pins are "
"mostly used to be read from a G-code subroutine, so the code can react to "
"different values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:987
msgid "*gmoccapy.toolmeasurement* _(bit OUT)_ - Enable or not tool measurement"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:988
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.blockheight* _(float OUT)_ - The measured value of the top face of "
"the workpiece"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:989
msgid "*gmoccapy.probeheight* _(float OUT)_ - The probe switch height"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:990
msgid ""
"*gmoccapy.searchvel* _(float OUT)_ - The velocity to search for the tool "
"probe switch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:991
msgid "*gmoccapy.probevel* _(float OUT)_ - The velocity to probe tool length"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:992
#, no-wrap
msgid "INI File Modifications"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:995
msgid "Modify your INI file to include the following sections."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:996
#, no-wrap
msgid "The RS274NGC Section"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1002
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[RS274NGC]\n"
"# is the sub, with is called when a error during tool change happens, not needed on every machine configuration\n"
"ON_ABORT_COMMAND=O <on_abort> call\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1005
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# The remap code\n"
"REMAP=M6  modalgroup=6 prolog=change_prolog ngc=change epilog=change_epilog\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1008
msgid ""
"Make sure INI_VARS and HAL_PIN_VARS are not set to 0. They are set to 1 by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1009 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1257
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Tool Sensor Section"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1012
msgid ""
"The position of the tool sensor and the start position of the probing "
"movement, all values are absolute coordinates, except MAXPROBE, which must "
"be given in relative movement."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1020
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[TOOLSENSOR]\n"
"X = 10\n"
"Y = 10\n"
"Z = -20\n"
"MAXPROBE = -20\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1022 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1293
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Change Position Section"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1025
msgid ""
"This is not named TOOL_CHANGE_POSITION on purpose - *canon uses that name "
"and will interfere otherwise.* The position to move the machine before "
"giving the change tool command. All values are in absolute coordinates."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1032 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1306
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[CHANGE_POSITION]\n"
"X = 10\n"
"Y = 10\n"
"Z = -2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1034 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1308
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Python Section"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1036
msgid "The Python plug ins serves interpreter and task."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1044
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[PYTHON]\n"
"# The path to start a search for user modules\n"
"PATH_PREPEND = python\n"
"# The start point for all.\n"
"TOPLEVEL = python/toplevel.py\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1046
#, no-wrap
msgid "Needed Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1050
msgid ""
"First make a directory \"python\" in your config folder.  From "
"`<your_linuxcnc-dev_directory>/configs/sim/gmoccapy/python` copy the "
"following files into the just created `config_dir/python` folder:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1052
msgid "`toplevel.py`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1053
msgid "`remap.py`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1054
