#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1073
#, no-wrap
msgid "Needed HAL Connections"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1076
msgid "Connect the tool probe in your HAL file like so:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1080 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1330
#, no-wrap
msgid "net probe  motion.probe-input <= <your_input_pin>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1083
msgid "The line might look like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1088
#, no-wrap
msgid "net probe  motion.probe-input <= parport.0.pin-15-in\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1091
msgid "In your postgui.hal file add the following lines:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1099
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# The next lines are only needed if the pins had been connected before\n"
"unlinkp iocontrol.0.tool-change\n"
"unlinkp iocontrol.0.tool-changed\n"
"unlinkp iocontrol.0.tool-prep-number\n"
"unlinkp iocontrol.0.tool-prepared\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# link to GMOCCAPY toolchange, so you get the advantage of tool description on change dialog\n"
"net tool-change gmoccapy.toolchange-change <= iocontrol.0.tool-change\n"
"net tool-changed gmoccapy.toolchange-changed => iocontrol.0.tool-changed\n"
"net tool-prep-number gmoccapy.toolchange-number <= iocontrol.0.tool-prep-number\n"
"net tool-prep-loop iocontrol.0.tool-prepare <= iocontrol.0.tool-prepared\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1108
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Settings Page"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1112
msgid ""
"To enter the page you will have to click on image:images/"
"gmoccapy_settings_button.png[align=\"left\"] and give an unlock code, which "
"is *123* by default.  If you want to change it at this time you will have to "
"edit the hidden preference file, see <<gmoccapy:display-section,the display "
"section>> for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1114
msgid "The page is separated in three main tabs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1115
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appearance"
msgstr "გარეგნობა"

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1117
#, no-wrap
msgid "GMOCCAPY settings page Appearance"
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1118
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuration page"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1118
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/gmoccapy_settings_appearance.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1121
msgid "On this tab you will find the following options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1122
#, no-wrap
msgid "Main Window"
msgstr "მთავარი ფანჯარა"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1127
msgid ""
"Here you can select how you wish the GUI to start.  The main reason for this "
"was the wish to get an easy way for the user to set the starting options "
"without the need to touch code.  You have three options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1129
msgid "_Start as full screen_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1130
msgid "_Start maximized_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1133
msgid ""
"_Start as window_ - If you select start as window the spinboxes to set the "
"position and size will get active.  One time set, the GUI will start every "
"time on the place and with the size selected.  Nevertheless the user can "
"change the size and position using the mouse, but that will not have any "
"influence on the settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1134
msgid ""
"_hide title bar_ - Allows the title bar to be hidden. (default: title bar "
"visible)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1135
msgid ""
"_hide cursor_ - Does allow to hide the cursor, what is very useful if you "
"use a touch screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1136
msgid "_hide tooltips_ - Hides the tool tips."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1137 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:509
#: src/gui/qtvcp-libraries.adoc:1255
#, no-wrap
msgid "Virtual Keyboard"
msgstr "ვირტუალური კლავიატურა"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1142
msgid ""
"The checkboxes allow the user to select if he wants the on board keyboard to "
"be shown immediately when entering the MDI Mode, the offset page, the "
"tooledit widget or when open a program in the EDIT mode.  The keyboard "
"button on the bottom button list will not be affected by these settings, so "
"you are able to show or hide the keyboard by pressing the button."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1144
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Examples:"
msgid "The default setting is:"
msgstr "მაგალითები:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1146
msgid "_Show keyboard on offset_ = False"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1147
msgid "_Show keyboard on tooledit_ = False"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1148
msgid "_Show keyboard on MDI_ = True"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1149
msgid "_Show keyboard on EDIT_ = True"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1150
msgid "_Show keyboard on load file_ = False"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1153
msgid ""
"If this section is not sensitive, you have not installed a virtual keyboard, "
"supported ones are _onboard_ and _matchbox-keyboard_."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1158
msgid ""
"If the keyboard layout is not correct, i.e. clicking Y gives Z, than the "
"layout has not been set properly, related to your locale settings.  For "
"onboard it can be solved with a small batch file with the following content:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1162
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#!/bin/bash\n"
"setxkbmap -model pc105 -layout de -variant basic\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1166
msgid ""
"The letters \"de\" are for German, you will have to set them according to "
"your locale settings.  Just execute this file before starting LinuxCNC, it "
"can be done also adding a starter to your local folder."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1169
#, no-wrap
msgid "./config/autostart\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1172
msgid "So that the layout is set automatically on starting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1174
msgid ""
"For matchbox-keyboard you will have to make your own layout, for a German "
"layout ask in the forum."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1176
#, no-wrap
msgid "GMOCCAPY with Onboard keyboard in edit mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1178
msgid ""
"image:images/gmoccapy_keyboard_edit_mode_mid.png[\"Onboard "
"keyboard\",align=\"left\",link=\"images/gmoccapy_keyboard_edit_mode.png\"]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1179
#, no-wrap
msgid "On Touch Off"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1182
msgid ""
"This gives the option whether to show the preview tab or the offset page tab "
"when you enter the touch off mode by clicking the corresponding bottom "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1184
msgid "_show preview_"
