#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1284
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardware settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1284
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/gmoccapy_settings_hardware.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1286
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardware MPG Scale"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1294
msgid ""
"For the different HAL pins to connect MPG wheels to, you may select "
"individual scales to be applied.  The main reason for this was my own test "
"to solve this through HAL connections, resulting in a very complex HAL "
"file.  Imagine a user having an MPG Wheel with 100 ppr and he wants to slow "
"down the max. vel. from 14000 to 2000 mm/min, that needs 12000 pulses, "
"resulting in 120 turns of the wheel! Or an other user having a MPG Wheel "
"with 500 ipr and he wants to set the spindle override which has limits from "
"50 to 120 % so he goes from min to max within 70 pulses, meaning not even "
"1/4 turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1296
msgid "By default all scales are set using the calculation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1299
#, no-wrap
msgid "(MAX - MIN)/100\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1304
msgid ""
"_Starting RPM_ - Sets the rpm to be used if the spindle is started and no S "
"value has been set."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1308
msgid ""
"This value will be presetted according to your settings in `[DISPLAY] "
"DEFAULT_SPINDLE_SPEED` of your INI file.  If you change the settings on the "
"settings page, that value will be default from that moment, your INI file "
"will not be modified."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1310
msgid ""
"_Spindle bar min_ and _Spindle bar max_ - Sets the limits of the spindle bar "
"shown in the INFO frame on the main screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1315
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Default values are:\n"
"MIN = 0\n"
"MAX = 6000"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1320
msgid ""
"It is no error giving wrong values.  If you give a maximum of 2000 and your "
"spindle makes 4000 RPM, only the bar level will be wrong on higher speeds "
"than 2000 RPM."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1321
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlock options"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1324
msgid "There are three options to unlock the settings page:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1326
msgid "_Use unlock code_ - The user must give a code to get in."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1327
msgid "_Do not use unlock code_ - There will be no security check."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1328
msgid ""
"_Use HAL pin to unlock_ - Hardware pin must be high to unlock the settings, "
"see <<gmoccapy:hardware-unlock,hardware unlock pin>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1330
msgid "Default is _use unlock code_ (default code is *123*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1332
#, no-wrap
msgid "Turtle Jog"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1334
msgid "This settings will have influence on the jog velocities."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1339
msgid ""
"_Hide turtle jog button_ - Will hide the button right of the jog velocity "
"slider.  If you hide this button, please take care that the \"rabbit mode\" "
"is activated, otherwise you will not be able to jog faster than the turtle "
"jog velocity, which is calculated using the turtle jog factor."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1341
msgid ""
"_Turtle jog factor_ - Sets the scale to apply for turtle jog mode (button "
"pressed, showing the turtle).  If you set a factor of 20, the turtle max. "
"jog velocity will be 1/20 of the max. velocity of the machine."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1344
msgid ""
"This button can be controlled using the <<gmoccapy:jog-velocity,Turtle-Jog "
"HAL Pin>>."
msgstr ""

