msgid "_X Pos._ - The X position of the tool switch."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1369
msgid "_Y Pos._ - The Y position of the tool switch."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1370
msgid ""
"_Z Pos._ - The Z position of the tool switch, we will go as rapid move to "
"this coordinate."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1372
msgid ""
"_Max. Probe_ - The distance to search for contact, an error will be "
"launched, if no contact is given in this range.  The distance has to be "
"given in relative coordinates, beginning the move from Z Pos., so you have "
"to give a negative value to go down!"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1375
msgid ""
"_Probe Height_ - The height of your probe switch, you can measure it.  Just "
"touch off the base where the probe switch is located and set that to zero.  "
"Then make a tool change and watch the tool_offset_z value, that is the "
"height you must enter here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1376
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probe velocities"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1381
msgid ""
"_Search Vel._ - The velocity to search for the tool switch.  After contact "
"the tool will go up again and then goes towards the probe again with probe "
"vel, so you will get better results."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/gmoccapy.adoc:1384
msgid ""
"_Probe Vel._ - The velocity for the second movement to the switch.  It "
"should be slower to get better touch results.  In simulation mode, this is "
"commented out in macros/change.ngc, otherwise the user would have to click "
"twice on the probe button."
msgstr ""

