#. type: Title =
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "PyVCP Examples"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:16
msgid ""
"To create a PyVCP panel to use with the AXIS interface that is attached to "
"the right of AXIS you need to do the following basic things."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:18 src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:31
msgid ""
"Create an XML file that contains your panel description and put it in your "
"config directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Add the PyVCP entry to the [DISPLAY] section of the INI file with your XML "
"file name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:21
msgid ""
"Add the POSTGUI_HALFILE entry to the [HAL] section of the INI file with the "
"name of your postgui HAL file name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:23 src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:34
msgid ""
"Add the links to HAL pins for your panel in the postgui.hal file to "
"'connect' your PyVCP panel to LinuxCNC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "Floating Panels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:28
msgid ""
"To create floating PyVCP panels that can be used with any interface you need "
"to do the following basic things."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:32
msgid "Add a loadusr line to your HAL file to load each panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:37
msgid ""
"The following is an example of a loadusr command to load two PyVCP panels "
"and name each one so the connection names in HAL will be known."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"loadusr -Wn btnpanel pyvcp -c btnpanel panel1.xml\n"
"loadusr -Wn sppanel pyvcp -c sppanel panel2.xml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:45
msgid "The -Wn makes HAL 'Wait for name' to be loaded before proceeding."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:47
msgid "The pyvcp -c makes PyVCP name the panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:49
msgid "The HAL pins from panel1.xml will be named btnpanel.<_pin name_>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:51
msgid "The HAL pins from panel2.xml will be named sppanel.<_pin name_>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:53
msgid ""
"Make sure the loadusr line is before any nets that make use of the PyVCP "
"pins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "Jog Buttons Example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:62
msgid ""
"In this example we will create a PyVCP panel with jog buttons for X, Y, and "
"Z.  This configuration will be built upon a StepConf Wizard generated "
"configuration.  First we run the StepConf Wizard and configure our machine, "
"on the Advanced Configuration Options page we then make a couple of "
"selections to add a blank PyVCP panel as shown in the following figure.  For "
"this example we named the configuration 'pyvcp_xyz' on the Basic Machine "
"Information page of the StepConf Wizard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "XYZ Wizard Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "PyVCP XYZ Wizard Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/xyz_ACO.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:70
msgid ""
"The StepConf Wizard will create several files and place them in the "
"`linuxcnc/configs/pyvcp_xyz` directory. If you left the create link checked "
"you will have a link to those files on your desktop."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the Widgets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:76
msgid ""
"Open up the custompanel.xml file by right clicking on it and selecting 'open "
"with text editor'. Between the <pyvcp></pyvcp> tags we will add the widgets "
"for our panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:79
msgid ""
"Look in the PyVCP Widgets Reference section of the manual for more detailed "
"information on each widget <<sec:pyvcp:widgets,documentation des widgets>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:82
msgid ""
"In your custompanel.xml file we will add the description of the widgets."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<pyvcp>\n"
"  <labelframe text=\"Jog Buttons\">\n"
"    <font>(\"Helvetica\",16)</font>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      <!-- the X jog buttons -->\n"
"      <hbox>\n"
"      <relief>RAISED</relief>\n"
"      <bd>3</bd>\n"
"      <button>\n"
"        <font>(\"Helvetica\",20)</font>\n"
"        <width>3</width>\n"
"        <halpin>\"x-plus\"</halpin>\n"
"        <text>\"X+\"</text>\n"
"      </button>\n"
"      <button>\n"
"        <font>(\"Helvetica\",20)</font>\n"
"        <width>3</width>\n"
"        <halpin>\"x-minus\"</halpin>\n"
"        <text>\"X-\"</text>\n"
"      </button>\n"
"      </hbox>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      <!-- the Y jog buttons -->\n"
"      <hbox>\n"
"      <relief>RAISED</relief>\n"
"      <bd>3</bd>\n"
"      <button>\n"
"        <font>(\"Helvetica\",20)</font>\n"
"        <width>3</width>\n"
"        <halpin>\"y-plus\"</halpin>\n"
"        <text>\"Y+\"</text>\n"
"      </button>\n"
"      <button>\n"
"        <font>(\"Helvetica\",20)</font>\n"
"        <width>3</width>\n"
"        <halpin>\"y-minus\"</halpin>\n"
"        <text>\"Y-\"</text>\n"
"      </button>\n"
"      </hbox>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:141
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      <!-- the Z jog buttons -->\n"
"      <hbox>\n"
"      <relief>RAISED</relief>\n"
"      <bd>3</bd>\n"
"      <button>\n"
"        <font>(\"Helvetica\",20)</font>\n"
"        <width>3</width>\n"
"        <halpin>\"z-plus\"</halpin>\n"
"        <text>\"Z+\"</text>\n"
"      </button>\n"
"      <button>\n"
"        <font>(\"Helvetica\",20)</font>\n"
"        <width>3</width>\n"
"        <halpin>\"z-minus\"</halpin>\n"
"        <text>\"Z-\"</text>\n"
"      </button>\n"
"      </hbox>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:161
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      <!-- the jog speed slider -->\n"
"      <vbox>\n"
"      <relief>RAISED</relief>\n"
"      <bd>3</bd>\n"
"      <label>\n"
"        <text>\"Jog Speed\"</text>\n"
"        <font>(\"Helvetica\",16)</font>\n"
"      </label>\n"
"      <scale>\n"
"        <font>(\"Helvetica\",14)</font>\n"
"        <halpin>\"jog-speed\"</halpin>\n"
"        <resolution>1</resolution>\n"
"        <orient>HORIZONTAL</orient>\n"
"        <min_>0</min_>\n"
"        <max_>80</max_>\n"
"      </scale>\n"
"      </vbox>\n"
"  </labelframe>\n"
"</pyvcp>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:169
msgid ""
"After adding the above you now will have a PyVCP panel that looks like the "
"following attached to the right side of AXIS. It looks nice but it does not "
"do anything until you 'connect' the buttons to halui. If you get an error "
"when you try and run scroll down to the bottom of the pop up window and "
"usually the error is a spelling or syntax error and it will be there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "Jog Buttons Image"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/xyz_buttons.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "Make Connections"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:176
msgid ""
"To make the connections needed open up your custom_postgui.hal file and add "
"the following."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:182
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the X PyVCP buttons\n"
"net my-jogxminus halui.axis.x.minus <= pyvcp.x-minus\n"
"net my-jogxplus halui.axis.x.plus <= pyvcp.x-plus\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:186
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the Y PyVCP buttons\n"
"net my-jogyminus halui.axis.y.minus <= pyvcp.y-minus\n"
"net my-jogyplus halui.axis.y.plus <= pyvcp.y-plus\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:190
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the Z PyVCP buttons\n"
"net my-jogzminus halui.axis.z.minus <= pyvcp.z-minus\n"
"net my-jogzplus halui.axis.z.plus <= pyvcp.z-plus\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:193
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the PyVCP jog speed slider\n"
"net my-jogspeed halui.axis.jog-speed <= pyvcp.jog-speed-f\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:199
msgid ""
"After resetting the E-Stop and putting it into jog mode and moving the jog "
"speed slider in the PyVCP panel to a value greater than zero the PyVCP jog "
"buttons should work. You can not jog when running a G-code file or while "
"paused or while the MDI tab is selected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "Port Tester"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:204
msgid ""
"This example shows you how to make a simple parallel port tester using PyVCP "
"and HAL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:207
msgid ""
"First create the ptest.xml file with the following code to create the panel "
"description."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:268
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<!-- Test panel for the parallel port cfg for out -->\n"
"<pyvcp>\n"
"  <hbox>\n"
"    <relief>RIDGE</relief>\n"
"    <bd>2</bd>\n"
"    <button>\n"
"      <halpin>\"btn01\"</halpin>\n"
"      <text>\"Pin 01\"</text>\n"
"    </button>\n"
"    <led>\n"
"      <halpin>\"led-01\"</halpin>\n"
"      <size>25</size>\n"
"      <on_color>\"green\"</on_color>\n"
"      <off_color>\"red\"</off_color>\n"
"    </led>\n"
"  </hbox>\n"
"  <hbox>\n"
"    <relief>RIDGE</relief>\n"
"    <bd>2</bd>\n"
"    <button>\n"
"      <halpin>\"btn02\"</halpin>\n"
"      <text>\"Pin 02\"</text>\n"
"    </button>\n"
"    <led>\n"
"      <halpin>\"led-02\"</halpin>\n"
"      <size>25</size>\n"
"      <on_color>\"green\"</on_color>\n"
"      <off_color>\"red\"</off_color>\n"
"    </led>\n"
"  </hbox>\n"
"  <hbox>\n"
"    <relief>RIDGE</relief>\n"
"    <bd>2</bd>\n"
"    <label>\n"
"      <text>\"Pin 10\"</text>\n"
"      <font>(\"Helvetica\",14)</font>\n"
"    </label>\n"
"    <led>\n"
"      <halpin>\"led-10\"</halpin>\n"
"      <size>25</size>\n"
"      <on_color>\"green\"</on_color>\n"
"      <off_color>\"red\"</off_color>\n"
"    </led>\n"
"  </hbox>\n"
"  <hbox>\n"
"    <relief>RIDGE</relief>\n"
"    <bd>2</bd>\n"
"    <label>\n"
"      <text>\"Pin 11\"</text>\n"
"      <font>(\"Helvetica\",14)</font>\n"
"    </label>\n"
"    <led>\n"
"      <halpin>\"led-11\"</halpin>\n"
"      <size>25</size>\n"
"      <on_color>\"green\"</on_color>\n"
"      <off_color>\"red\"</off_color>\n"
"    </led>\n"
"  </hbox>\n"
"</pyvcp>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:272
msgid ""
"This will create the following floating panel which contains a couple of in "
"pins and a couple of out pins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:273
#, no-wrap
msgid "Port Tester Panel"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:273
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/ptest.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:277
msgid ""
"To run the HAL commands that we need to get everything up and running we put "
"the following in our ptest.hal file."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:290
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"loadrt hal_parport cfg=\"0x378 out\"\n"
"loadusr -Wn ptest pyvcp -c ptest ptest.xml\n"
"loadrt threads name1=porttest period1=1000000\n"
"addf parport.0.read porttest\n"
"addf parport.0.write porttest\n"
"net pin01 ptest.btn01 parport.0.pin-01-out ptest.led-01\n"
"net pin02 ptest.btn02 parport.0.pin-02-out ptest.led-02\n"
"net pin10 parport.0.pin-10-in ptest.led-10\n"
"net pin11 parport.0.pin-11-in ptest.led-11\n"
"start\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:293
msgid ""
"To run the HAL file we use the following command from a terminal window."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/pyvcp-examples.adoc:296
#, no-wrap
msgid "~$ halrun -I -f ptest.hal\n"
msgstr ""

