#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:64
msgid ""
"If your configuration is not currently set up to use QtDragon, you can "
"change it by editing the INI file sections.  For an exhaustive list of "
"options, see the <<sub:ini:sec:display,display section>> of the INI file "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:68
msgid ""
"You can only have one of each section (e.g., [HAL]) in the INI file.  If you "
"see in these docs multiple section options, place them all under the one "
"appropriate section name."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:72
msgid "In the section `[DISPLAY]` change the `DISPLAY =` assignment to read:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:74
msgid "`qtdragon` for a small version"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:75
msgid "`qtdradon_hd` for the large version."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:77
msgid ""
"You can add `-v`, `-d`, `-i`, or `-q` for (respectably) verbose, debug, info "
"or quiet output to the terminal."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:82
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"DISPLAY = qtvcp qtdragon\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:84 src/gui/touchy.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preferences"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To keep track of preferences, QtDragon looks for a preference text file. Add the following entry under the `[DISPLAY]` heading.\n"
"It can use `~` for home directory or `WORKINGFOLDER` or `CONFIGFOLDER` to represent QtVCP's idea of those directories:\n"
"This example will save the file in the config folder of the launch screen. (Other options are possible see the QtVCP's screenoption widget docs.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"PREFERENCE_FILE_PATH = WORKINGFOLDER/qtdragon.pref\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can specify where to save history/logs.\n"
"These file names can be user selected.\n"
"In the section `[DISPLAY]` add:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:110
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"MDI_HISTORY_FILE = mdi_history.dat\n"
"MACHINE_LOG_PATH = machine_log.dat\n"
"LOG_FILE = qtdragon.log\n"
msgstr ""

