#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:185
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optional popup custom message dialogs, controlled by HAL pins.\n"
"MESSAGE_TYPE can be 'okdialog' or 'yesnodialog'. See `qtvcp/library/messages` for more information.\n"
"This example shows how to make a dialog that requires the user to select 'ok' to acknowledge and hide.\n"
"These dialogs could be used for such things as low lube oil warnings, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:194
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"MESSAGE_BOLDTEXT = This is the short text\n"
"MESSAGE_TEXT = This is the longer text of the both type test. It can be longer than the status bar text\n"
"MESSAGE_DETAILS = BOTH DETAILS\n"
"MESSAGE_TYPE = okdialog\n"
"MESSAGE_PINNAME = oktest\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:197
msgid "Multimessages use an s32 HAL pin to pop multiple defined messages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:218
#, no-wrap
msgid "Embed Custom VCP Panels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:223
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can optionally embed QtVCP Virtual Control Panels into the QtDragon screens.\n"
"These panels can be either user built or builtin <<cha:qtvcp:panels,QtVCP Panels>>.\n"
"See QtVCP/VCP panels for other available builtin panels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:227
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `EMBED_TAB_NAME` entry will used as the title for the new tab.(must be unique)\n"
"Tab `EMBED_TAB_LOCATION` options include: `tabWidget_utilities`, `tabWidget_setup` and `stackedWidget_mainTab` and `WINDOW`.\n"
"Tab `EMBED_TAB_COMMAND` specifies what embed-able program to run, including any of its command line options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:232
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If using the `tabWidget_utilities` or `tabWidget_setup` locations, an extra tab will appear with the panel.\n"
"If using `stackedWidget_mainTab`, a button labelled 'User' will appear.\n"
"Pressing this button will cycle through displaying all available panels (specified for this location) on the main tab area.\n"
"You also use `WINDOW` to create a pop up window that cab be shown/hidden with an arrow button that will appear near the machine on button"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "Embedding Vismach Mill"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:234
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample adding a builtin panel to the utilities tab, i.e., a graphical animated machine using the vismach library."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:241
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"EMBED_TAB_NAME = Vismach demo\n"
"EMBED_TAB_COMMAND = qtvcp vismach_mill_xyz\n"
"EMBED_TAB_LOCATION = tabWidget_utilities\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:243
#, no-wrap
msgid "Embedding Spindle Belts Panel"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:246
msgid ""
"This example panel is designed to display additional RS485 VFD data and also "
"to configure a 4 sheave, 2 belt spindle drive via a series of buttons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "QtDragon spindle_belts Panel - Spindle Belts VCP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/qtdragon_spindle_belts.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:254
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"EMBED_TAB_NAME = Spindle Belts\n"
"EMBED_TAB_COMMAND = qtvcp spindle_belts\n"
"EMBED_TAB_LOCATION = tabWidget_utilities\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:256
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subroutine Paths"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:262
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If using NGCGUI, remap or custom M codes routines, LinuxCNC needs to know where to look for the files.\n"
"This sample is typical of what is needed for NgcGui, Basic Probe. and Versa Probe remap code.\n"
"These paths will need to be adjusted to point to the actual files on your system. <<sub:ini:sec:rs274ngc,RS274NZGC Section Details>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:269
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[RS274NGC]\n"
"SUBROUTINE_PATH = :~/linuxcnc/nc_files/examples/ngcgui_lib:~/linuxcnc/nc_files/examples/ngcgui_lib/utilitysubs: \\\n"
"~/linuxcnc/nc_files/examples/probe/basic_probe/macros:~/linuxcnc/nc_files/examples/remap-subroutines: \\\n"
"~/linuxcnc/nc_files/examples/ngcgui_lib/remap_lib\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:273
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"QtVCP's NGCGUI program also need to know where to open for subroutine selection and pre-selection.\n"
"NGCGUI_SUBFILE_PATH must point to an actual path on your system and also a path described in SUBROUTINE_PATHS."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:284
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"# NGCGUI subroutine path.\n"
"# Thr path must also  be in [RS274NGC] SUBROUTINE_PATH\n"
"NGCGUI_SUBFILE_PATH = ~/linuxcnc/nc_files/examples/ngcgui_lib\n"
"# pre selected programs tabs\n"
"# specify filenames only, files must be in the NGCGUI_SUBFILE_PATH\n"
"NGCGUI_SUBFILE = slot.ngc\n"
"NGCGUI_SUBFILE = qpocket.ngc\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:289
msgid "Magic comments can be used to control the G-code preview."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:292
msgid ""
"On very large programs the preview can take a long time to load.  You can "
"control what is shown and what is hidden the the graphics screen by adding "
"the appropriate comments from this list into your G-code:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:297
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(PREVIEW,stop)\n"
"(PREVIEW,hide)\n"
"(PREVIEW,show)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:299
#, no-wrap
msgid "Program Extensions/Filters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:304
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can control what programs are displayed in the filemanager window with program extensions.\n"
"Create a line with the '.' endings you wish to use separated by commas, then a space and the description.\n"
"You can add multiple lines for different selections in the combo box."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:309
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[FILTER]\n"
"PROGRAM_EXTENSION = .ngc,.nc,.tap G-Code file (*.ngc,*.nc,*.tap)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:314
msgid ""
"QtDragon has the ability to send loaded files through a 'filter program'.  "
"This filter can do any desired task: Something as simple as making sure the "
"file ends with 'M2', or something as complicated as generating G-code from "
"an image.  See <<cha:filter,Filter Programs>> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:320
msgid ""
"The '[FILTER]' section of the INI file controls how filters work.  First, "
"for each type of file, write a 'PROGRAM_EXTENSION' line.  Then, specify the "
"program to execute for each type of file.  This program is given the name of "
"the input file as its first argument, and must write rs274ngc code to "
"standard output.  This output is what will be displayed in the text area, "
"previewed in the display area, and executed by LinuxCNC when 'Run'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:322
msgid ""
"The following lines add support for the `image-to-gcode` converter included "
"with LinuxCNC and running Python based filter programs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:332
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[FILTER]\n"
"PROGRAM_EXTENSION = .png,.gif,.jpg Greyscale Depth Image\n"
"PROGRAM_EXTENSION = .py Python Script\n"
"png = image-to-gcode\n"
"gif = image-to-gcode\n"
"jpg = image-to-gcode\n"
"py = python\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:334
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probe/Touchplate/Laser Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:338
msgid ""
"QtDragon has INI entries for two optional probing tab screens available.  "
"Comment/uncomment which ever you prefer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:340
msgid ""
"'Versa probe' is a QtVCP ported version of a popular GladeVCP probing panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:341
msgid ""
"'Basic Probe' is a QtVCP ported version based on the third party basic probe "
"screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:343
msgid ""
"Both perform similar probing routines, though Versa probe optionally handles "
"auto tool measurement."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:349 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1230
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[PROBE]\n"
"#USE_PROBE = versaprobe\n"
"USE_PROBE = basicprobe\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:351
#, no-wrap
msgid "Abort detection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:356
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When using qtdragon's probing routines, it is important to detect a user abort request.\n"
"By default, LinuxCNC does not report an abort in a useful way for the probe routines.\n"
"You need to add a ngc file to print out an error that can be detected. <<sub:remap:sec:error-handling, Remap Abort Details>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:362
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[RS274NGC]\n"
"# on abort, this ngc file is called. required for basic/versa probe routines. +\n"
"ON_ABORT_COMMAND=O <on_abort> call\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:366
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This example code will send a message on abort. The probe routines can detect this sample.\n"
"According to the setting above, it would need to be saved as 'on_abort.ngc' within LinuxCNC's [RS274NGC] SUBROUTINE_PATHS and [DISPLAY] PROGRAM_PREFIX search paths."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:370 src/remap/remap.adoc:976
#, no-wrap
msgid "o<on_abort> sub\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:382
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"o100 if [#1 eq 5]\n"
"    (machine on)\n"
"o100 elseif [#1 eq 6]\n"
"    (machine off)\n"
"o100 elseif [#1 eq 7]\n"
"    (estopped)\n"
"o100 elseif [#1 eq 8]\n"
"    (msg,Process Aborted)\n"
"o100 else\n"
"    (DEBUG,Abort Parameter is %d[#1])\n"
"o100 endif\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:385 src/remap/remap.adoc:1001
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"o<on_abort> endsub\n"
"m2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:387
#, no-wrap
msgid "Startup codes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:391
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You should set default M/G code for start up. These will be overridden by running a NGC file.\n"
"These are only sample codes, integrator should choose appropriate codes."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:397
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[RS274NGC]\n"
"# start up G/M codes when first loaded\n"
"RS274NGC_STARTUP_CODE = G17 G20 G40 G43H0 G54 G64P0.0005 G80 G90 G94 G97 M5 M9\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:409
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"QtDragon has up to ten convenience buttons for calling 'macro actions'.\n"
"These are under the heading '[MDI_COMMAND_LIST]' as 'MDI_COMMAND_MACRO0 =' to 'MDI_COMMAND_MACRO9 ='\n"
"These could also call OWord routines if desired.\n"
"In the sample configurations they are labelled for moving between current user system origin (zero point) and Machine system origin.\n"
"User origin is the first MDI command in the INI list, machine origin is the second.\n"
"This example shows how to move Z axis up first. Commands separated by the ';' are run one after another.\n"
"The button label text can be set with any text after a comma, the `\\n` symbol adds a line break."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:416
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[MDI_COMMAND_LIST]\n"
"# for macro buttons\n"
"MDI_COMMAND_MACRO0 = G0 Z25;X0 Y0;Z0, Goto\\nUser\\nZero\n"
"MDI_COMMAND_MACRO1 = G53 G0 Z0;G53 G0 X0 Y0,Goto\\nMachn\\nZero\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:418
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post GUI HAL File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:423
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These optional HAL files will be called after QtDragon has loaded everything else.\n"
"You can add multiple line for multiple file. Each one will be called in the order they appear.\n"
"Calling HAL files after QtDragon is already loaded assures that QtDragon's HAL pins are available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:424
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample with typical entries for the specificion of HAL files to be read after the QtDragon was started. Adjust these lines to match actual requirements."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:430
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[HAL]\n"
"POSTGUI_HALFILE = qtdragon_hd_postgui.hal\n"
"POSTGUI_HALFILE = qtdragon_hd_debugging.hal\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:432
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post GUI HAL Command"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:437
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These optional HAL commands will be run after QtDragon has loaded everything else.\n"
"You can add multiple line. Each one will be called in the order they appear.\n"
"Any HAL command can be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:438
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample with typical files in INI file to load modules after the GUI is available. Adjust these to match your actual requirements."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:445
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[HAL]\n"
"POSTGUI_HALCMD = loadusr qtvcp test_probe\n"
"POSTGUI_HALCMD = loadusr qtvcp test_led\n"
"POSTGUI_HALCMD = loadusr halmeter\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:446
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Overview"
msgid "HAL Bridge"
msgstr "მიმოხილვა"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:449
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hal Bridge is similar to HALUI - it has HAL pins that communicate with QtDragon.\n"
"These pins could be used with HALUI to built a more friendly control panel. +"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:451
msgid "It can report/change the current selected Axis button. +"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:452
msgid "The jog rate/increments will be reported. +"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:453
msgid ""
"There is a cycle start and pause pin - these call the code in QtDragon "
"rather then the motion controller. +"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:454
msgid ""
"If there are macros defined in the INI, there will be pins available to "
"initiate them. +"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:455
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample entry. Remove '-d' to quiet debugging messages."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:460
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[HAL]\n"
"HALBRIDGE= hal_bridge -d\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:462
#, no-wrap
msgid "Typical HAL pins avaialble:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:482
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Component Pins:\n"
"Owner   Type  Dir                 Value  Name\n"
"    38  s32   OUT                     0  base-thread.time\n"
"    29  bit   OUT                 FALSE  bridge.axis-x-is-selected\n"
"    29  bit   IN                  FALSE  bridge.axis-x-select\n"
"    29  bit   OUT                 FALSE  bridge.axis-y-is-selected\n"
"    29  bit   IN                  FALSE  bridge.axis-y-select\n"
"    29  bit   OUT                 FALSE  bridge.axis-z-is-selected\n"
"    29  bit   IN                  FALSE  bridge.axis-z-select\n"
"    29  bit   IN                  FALSE  bridge.cycle-pause-in\n"
"    29  bit   IN                  FALSE  bridge.cycle-start-in\n"
"    29  float OUT                     0  bridge.jog-increment\n"
"    29  float OUT                     0  bridge.jog-increment-angular\n"
"    29  float OUT                    15  bridge.jog-rate\n"
"    29  float OUT                   360  bridge.jog-rate-angular\n"
"    29  s32   OUT                    -1  bridge.joint-selected\n"
"    29  bit   IN                  FALSE  bridge.macro-cmd-MACRO0\n"
"    29  bit   IN                  FALSE  bridge.macro-cmd-MACRO1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:484
#, no-wrap
msgid "Builtin Sample Configurations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:488
msgid ""
"The sample configurations `sim/qtdragon/` or `sim/qtdragon_hd` are already "
"configured to use QtDragon as the screen.  There are several examples that "
"demonstrate various machine configurations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:489
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key Bindings"
msgstr "კლავიატურის ბმები"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:494
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"QtDragon is not intended to primarily use a keyboard for machine control.\n"
"It lacks many keyboard short cuts that for instance AXIS has - but you can use a mouse or touchscreen.\n"
"There are several key presses that will control the machine for convenience."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:502
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"F1 - Estop on/off\n"
"F2 - Machine on/off\n"
"F12 - Style Editor\n"
"Home - Home All Joint of the Machine\n"
"Escape - Abort Movement\n"
"Pause - Pause Machine Movement\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:508
msgid ""
"Buttons that are checkable will change their text colour when checked.  This "
"is controlled by the stylesheet/theme"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:515
msgid ""
"QtDragon includes a virtual keyboard for use with touchscreens.  To enable "
"the keyboard, check the Use Virtual Keyboard checkbox in the Settings page.  "
"Clicking on any input field, such as probe parameters or tool table entries, "
"will show the keyboard.  To hide the keyboard, do one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:517
msgid "press the 'HIDE' button on the virtual keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:518
msgid "click the MAIN page button"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:519
msgid "go into AUTO mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:521
msgid ""
"It should be noted that keyboard jogging is disabled when using the virtual "
"keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:526
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These pins are specific to the QtDragon screen.\n"
"There are of course are many more HAL pins that must be connected for LinuxCNC to function."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:529
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you need a manual tool change prompt, add these lines in your postgui file.\n"
"QtDragon emulates the hal_manualtoolchange HAL pins - don't load the separate HAL component 'hal_manualtoolchange'."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:535 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:688
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"net tool-change      hal_manualtoolchange.change   <=  iocontrol.0.tool-change\n"
"net tool-changed     hal_manualtoolchange.changed  <=  iocontrol.0.tool-changed\n"
"net tool-prep-number hal_manualtoolchange.number   <=  iocontrol.0.tool-prep-number\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:538
msgid ""
"Also if you don't have an automatic tool changer make sure these pins are "
"connected in one of the HAL files:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:542
#, no-wrap
msgid "net tool-prepare-loopback iocontrol.0.tool-prepare => iocontrol.0.tool-prepared\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:545
msgid "This input pin should be connected to indicate probe state."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:549
#, no-wrap
msgid "qtdragon.led-probe\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:554
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These pins are inputs related to spindle VFD indicating.\n"
"The volt and amp pins are used to calculate spindle power. You must also set the MAX_SPINDLE_POWER in the INI."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:562
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"qtdragon.spindle-modbus-connection\n"
"qtdragon.spindle-modbus-errors\n"
"qtdragon.spindle-amps\n"
"qtdragon.spindle-fault\n"
"qtdragon.spindle-volts\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:566
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This bit pin is an output to the spindle control to pause it.\n"
"You would connect it to `spindle.0.inhibit`."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:570
#, no-wrap
msgid "qtdragon.spindle-inhibit\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:576
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"QtDragon spindle speed display and spindle-at-speed LED require that\n"
" `spindle.0.speed-in` be connected to spindle speed feedback. +\n"
"Encoder or VFD feedback could be used, as long as the feedback is in revolutions per second (RPS). +\n"
"If no feedback is available you can have the display show the requested speed by connecting pins like so:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:580
#, no-wrap
msgid "net spindle-speed-feedback spindle.0.speed-out-rps => spindle.0.speed-in\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:583
msgid "This bit output pin can be connected to turn on a laser:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:587
#, no-wrap
msgid "qtdragon.btn-laser-on\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:590
msgid "This float output pin indicates the camera rotation in degrees:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:594
#, no-wrap
msgid "qtdragon.cam-rotation\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:597
msgid ""
"These bit/s32/float pins are related to external offsets if they are used:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:606
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"qtdragon.eoffset-clear\n"
"qtdragon.eoffset-enable\n"
"qtdragon.eoffset-value\n"
"qtdragon.eoffset-spindle-count\n"
"qtdragon.eoffset-zlevel-count\n"
"qtdragon.eoffset-is-active\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:609
msgid ""
"These float output pins reflect the current slider jograte (in machine "
"units):"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:614
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"qtdragon.slider-jogspeed-linear\n"
"qtdragon.slider-jogspeed-angular\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
