#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:231
#, no-wrap
msgid "Handler Patching - Subclassing Builtin Screens"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:235 src/gui/qtvcp-vcp-panels.adoc:498
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can have QtVCP load a subclassed version of the standard handler file. In that file we can manipulate the original functions or add new ones.\n"
"Subclassing just means our handler file first loads the original handler file and adds our new code on top of it - effectively a patch of changes.\n"
"This is useful for changing/adding behaviour while still retaining standard handler updates from LinuxCNC repositories."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:238
msgid ""
"You may still need to use the handler copy dialog to copy the original "
"handler file to decide how to patch it.  See 'custom handler file'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:242
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There should be a folder in the config folder; for screens: named '<CONFIG FOLDER>/qtvcp/screens/<SCREEN NAME>/'\n"
"add the handle patch file there, named like so <ORIGINAL SCREEN NAME>_handler.py,\n"
"e.g., for QtDragon the file would be called 'qtdragon_handler.py'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:244
msgid "Here is a sample to add X axis jog pins to a screen like QtDragon:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:253
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"import sys\n"
"import importlib\n"
"from qtvcp.core import Path, Qhal, Action\n"
"PATH = Path()\n"
"QHAL = Qhal()\n"
"ACTION = Action()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:260
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# get reference to original handler file so we can subclass it\n"
"sys.path.insert(0, PATH.SCREENDIR)\n"
"module = \"{}.{}_handler\".format(PATH.BASEPATH,PATH.BASEPATH)\n"
"mod = importlib.import_module(module, PATH.SCREENDIR)\n"
"sys.path.remove(PATH.SCREENDIR)\n"
"HandlerClass = mod.HandlerClass\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:264
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# return our subclassed handler object to QtVCP\n"
"def get_handlers(halcomp, widgets, paths):\n"
"    return [UserHandlerClass(halcomp, widgets, paths)]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:269
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# sub class HandlerClass which was imported above\n"
"class UserHandlerClass(HandlerClass):\n"
"    # add a terminal message so we know this got loaded\n"
"    print('\\nCustom subclassed handler patch loaded.\\n')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:273
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    def init_pins(self):\n"
"        # call original handler init_pins function\n"
"        super().init_pins()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:277
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        # add jog pins X axis\n"
"        pin = QHAL.newpin(\"jog.axis.jog-x-plus\", QHAL.HAL_BIT, QHAL.HAL_IN)\n"
"        pin.value_changed.connect(lambda s: self.kb_jog(s, 0, 1, fast = False, linear = True))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:280
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        pin = QHAL.newpin(\"jog.axis.jog-x-minus\", QHAL.HAL_BIT, QHAL.HAL_IN)\n"
"        pin.value_changed.connect(lambda s: self.kb_jog(s, 0, -1, fast = False, linear = True))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:282
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minor Python Code Changes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:286
msgid ""
"Another Python file can be used to *add commands* to the screen, after the "
"handler file is parsed.  This can be useful for minor changes while still "
"honouring standard handler updates from LinuxCNC repositories."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:289
msgid ""
"Handler patching is a better way to add changes - instance patching is black "
"magic voodoo - this is here for legacy reasons."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:293
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the _INI file_ under the `[DISPLAY]` heading add *`USER_COMMAND_FILE = _PATH_`*\n"
"_PATH_ can be any valid path. It can use `~` for home directory or `WORKINGFOLDER` or `CONFIGFOLDER` to represent QtVCP's idea of those directories, e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:298
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[DISPLAY]\n"
"USER_COMMAND_FILE = CONFIGFOLDER/<screen_name_added_commands>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:302
msgid ""
"If no entry is found in the _INI_, QtVCP will look in the *default path*.  "
"The default path is in the configuration directory as a hidden file using "
"the screen basename and rc, e.g., *`CONFIGURATION DIRECTORY/."
"<screen_name>rc`*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:304
msgid ""
"This file will be read and executed as Python code in the *handler file "
"context*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:310
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Only local functions and local attributes* can be referenced.\n"
"Global libraries defined in the screen's handler file can be referenced by importing the handler file.\n"
"These are usually seen as all capital words with no preceding self.\n"
"'self' references the window class functions.\n"
"'self.w' typically references the widgets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:312
msgid "What can be used can vary by screen and development cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:313
#, no-wrap
msgid "A simple example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:315
msgid ""
"Reference the main window to change the title (won't show if using INI "
"entries for title change)."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:319
#, no-wrap
msgid "self.w.setWindowTitle('My Title Test')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:321
#, no-wrap
msgid "An advanced instance patching example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:324
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This could work with the QtDragon screen's handler file.\n"
"Here we show how to add new functions and override existing ones."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:330
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Needed to instance patch.\n"
"# reference: https://ruivieira.dev/python-monkey-patching-for-readability.html\n"
"import types\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:334
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# import the handlerfile to get reference to its libraries.\n"
"# use <screenname>_handler\n"
"import qtdragon_handler as hdlr\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:341
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# This is actually an unbounded function with 'obj' as a parameter.\n"
"# You call this function without the usual preceding 'self.'.\n"
"# This is because will will not be patching it into the original handler class instance\n"
"# It will only be called from code in this file.\n"
"def test_function(obj):\n"
"    print(dir(obj))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:349
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# This is a new function we will added to the existing handler class instance.\n"
"# Notice it calls the unbounded function with 'self' as an parameter 'self' is the only global reference available.\n"
"# It references the window instance.\n"
"def on_keycall_F10(self,event,state,shift,cntrl):\n"
"    if state:\n"
"        print ('F10')\n"
"        test_function(self)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:357
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# This will be used to override an existing function in the existing handler class instance.\n"
"# Note, we also call a copy of the original function too.\n"
"# This shows how to extend an existing function to do extra functions.\n"
"def on_keycall_F11(self,event,state,shift,cntrl):\n"
"    if state:\n"
"        self.on_keycall_F11_super(event,state,shift,cntrl)\n"
"        print ('Hello')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:362
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# We are referencing the KEYBIND library that was instantiated in the original handler class instance\n"
"# by adding 'hdlr.' to it (from the imp).\n"
"# This function tells KEYBIND to call 'on_keycall_F10' when F10 is pressed.\n"
"hdlr.KEYBIND.add_call('Key_F10','on_keycall_F10')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:366
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Here we are instance patching the original handler file to add a new function\n"
"# that calls our new function (of the same name) defined in this file.\n"
"self.on_keycall_F10 = types.MethodType(on_keycall_F10, self)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:371
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Here we are defining a copy of the original 'on_keycall_F11' function,\n"
"# so we can call it later. We can use any valid, unused function name.\n"
"# We need to do this before overriding the original function.\n"
"self.on_keycall_F11_super = self.on_keycall_F11\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:375
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Here we are instance patching the original handler file to override an existing function\n"
"# to point to our new function (of the same name) defined in this file.\n"
"self.on_keycall_F11 = types.MethodType(on_keycall_F11, self)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:378
#, no-wrap
msgid "# add a new pin to the screen:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:382
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# pin callback to print the state\n"
"def new_pin_changed(data):\n"
"    print(data)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:391
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Special function that gets called before the HAL component is set ready.\n"
"# Here we used the function to add a bit input pin with a callback.\n"
"def after_override__(self):\n"
"    try:\n"
"        pin = hdlr.QHAL.newpin(\"new_pin\", hdlr.QHAL.HAL_BIT, hdlr.QHAL.HAL_IN)\n"
"        pin.value_changed.connect(new_pin_changed)\n"
"    except Exception as e:\n"
"        print(e)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:395
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Here we are instance patching the original handler file to add a new function\n"
"# that calls our new function (of the same name) defined in this file.\n"
"self.after_override__ = types.MethodType(after_override__, self)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/qtvcp.adoc:398
#, no-wrap
msgid "Full Creative Control with custom handler/ui files"
