#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error Code Collecting"
msgstr ""

#. FIXME which place ?
#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:103
msgid "*LinuxCNC's error code collecting can only be read from one place*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:106
msgid "When read, it is *'consumed'*, i.e. _no other object can read it_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:108
msgid ""
"In QtVCP screens, it is recommended to _use the_ `ScreenOptions` _widget to "
"set up error reading_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:110
msgid "_Errors are then *sent to other objects* via_ *`STATUS`* _signals_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:114
msgid ""
"*LinuxCNC has no internal record of jog rate*: _you must specify it at the "
"time of jogging_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:116
msgid ""
"QtVCP uses the `STATUS` library to _keep track of the latest linear and "
"angular jog rates_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:124
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is *always specified in machine units per minute* and _must be converted when in non-machine units mode_.\n"
"So, if your machine is imperial based but you are in metric mode, changes to jog rate sent to `ACTION` functions must be converted to imperial.\n"
"In the same manner, if the machine is metric based and you are in imperial mode, changes to jog rate must be sent to `ACTION` functions in metric units.\n"
"_For angular jog rates the units don't change in metric/imperial mode_ so you can send them to `ACTION` functions without conversion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:128
msgid ""
"While you are free to ignore this jogging record while building screens, "
"anyone modifying your screen and using the builtin jog rate widgets would "
"not get the desired results as the `ACTION` library's *`DO_JOG`* function "
"gets it's jog rate from the `STATUS` library."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keybinding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:132
msgid "Keybinding is always a _difficult-to-get-right-in-all-cases_ affair."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:134
msgid "Custom keybinding functions are to be _defined in the handler file_."
msgstr ""

#. TODO Elaborate ?
#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-development.adoc:137
msgid ""
"Most importantly widgets that require regular key input and not jogging, "
"should be checked for in the `processed_key_event__` function."
msgstr ""

