#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3199
msgid ""
"The *`python_command_option`* allow small snippets of Python code to be run "
"from the push of a button, without having to edit the handler file.  Though, "
"it can call functions in the handler file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3201
msgid "When using the `command_string` properties."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3202
#, no-wrap
msgid "*`true_python_cmd_string`*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3204
msgid "A Python command that will be called when the button is toggled `True`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3204
#, no-wrap
msgid "*`false_python_cmd_string`*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3206
msgid ""
"A Python command that will be called when the button is toggled `False`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3208
msgid "_Special capitalized words_ will give access to the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3212
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Will give access to the widgets instances and handler functions.\n"
"E.g., `INSTANCE.my_handler_function_call(True)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3212
#, no-wrap
msgid "*`ACTION`*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3215
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Will give access to QtVCP's `ACTION` library.\n"
"E.g., `ACTION.TOGGLE_FLOOD()`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3215
#, no-wrap
msgid "*`PROGRAM_LOADER`*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:3218
