#. type: Index entry
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:44 src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "addf"
msgstr ""

#. type: Index entry
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:49
msgid "HAL addf"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:49
msgid ""
"The `addf` command adds a function to a real-time thread.  If the StepConf "
"wizard was used to create the configuration, two threads have been created "
"(``base-thread`` and ``servo-thread``)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:55
msgid ""
"`addf` adds function _functname_ to thread _threadname_.  Default is to add "
"the function in the order they are in the file.  If _position_ is specified, "
"adds the function to that spot in the thread.  A negative _position_ "
"indicates the position with respect to the end of the thread.  For example "
"'1' is start of thread, '-1' is the end of the thread, '-3' is third from "
"the end."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:59
msgid ""
"For some functions it is important to load them in a certain order, like the "
"parport read and write functions.  The function name is usually the "
"component name plus a number.  In the following example the component 'or2' "
"is loaded and `show function` shows the name of the or2 function."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ halrun\n"
"halcmd: loadrt or2\n"
"halcmd: show function\n"
"Exported Functions:\n"
"Owner   CodeAddr  Arg       FP   Users  Name\n"
" 00004  f8bc5000  f8f950c8  NO       0   or2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:73
msgid ""
"You have to add a function from a HAL real time component to a thread to get "
"the function to update at the rate of the thread.  Usually there are two "
"threads as shown in this example.  Some components use floating point math "
"and must be added to a thread that supports floating point math.  The `FP` "
"indicates if floating point math is supported in that thread."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:82
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ halrun\n"
"halcmd: loadrt motmod base_period_nsec=55555 servo_period_nsec=1000000 num_joints=3\n"
"halcmd: show thread\n"
"Realtime Threads:\n"
"     Period  FP     Name               (     Time, Max-Time )\n"
"     995976  YES          servo-thread (        0,        0 )\n"
"      55332  NO            base-thread (        0,        0 )\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:87
msgid ""
"base-thread (the high-speed thread): This thread handles items that need a "
"fast response, like making step pulses, and reading and writing the parallel "
"port.  Does not support floating point math."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:89
msgid ""
"servo-thread (the slow-speed thread): This thread handles items that can "
"tolerate a slower response, like the motion controller, ClassicLadder, and "
"the motion command handler and supports floating point math."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "addf Syntax and Example"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:95
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"addf <function> <thread>\n"
"addf mux4.0 servo-thread\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:99
msgid ""
"If the component requires a floating point thread that is usually the slower "
"servo-thread."
msgstr ""

#. type: Index entry
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:101 src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "loadusr"
msgstr ""

#. type: Index entry
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:107
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Float"
msgid "HAL loadusr"
msgstr "მცურავი"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/hal/basic-hal.adoc:107
msgid ""
"The command `loadusr` loads a non-realtime HAL component.  Non-realtime "
"programs are their own separate processes, which optionally talk to other "
"HAL components via pins and parameters.  You cannot load realtime components "
"into non-realtime space."
