#. type: Index entry
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:5 src/hal/halmodule.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Creating Non-realtime Python Components"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:9
msgid ""
"This section explains principles behind the implementation of HAL components "
"with the Python programming language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Basic usage example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:14
msgid ""
"A non-realtime component begins by creating its pins and parameters, then "
"enters a loop which will periodically drive all the outputs from the "
"inputs.  The following component copies the value seen on its input pin "
"('passthrough.in') to its output pin ('passthrough.out') approximately once "
"per second."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n"
"import hal, time\n"
"h = hal.component(\"passthrough\")\n"
"h.newpin(\"in\", hal.HAL_FLOAT, hal.HAL_IN)\n"
"h.newpin(\"out\", hal.HAL_FLOAT, hal.HAL_OUT)\n"
"h.ready()\n"
"try:\n"
"    while 1:\n"
"        time.sleep(1)\n"
"        h['out'] = h['in']\n"
"except KeyboardInterrupt:\n"
"    raise SystemExit\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:33
msgid ""
"Copy the above listing into a file named \"passthrough\", make it executable "
"('chmod +x'), and place it on your '$PATH'.  Then try it out:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "Screen copy with details on the execution of the newly created passthrough HAL module."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ halrun\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "halcmd: loadusr passthrough\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:41 src/hal/halmodule.adoc:50
#: src/hal/tutorial.adoc:157 src/hal/tutorial.adoc:279
#: src/hal/tutorial.adoc:297 src/hal/tutorial.adoc:336
#: src/hal/tutorial.adoc:573
#, no-wrap
msgid "halcmd: show pin\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Component Pins:\n"
"    Owner Type  Dir     Value  Name\n"
"     03   float IN          0  passthrough.in\n"
"     03   float OUT         0  passthrough.out\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "halcmd: setp passthrough.in 3.14\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Component Pins:\n"
"    Owner Type  Dir     Value  Name\n"
"     03   float IN       3.14  passthrough.in\n"
"     03   float OUT      3.14  passthrough.out\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "Non-realtime components and delays"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:63
msgid ""
"If you typed \"show pin\" quickly, you may see that 'passthrough.out' still "
"had its old value of 0.  This is because of the call to 'time.sleep(1)', "
"which makes the assignment to the output pin occur at most once per second.  "
"Because this is a non-realtime component, the actual delay between "
"assignments can be much longer if the memory used by the passthrough "
"component is swapped to disk, as the assignment could be delayed until that "
"memory is swapped back in."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:66
msgid ""
"Thus, non-realtime components are suitable for user-interactive elements "
"such as control panels (delays in the range of milliseconds are not noticed, "
"and longer delays are acceptable), but not for sending step pulses to a "
"stepper driver board (delays must always be in the range of microseconds, no "
"matter what)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create pins and parameters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:77
msgid ""
"The component itself is created by a call to the constructor "
"'hal.component'.  The arguments are the HAL component name and (optionally) "
"the prefix used for pin and parameter names.  If the prefix is not "
"specified, the component name is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/halmodule.adoc:86
msgid ""
"Then pins are created by calls to methods on the component object.  The "
"arguments are: pin name suffix, pin type, and pin direction.  For "
"parameters, the arguments are: parameter name suffix, parameter type, and "
"parameter direction."
msgstr ""

