#. type: Title ===
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:312
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONTACTS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:315
msgid ""
"Represent switches or relay contacts. They are controlled by the variable "
"letter and number assigned to them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:323
msgid ""
"The variable letter can be B, I, or Q and the number can be up to a three "
"digit number, e.g. `%I2`, `%Q3`, or `%B123`.  Variable I is controlled by a "
"HAL input pin with a corresponding number.  Variable B is for internal "
"contacts, controlled by a B coil with a corresponding number.  Variable Q is "
"controlled by a Q coil with a corresponding number (like a relay with "
"multiple contacts).  E.g., if HAL pin `classicladder.0.in-00` is true then "
"%I0 N.O. contact would be on (closed, true, whatever you like to call it).  "
"If %B7 coil is 'energized' (on, true, etc) then %B7 N.O. contact would be "
"on.  If %Q1 coil is 'energized' then %Q1 N.O. contact would be on (and HAL "
"pin `classicladder.0.out-01` would be true)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:326
msgid ""
"'N.O. Contact' - image:images/ladder_action_load.png[\"Normally Open "
"Contact\"] (Normally Open)  When the variable is false the switch is off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:328
msgid ""
"'N.C. Contact' - image:images/ladder_action_loadbar.png[\"Normally Closed "
"Contact\"] (Normally Closed)  When the variable is false the switch is on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:329
msgid ""
"'Rising Edge Contact' - When the variable changes from false to true, the "
"switch is PULSED on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:330
msgid ""
"'Falling Edge Contact' - When the variable changes from true to false, the "
"switch is PULSED on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:331
#, no-wrap
msgid "IEC TIMERS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:334
msgid ""
"Represent new count down timers. IEC Timers replace Timers and Monostables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:336
msgid "IEC Timers have 2 contacts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:338
msgid "'I' - input contact"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:339
msgid "'Q' - output contact"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:341
msgid "There are three modes - TON, TOF, TP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:344
msgid ""
"'TON' - When timer input is true countdown begins and continues as long as "
"input remains true.  After countdown is done and as long as timer input is "
"still true the output will be true."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:345
msgid ""
"'TOF' - When timer input is true, sets output true. When the input is false "
"the timer counts down then sets output false."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:346
msgid ""
"'TP' - When timer input is pulsed true or held true timer sets output true "
"till timer counts down. (one-shot)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:348
msgid ""
"The time intervals can be set in multiples of 100&8239;ms, seconds, or "
"minutes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:350
msgid ""
"There are also Variables for IEC timers that can be read and/or written to "
"in compare or operate blocks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:352
msgid "'%TMxxx.Q' - timer done (Boolean, read write)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:353
msgid "'%TMxxx.P' - timer preset (read write)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:354
msgid "'%TMxxx.V' - timer value (read write)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:355
#, no-wrap
msgid "TIMERS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:358
msgid ""
"Represent count down timers. This is deprecated and replaced by IEC Timers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:360
msgid "Timers have 4 contacts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:362
msgid "'E' - enable (input) starts timer when true, resets when goes false"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:363
msgid ""
"'C' - control (input) must be on for the timer to run (usually connect to E)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:364
msgid ""
"'D' - done (output) true when timer times out and as long as E remains true"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:365
msgid "'R' - running (output) true when timer is running"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:367
msgid "The timer base can be multiples of milliseconds, seconds, or minutes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:369
msgid ""
"There are also Variables for timers that can be read and/or written to in "
"compare or operate blocks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:371
msgid "'%Txx.R' - Timer xx running (Boolean, read only)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:372
msgid "'%Txx.D' - Timer xx done (Boolean, read only)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:373
msgid "'%Txx.V' - Timer xx current value (integer, read only)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:374
msgid "'%Txx.P' - Timer xx preset (integer, read or write)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:375
#, no-wrap
msgid "MONOSTABLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:378
msgid ""
"Represent the original one-shot timers. This is now deprecated and replaced "
"by IEC Timers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:380
msgid "Monostables have 2 contacts, I and R."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:382
msgid "'I' - input (input) will start the mono timer running."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:383
msgid "'R' - running (output) will be true while timer is running."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:388
msgid ""
"The I contact is rising edge sensitive meaning it starts the timer only when "
"changing from false to true (or off to on).  While the timer is running the "
"I contact can change with no effect to the running timer.  R will be true "
"and stay true till the timer finishes counting to zero.  The timer base can "
"be multiples of milliseconds, seconds, or minutes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:390
msgid ""
"There are also Variables for monostables that can be read and/or written to "
"in compare or operate blocks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:392
msgid "'%Mxx.R' - Monostable xx running (Boolean, read only)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:393
msgid "'%Mxx.V' - Monostable xx current value (integer, read only)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:394
msgid "'%Mxx.P' - Monostable xx preset (integer, read or write)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:395
#, no-wrap
msgid "COUNTERS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:398
msgid "Represent up/down counters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:400
msgid "There are 7 contacts:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:402
msgid "'R' - reset (input) will reset the count to 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:403
msgid ""
"'P' - preset (input) will set the count to the preset number assigned from "
"the edit menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:404
msgid "'U' - up count (input) will add one to the count."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:405
msgid "'D' - down count (input) will subtract one from the count."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:406
msgid ""
"'E' - under flow (output) will be true when the count rolls over from 0 to "
"9999."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:407
msgid "'D' - done (output) will be true when the count equals the preset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:408
msgid ""
"'F' - overflow (output) will be true when the count rolls over from 9999 to "
"0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:410
msgid ""
"The up and down count contacts are edge sensitive meaning they only count "
"when the contact changes from false to true (or off to on if you prefer)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:412
msgid "The range is 0 to 9999."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:414
msgid ""
"There are also Variables for counters that can be read and/or written to in "
"compare or operate blocks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:416
msgid "'%C'__xx__`.D` - Counter _xx_ done (_Boolean_, _read only_)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:417
msgid "'%C'__xx__`.E` - Counter _xx_ empty overflow (_Boolean_, _read only__)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:418
msgid "'%C'__xx__`.F` - Counter _xx_ full overflow (_Boolean_, _read only_)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:419
msgid ""
"'%C'__xx__`.V` - Counter _xx_ current value (_integer_, _read_ or _write_)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:420
msgid "'%C'__xx__`.P` - Counter _xx_ preset (_integer_, _read_ or _write_)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:421
#, no-wrap
msgid "COMPARE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:424
msgid ""
"For arithmetic comparison. Is variable %XXX = to this number (or evaluated "
"number)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:426
msgid ""
"The compare block will be true when comparison is true. You can use most "
"math symbols:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:428
msgid "`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `=` (standard math symbols)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:429
msgid ""
"`<` (less than), `>` (greater than), `<=` (less or equal), `>=` (greater or "
"equal), `<>` (not equal)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:431
msgid ""
"`(`, `)` separate into groups example `%IF1=2,&%IF2<5` in pseudo code "
"translates to if %IF1 is equal to 2 and %IF2 is less than 5 then the "
"comparison is true.  Note the comma separating the two groups of comparisons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:432
msgid "`^` (exponent), `%` (modulus), `&` (and), `|` (or),. -"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:433
msgid "`ABS` (absolute), `MOY` (French for average), `AVG` (average)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:435
msgid "For example ABS(%W2)=1, MOY(%W1,%W2)<3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:438
msgid ""
"No spaces are allowed in the comparison equation.  For example `%C0.V>%C0.P` "
"is a valid comparison expression while `%C0.V > %CO.P` is not a valid "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:441
msgid ""
"There is a list of Variables down the page that can be used for reading from "
"and writing to ladder objects.  When a new compare block is opened be sure "
"and delete the `#` symbol when you enter a compare."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:443
msgid ""
"To find out if word variable #1 is less than 2 times the current value of "
"counter #0 the syntax would be:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:446
#, no-wrap
msgid "%W1<2*%C0.V\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:449
msgid "To find out if S32in bit 2 is equal to 10 the syntax would be:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:452
#, no-wrap
msgid "%IW2=10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:455
msgid ""
"Note: Compare uses the arithmetic equals not the double equals that "
"programmers are used to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:456
#, no-wrap
msgid "VARIABLE ASSIGNMENT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:460
msgid ""
"For variable assignment, e.g. assign this number (or evaluated number) to "
"this variable %xxx, there are two math functions MINI and MAXI that check a "
"variable for maximum (0x80000000) and minimum values (0x07FFFFFFF) (think "
"signed values) and keeps them from going beyond."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:462
msgid ""
"When a new variable assignment block is opened be sure to delete the `#` "
"symbol when you enter an assignment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:464
msgid ""
"To assign a value of 10 to the timer preset of IEC Timer 0 the syntax would "
"be:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:467
#, no-wrap
msgid "%TM0.P=10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:470
msgid "To assign the value of 12 to s32out bit 3 the syntax would be:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:473
#, no-wrap
msgid "%QW3=12\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:478
msgid ""
"When you assign a value to a variable with the variable assignment block the "
"value is retained until you assign a new value using the variable assignment "
"block.  The last value assigned will be restored when LinuxCNC is started."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:482
msgid ""
"The following figure shows an Assignment and a Comparison Example.  %QW0 is "
"a S32out bit and %IW0 is a S32in bit.  In this case the HAL pin "
"`classicladder.0.s32out-00` will be set to a value of 5 and when the HAL pin "
"`classicladder.0.s32in-00` is 0 the HAL pin `classicladder.0.out-00` will be "
"set to True."
msgstr ""

