"`%X`__xxx__`.V` - Time of activity in seconds of step _xxx_ (sequential "
"language)"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:577
msgid "`%E`__xx__ - Errors (Boolean, read write(will be overwritten))"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:580
msgid ""
"'Indexed or vectored variables' - These are variables indexed by another "
"variable.  Some might call this vectored variables.  Example: `%W0[%W4]` => "
"if %W4 equals 23 it corresponds to %W23"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:581
#, no-wrap
msgid "GRAFCET (State Machine) Programming"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:589
msgid ""
"This is probably the least used and most poorly understood feature of "
"ClassicLadder.  Sequential programming is used to make sure a series of "
"ladder events always happen in a prescribed order.  Sequential programs do "
"not work alone.  There is always a ladder program as well that controls the "
"variables.  Here are the basic rules governing sequential programs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:592
msgid ""
"Rule 1 : Initial situation - The initial situation is characterized by the "
"initial steps which are by definition in the active state at the beginning "
"of the operation.  There shall be at least one initial step."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:595
msgid ""
"Rule 2 : R2, Clearing of a transition - A transition is either enabled or "
"disabled.  It is said to be enabled when all immediately preceding steps "
"linked to its corresponding transition symbol are active, otherwise it is "
"disabled.  A transition cannot be cleared unless it is enabled, and its "
"associated transition condition is true."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:596
msgid ""
"Rule 3 : R3, Evolution of active steps - The clearing of a transition "
"simultaneously leads to the active state of the immediately following "
"step(s) and to the inactive state of the immediately preceding step(s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:597
msgid ""
"Rule 4 : R4, Simultaneous clearing of transitions - All simultaneous cleared "
"transitions are simultaneously cleared."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:598
msgid ""
"Rule 5 : R5, Simultaneous activation and deactivation of a step - If during "
"operation, a step is simultaneously activated and deactivated, priority is "
"given to the activation."
msgstr ""

#. FIXME Convert CL sequential editor window description to table or add callouts on image
#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:607
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the SEQUENTIAL editor window. (Starting from the top left):\n"
"Selector arrow, Eraser\n"
"Ordinary step,  Initial (Starting) step\n"
"Transition,  Step and Transition\n"
"Transition Link-Downside,  Transition Link-Upside\n"
"Pass-through Link-Downside, Pass-through Link-Upside Jump\n"
"Link, Comment Box +"
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:608 src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:609
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sequence Editor Window"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:609
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/sequence-editor.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:612
msgid "'ORDINARY STEP' - has a unique number for each one"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:613
msgid ""
"'STARTING STEP' - a sequential program must have one. This is where the "
"program will start."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:614
msgid ""
"'TRANSITION' - shows the variable that must be true for control to pass "
"through to the next step."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:615
msgid "'STEP AND TRANSITION' - combined for convenience"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:616
msgid ""
"'TRANSITION LINK-DOWNSIDE' - splits the logic flow to one of two possible "
"lines based on which of the next steps is true first (Think OR logic)"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:617
msgid "'TRANSITION LINK=UPSIDE' - combines two (OR) logic lines back in to one"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:618
msgid ""
"'PASS-THROUGH LINK-DOWNSIDE' - splits the logic flow to two lines that BOTH "
"must be true to continue (Think AND logic)"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:619
msgid ""
"'PASS-THROUGH LINK-UPSIDE' - combines two concurrent (AND logic) logic lines "
"back together"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:620
msgid ""
"'JUMP LINK' - connects steps that are not underneath each other such as "
"connecting the last step to the first"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:621
msgid "'COMMENT BOX' - used to add comments"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:625
msgid ""
"To use links, you must have steps already placed.  Select the type of link, "
"then select the two steps or transactions one at a time.  It takes practice!"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:631
msgid ""
"With sequential programming: The variable `%X`__xxx__ (e.g., `%X5`) is used "
"to see if a step is active.  The variable `%X`__xxx__`.V` (e.g., `%X5.V`) is "
"used to see how long the step has been active.  The %X and %X.v variables "
"are use in LADDER logic. The variables assigned to the transitions (e.g., "
"%B) control whether the logic will pass to the next step.  After a step has "
"become active the transition variable that caused it to become active has no "
"control of it anymore.  The last step has to JUMP LINK back only to the "
"beginning step."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:632
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modbus"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:635
msgid "Things to consider:"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:637
msgid ""
"Modbus is a non-realtime program so it might have latency issues on a "
"heavily laden computer."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:638
msgid ""
"Modbus is not really suited to hard real time events such as position "
"control of motors or to control E-stop."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:639
msgid "The ClassicLadder GUI must be running for Modbus to be running."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:640
msgid "Modbus is not fully finished so it does not do all modbus functions."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:642
msgid ""
"To get MODBUS to initialize you must specify that when loading the "
"ClassicLadder non-realtime program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:643
#, no-wrap
msgid "Loading Modbus"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:646
#, no-wrap
msgid "loadusr -w classicladder --modmaster myprogram.clp\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:650
msgid ""
"The `-w` makes HAL wait until you close ClassicLadder before closing "
"realtime session.  ClassicLadder also loads a TCP modbus slave if you add `--"
"modserver` on command line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:651
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modbus Functions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:653
msgid "'1' - read coils"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:654
msgid "'2' - read inputs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:655
msgid "'3' - read holding registers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:656
msgid "'4' - read input registers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:657
msgid "'5' - write single coils"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:658
msgid "'6' - write single register"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:659
msgid "'8' - echo test"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:660
msgid "'15' - write multiple coils"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:661
msgid "'16' - write multiple registers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:663
msgid ""
"If you do not specify a '--modmaster' when loading the ClassicLadder non-"
"realtime program this page will not be displayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:665
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modbus I/O Config"
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:666
#, no-wrap
msgid "Config I/O"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:666
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/Config-io.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:669
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modbus Communication Config"
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:670
#, no-wrap
msgid "Config Coms"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:670
#, no-wrap
msgid "images/Config-com.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:673
msgid ""
"'SERIAL PORT' - For IP blank. For serial the location/name of serial driver, "
"e.g., /dev/ttyS0 ( or /dev/ttyUSB0 for a USB-to-serial converter)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:674
msgid ""
"'SERIAL SPEED' - Should be set to speed the slave is set for - 300, 600, "
"1200, 2400, 4800, 9600, 19200, 38400, 57600, 115200 are supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:675
msgid ""
"'PAUSE AFTER TRANSMIT' - Pause (milliseconds) after transmit and before "
"receiving answer, some devices need more time (e.g., USB-to-serial "
"converters)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:677
msgid ""
"'PAUSE INTER-FRAME' - Pause (milliseconds) after receiving answer from "
"slave.  This sets the duty cycle of requests (it's a pause for EACH request)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:678
msgid ""
"'REQUEST TIMEOUT LENGTH' - Length (milliseconds) of time before we decide "
"that the slave didn't answer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:679
msgid ""
"'MODBUS ELEMENT OFFSET' - used to offset the element numbers by 1 (for "
"manufacturers numbering differences)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:680
msgid ""
"'DEBUG LEVEL' - Set this to 0-3 (0 to stop printing debug info besides no-"
"response errors)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:681
msgid ""
"'READ COILS/INPUTS MAP TO' - Select what variables that read coils/inputs "
"will update. (B or Q)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:682
msgid ""
"'WRITE COILS MAP TO' - Select what variables that write coils will updated "
"from (B,Q,or I)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:683
msgid ""
"'READ REGISTERS/HOLDING' - Select what variables that read registers will "
"update (W or QW)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:684
msgid ""
"'WRITE REGISTERS MAP TO' - Select what variables that read registers will "
"updated from (W, QW, or IW)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:686
msgid ""
"'SLAVE ADDRESS' - For serial the slaves ID number usually settable on the "
"slave device (usually 1-256).  For IP the slave IP address plus optionally "
"the port number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:687
msgid ""
"'TYPE ACCESS' - This selects the MODBUS function code to send to the slave "
"(eg what type of request)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:688
msgid ""
"'COILS / INPUTS' - Inputs and Coils (bits) are read from/written to I, B, or "
"Q variables (user selects)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:689
msgid ""
"'REGISTERS (WORDS)' - Registers (Words/Numbers) map to IW, W, or QW "
"variables (user selects)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:690
msgid ""
"'1st MODBUS ELEMENT' - The address (or register number) of the first element "
"in a group (remember to set MODBUS ELEMENT OFFSET properly)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:691
msgid "'NUMBER OF ELEMENTS' - The number of elements in this group."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:692
msgid "'LOGIC' - You can invert the logic here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:693
msgid ""
"'1st%I%Q IQ WQ MAPPED' - This is the starting number of %B, %I, %Q, %W, %IW, "
"or %QW variables that are mapped onto/from the modbus element group "
"(starting at the first modbus element number)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:695
msgid ""
"In the example above: Port number - for my computer /dev/ttyS0 was my serial "
"port."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:697
msgid "The serial speed is set to 9600 baud."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:699
msgid ""
"Slave address is set to 12 (on my VFD I can set this from 1-31, meaning I "
"can talk to 31 VFDs maximum on one system)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:702
msgid ""
"The first line is set up for 8 input bits starting at the first register "
"number (register 1).  So register numbers 1-8 are mapped onto "
"ClassicLadder's %B variables starting at %B1 and ending at %B8."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:704
msgid ""
"The second line is set for 2 output bits starting at the ninth register "
"number (register 9) so register numbers 9-10 are mapped onto ClassicLadder's "
"%Q variables starting at %Q9 ending at %Q10."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:707
msgid ""
"The third line is set to write 2 registers (16 bits each) starting at the "
"0^th^ register number (register 0), so register numbers 0-1 are mapped onto "
"ClassicLadder's %W variables starting at %W0 ending at %W1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:710
msgid ""
"It's easy to make an off-by-one error as sometimes the modbus elements are "
"referenced starting at one rather then 0 (actually by the standard that is "
"the way it's supposed to be!).  You can use the modbus element offset radio "
"button to help with this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:712
msgid ""
"The documents for your modbus slave device will tell you how the registers "
"are set up- there is no standard way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:714
msgid ""
"The SERIAL PORT, PORT SPEED, PAUSE, and DEBUG level are editable for changes "
"(when you close the config window values are applied, though Radio buttons "
"apply immediately)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:717
msgid ""
"To use the echo function select the echo function and add the slave number "
"you wish to test.  You don't need to specify any variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:720
msgid ""
"The number 257 will be sent to the slave number you specified and the slave "
"should send it back.  You will need to have ClassicLadder running in a "
"terminal to see the message."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:721
#, no-wrap
msgid "MODBUS Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:724
msgid "Serial:"
msgstr "სერიული:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:726
msgid "ClassicLadder uses RTU protocol (not ASCII)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:727
msgid "8 data bits, No parity is used, and 1 stop bit is also known as 8-N-1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:729
msgid ""
"Baud rate must be the same for slave and master.  ClassicLadder can only "
"have one baud rate so all the slaves must be set to the same rate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:730
msgid "Pause inter frame is the time to pause after receiving an answer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:731
msgid ""
"MODBUS_TIME_AFTER_TRANSMIT is the length of pause after sending a request "
"and before receiving an answer (this apparently helps with USB converters "
"which are slow)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:732
#, no-wrap
msgid "MODBUS Info"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:735
msgid ""
"ClassicLadder can use distributed inputs/outputs on modules using the Modbus "
"protocol (\"master\": polling slaves)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:736
msgid "The slaves and theirs I/O can be configured in the config window."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:737
msgid ""
"2 exclusive modes are available : ethernet using Modbus/TCP and serial using "
"Modbus/RTU."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:738
msgid "No parity is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:739
msgid "If no port name for serial is set, TCP/IP mode will be used..."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:740
msgid "The slave address is the slave address (Modbus/RTU) or the IP address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:741
msgid ""
"The IP address can be followed per the port number to use (xx.xx.xx.xx:pppp) "
"else the port 9502 will be used per default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:742
msgid ""
"2 products have been used for tests: a Modbus/TCP one (Adam-6051, https://"
"www.advantech.com) and a serial Modbus/RTU one (https://www.ipac.ws)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:743
msgid "See examples: adam-6051 and modbus_rtu_serial."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:744
msgid ""
"Web links: https://www.modbus.org and this interesting one: https://"
"www.iatips.com/modbus.html"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:745
msgid "MODBUS TCP SERVER INCLUDED"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:746
msgid ""
"ClassicLadder has a Modbus/TCP server integrated. Default port is 9502.  "
"(the previous standard 502 requires that the application must be launched "
"with root privileges)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:747
msgid ""
"List of Modbus functions code supported are: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 15 and 16."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:748
msgid ""
"Modbus bits and words correspondence table is actually not parametric and "
"correspond directly to the %B and %W variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:750
msgid "More information on modbus protocol is available on the internet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:752
msgid "https://www.modbus.org/[https://www.modbus.org/]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:753
#, no-wrap
msgid "Communication Errors"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:758
msgid ""
"If there is a communication error, a warning window will pop up (if the GUI "
"is running) and %E0 will be true.  Modbus will continue to try to "
"communicate. The %E0 could be used to make a decision based on the error.  A "
"timer could be used to stop the machine if timed out, etc."
msgstr ""

