msgstr "საერთო პარამეტრები"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:10
msgid ""
"*elbpcom* [**--ip=**_IP_] [**--port=**_PORT_] [**--timeout=**_TIMEOUT_] [**--"
"space=**_MEMSPACE_] [**--size=**_TRANSFER_SIZE_]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reading data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:11
msgid ""
"*elbpcom* [_common options_] [*--info*] **--address=**_ADDRESS_ **--"
"read=**_LENGTH_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:12
msgid ""
"*elbpcom* [_common options_] **--address=**_ADDRESS_ **--write=**_HEXDATA_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read and decode memory space info area"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:13
msgid "*elbpcom* [**--space=**_MEMSPACE_] *--read-info*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sending arbitrary packets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:14
msgid "*elbpcom* [_common options_] _HEXDATA_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Read or write data from a Mesa ethernet card that uses the LBP16 protocol, "
"such as the 7I80. This can be useful for performing certain low-level tasks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:24
msgid ""
"For more information about the meaning of each address space, see the card "
"documentation.  Incorrect use of this utility can have negative effects such "
"as changing the board's IP address or even corrupting the FPGA bitfile in "
"the EEPROM.  For some tasks, such as updating FPGA bitfiles and setting IP "
"addresses, *mesaflash*(1) is a more appropriate tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:26
msgid "If not specified, the default values are"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:28
msgid ""
"**--ip=**_192.168.1.121_ **--port=**_27181_ **--timeout=**_.2_ **--"
"space=**_0_ **--size=**_0_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:31
msgid ""
"If the **--size** argument _TRANSFER_SIZE_ is 0, elbpcom will look up the "
"preferred transfer size of the space in the space's info area."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:33
msgid ""
"This example demonstrates reading the HOSTMOT2 identifying string from the "
"IDROM in space 0:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ elbpcom --address 0x104 --read 8\n"
"> 82420401\n"
"< 484f53544d4f5432\n"
"      HOSTMOT2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:44
msgid ""
"First the request is shown in hex. Then the response (if any) is shown in "
"hex.  Finally, the response is shown in ASCII, with \".\" replacing any non-"
"ASCII characters.  This is similar to the following invocations of mesaflash:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ ./mesaflash  --device 7i80 --rpo 0x104\n"
"54534F48\n"
"$ ./mesaflash  --device 7i80 --rpo 0x108\n"
"32544F4D\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:53
msgid "Notice its different treatment of byte order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:57
msgid ""
"mesaflash(1), hostmot2(9), hm2_eth(9), https://www.mesanet.com[Mesa's "
"documentation for the Anything I/O boards]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "gladevcp(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:7
msgid ""
"gladevcp - Virtual Control Panel for LinuxCNC based on Glade, Gtk and HAL "
"widgets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:11
msgid ""
"*gladevcp* [*-g* _WxH+X+Y_] [*-c* _component-name_] [*-u* _handler_] [*-U* "
"_useroption_] [*-H* _HAL-file_] [*-d*] _myfile.ui_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:14 src/man/man1/pyvcp.1.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-g* _WxH+X+Y_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:18
msgid ""
"This sets the initial geometry of the root window. Use 'WxH' for just size, "
"'+X+Y' for just position, or 'WxH+X+Y' for both. Size / position use pixel "
"units. Position is referenced from top left."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:18 src/man/man1/pyvcp.1.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-c* _component-name_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:21
msgid ""
"Use _component-name_ as the HAL component name. If the component name is not "
"specified, the basename of the UI file is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-u* _handler_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Instructs GladeVCP to inspect the Python script _handler_ for event "
"handlers, and connect them to signals in the UI file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-U* _useroption_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:27
msgid ""
"GladeVCP collects all _useroption_ strings and passes them to the handler "
"init() method as a list of strings without further inspection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-x* _XID_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:30
msgid ""
"Reparent GladeVCP into an existing window _XID_ instead of creating a new "
"top level window."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-H* _halfile_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:33
msgid ""
"GladeVCP runs _HAL file_ - a list of HAL commands - by executing _halcmd -c "
"filename_ after the HAL component is finalized."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:33 src/man/man1/qtvcp.1.adoc:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-d*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:35
msgid "enable debug output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-R* _gtkrcfile_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:37
msgid "explicitly load a gtkrc file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-t* _THEME_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:40
msgid ""
"set gtk theme. Default is the _system_ theme.  Different panels can have "
"different themes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-m* _MAXIMUM_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:44
msgid ""
"force panel window to maximize. Together with the _-g geometry_ option one "
"can move the panel to a second monitor and force it to use all of the screen"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:44 src/man/man1/halcmd.1.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-R*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:48
msgid ""
"explicitly deactivate workaround for a GTK bug which makes matches of widget "
"and widget_class matches in GTK theme and gtkrc files fail.  Normally not "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/gladevcp.1.adoc:52
msgid ""
"_GladeVCP_ in the LinuxCNC documentation for a description of GladeVCP's "
"capabilities and the associated HAL widget set, along with examples."
msgstr ""

