#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "halstreamer(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:6
msgid "halstreamer - stream file data into HAL in real-time"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:11
msgid "*halstreamer* [_options_]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:18
msgid ""
"The HAL component *streamer*(9) and the program *halstreamer* are used "
"together to stream data from a file into the HAL in real-time.  In real-"
"time, *streamer* exports HAL pins and creates a FIFO (first in, first out "
"queue) in shared memory.  The non-realtime program *halstreamer* copies data "
"from stdin into the FIFO, so that *streamer* can write it to the HAL pins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:25
msgid ""
"Instructs *halstreamer* to write to FIFO _CHAN_.  FIFOs are numbered from "
"zero, and the default value is zero, so this option is not needed unless "
"multiple FIFOs have been created."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:28
msgid "Instructs *halsampler* to read from _FILENAME_ instead of from stdin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:33
msgid ""
"A FIFO must first be created by loading *streamer*(9) with *halcmd loadrt* "
"or a *loadrt* command in a HAL file.  Then *halstreamer* can be invoked to "
"begin writing data into the FIFO."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:37
msgid ""
"Data is read from stdin, and is almost always either redirected from a file "
"or piped from some other program, since keyboard input would be unable to "
"keep up with even slow streaming rates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:44
msgid ""
"Each line of input must match the pins that are attached to the FIFO, for "
"example, if the *streamer* config string was \"ffbs\" then each line of "
"input must consist of two floats, a bit, and a signed integer, in that order "
"and separated by whitespace.  Floats must be formatted as required by "
"*strtod*(3), signed and unsigned integers must be formatted as required by "
"*strtol*(3) and *strtoul*(3), and bits must be either '0' or '1'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:46
msgid ""
"Input lines that begin with '#' will be treated as comments and silently "
"skipped."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:50
msgid ""
"*halstreamer* transfers data to the FIFO as fast as possible until the FIFO "
"is full, then it retries at regular intervals, until it is either killed or "
"reads EOF from stdin.  Data can be redirected from a file or piped from some "
"other program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:54
msgid ""
"The FIFO size should be chosen to ride through any momentary disruptions in "
"the flow of data, such as disk seeks.  If the FIFO is big enough, "
"*halstreamer* can be restarted with the same or a new file before the FIFO "
"empties, resulting in a continuous stream of data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:57
msgid ""
"The data format for *halstreamer* input is the same as for *halsampler*(1) "
"output, so 'waveforms' captured with *halsampler* can be replayed using "
"*halstreamer*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:63
msgid ""
"If a problem is encountered during initialization, *halstreamer* prints a "
"message to stderr and returns failure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:67
msgid ""
"If a badly formatted line is encountered while writing to the FIFO, it "
"prints a message to stderr, skips the line, and continues (this behavior may "
"be revised in the future)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:70
msgid ""
"Upon reading EOF from the input, it returns success.  If it is terminated "
"before the input ends, it returns failure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halstreamer.1.adoc:75
msgid "streamer(9), sampler(9), halsampler(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "haltcl(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:6
msgid ""
"haltcl - manipulate the LinuxCNC HAL from the command line using a Tcl "
"interpreter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:10
msgid "*haltcl* [*-i* _<INI file>_] [_filename_]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Tcl is a scripting language from the 90s that is very easy to extend. "
"*Haltcl* extends the regular Tcl interpreter with a set of commands to "
"interact with HAL, i.e. it allows to manipulate the HAL (Hardware "
"Abstraction Layer) from the command line using a Tcl interpreter. *haltcl* "
"can optionally read commands from a file (filename), allowing complex HAL "
"configurations to be set up with a single command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:25
msgid ""
"If specified, the INI file is read and used to create Tcl global variable "
"arrays.  An array is created for each SECTION of the INI file with elements "
"for each ITEM in the section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:27
msgid "For example, if the INI file contains:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[SECTION_A]\n"
"ITEM_1 = 1\n"
"[SECTION_A]\n"
"ITEM_2 = 2\n"
"[SECTION_B]\n"
"ITEM_1 = 10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The corresponding Tcl variables are:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SECTION_A(ITEM_1) = 1\n"
"SECTION_A(ITEM_2) = 2\n"
"SECTION_B(ITEM_1) = 10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-ini* _<INI file>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:47
msgid "Declining usage, use *-i* _<INI file>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "*filename*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:51
msgid ""
"If specified, the Tcl commands of *filename* are executed. If no filename is "
"specified, haltcl opens an interactive session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:56
msgid ""
"The executable *haltcl* includes the commands of a Tcl interpreter augmented "
"with commands for the hal language as described for *halcmd*(1).  The "
"augmented commands can be listed with the command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:58
msgid "`haltcl: hal --commands`+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:60
msgid ""
"`addf alias delf delsig getp gets ptype stype help linkpp linkps linksp list "
"loadrt loadusr lock net newsig save setexact_for_test_suite_only setp sets "
"show source start status stop unalias unlinkp unload unloadrt unloadusr "
"unlock waitusr`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:64
msgid ""
"Two of the augmented commands, 'list' and 'gets', require special treatment "
"to avoid conflict with Tcl built-in commands having the same names.  To use "
"these commands, precede them with the keyword 'hal':"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"hal list\n"
"hal gets\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/haltcl.1.adoc:82
msgid "halcmd(1), halrun(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "halui(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc:6
msgid "halui - observe HAL pins and command LinuxCNC through NML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc:10
msgid "*halui* [*-ini* _<path-to-INI>_]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc:15
msgid ""
"The program *halui* is used to build a User Interface using hardware knobs "
"and switches.  It exports a big number of pins, and acts accordingly when "
"these change."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-ini* _filename_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc:22
msgid ""
"Use the _filename_ as the configuration file. Note: halui must find the nml "
"file specified in the INI, usually that file is in the same folder as the "
"INI, so it makes sense to run halui from that folder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc:28
msgid ""
"When run, *halui* will export a large number of pins. A user can connect "
"those to his physical knobs & switches & leds, and when a change is noticed "
"halui triggers an appropriate event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc:31
msgid ""
"Caveat, *halui* expects the signals to be debounced, so if needed (bad knob "
"contact) connect the physical button to a HAL debounce filter first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc:36
