#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/io.1.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*[EMCIO]*\n"
"*EMCIO = io*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/io.1.adoc:17
msgid ""
"I/O control handles I/O tasks like coolant, toolchange and E-stop.  The "
"signals are turned on and off in non-realtime with G-code or in the case of "
"E-stop in HAL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/io.1.adoc:20
msgid ""
"The following pins are created by the non-realtime IO controller, usually "
"found in `$LINUXCNC_HOME/bin/io`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/io.1.adoc:24
msgid ""
"iocontrol is a non-realtime process - if you have strict timing requirements "
"or simply need more I/O, consider using the realtime synchronized I/O "
"provided by *motion*(9) instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/io.1.adoc:27
msgid ""
"The INI file is searched for in the directory from which halcmd was run, "
"unless an absolute path is specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/io.1.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "*iocontrol.0.coolant-flood* (Bit, Out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
