msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:300
msgid ""
"With set, jog the indicated joint or axis by increment _<incr>_ at the "
"_<speed>_; sign of speed is direction. If TELEOP_ENABLE is OFF, use "
"__joint_number__.  If TELEOP_ENABLE is ON, use __axis_letter__."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:301
#, no-wrap
msgid "*feed_override* _<percent>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:304
msgid ""
"With get, any parameter is ignored and the current feed override is returned "
"(as a percentage of commanded feed).  With set, sets the feed override as "
"specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:305
#, no-wrap
msgid "*spindle_override* _<percent>_ {__<spindle>__}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:309
msgid ""
"With get, any parameter is ignored and the current spindle override is "
"returned (as a percentage of commanded speed).  With set, sets the spindle "
"override as specified.  If _spindle_ is omitted, spindle 0 is selected. If "
"-1, all spindles are selected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:310
#, no-wrap
msgid "*abs_cmd_pos* [{0|1|...}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:313
msgid ""
"With get, returns the specified axis' commanded position in absolute "
"coordinates.  If no axis is specified, returns all axes' commanded absolute "
"position."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:314
#, no-wrap
msgid "*abs_act_pos* [{0|1|...}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:317
msgid ""
"With get, returns the specified axis' actual position in absolute "
"coordinates.  If no axis is specified, returns all axes' actual absolute "
"position."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:318
#, no-wrap
msgid "*rel_cmd_pos* [{0|1|...}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:321
msgid ""
"With get, returns the specified axis' commanded position in relative "
"coordinates, including tool length offset.  If no axis is specified, returns "
"all axes' commanded relative position."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:322
#, no-wrap
msgid "*rel_act_pos* [{0|1|...}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:325
msgid ""
"With get, returns the specified axis' actual position in relative "
"coordinates, including tool length offset.  If no axis is specified, returns "
"all axes' actual relative position."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:326
#, no-wrap
msgid "*joint_pos* [{0|1|...}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:329
msgid ""
"With get, returns the specified joint's actual position in absolute "
"coordinates, excluding tool length offset.  If no joint is specified, "
"returns all joints' actual absolute position."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:330
#, no-wrap
msgid "*pos_offset [{X|Y|Z|R|P|W}]*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:332
msgid ""
"With get, returns the position offset associated with the world coordinate "
