#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "shuttle(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:7
msgid ""
"shuttle - control HAL pins with the ShuttleXpress, ShuttlePRO, and "
"ShuttlePRO2 device made by Contour Design"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:11
msgid "*loadusr shuttle* [_DEVICE_ ...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:30 src/man/man1/xhc-hb04.1.adoc:30
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "UDEV"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:34
msgid ""
"The shuttle driver needs read permission to the Shuttle devices' /dev/"
"hidraw* device files.  This can be accomplished by adding a file */etc/udev/"
"rules.d/99-shuttle.rules*, with the following contents:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SUBSYSTEM==\"hidraw\", ATTRS\\{idVendor}==\"0b33\",\n"
"ATTRS\\{idProduct}==\"0020\", MODE=\"0444\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:41
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SUBSYSTEM==\"hidraw\", ATTRS\\{idVendor}==\"05f3\",\n"
"ATTRS\\{idProduct}==\"0240\", MODE=\"0444\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SUBSYSTEM==\"hidraw\", ATTRS\\{idVendor}==\"0b33\",\n"
"ATTRS\\{idProduct}==\"0030\", MODE=\"0444\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:49
msgid ""
"The LinuxCNC Debian package installs an appropriate udev file automatically, "
"but if you are building LinuxCNC from source and are not using the Debian "
"packaging, you'll need to install this file by hand.  If you install the "
"file by hand you'll need to tell udev to reload its rules files by running "
"`udevadm control --reload-rules`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "A warning about the Jog Wheel"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:56
msgid ""
"The Shuttle devices have an internal 8-bit counter for the current jog-wheel "
"position.  The shuttle driver can not know this value until the Shuttle "
"device sends its first event.  When the first event comes into the driver, "
"the driver uses the device's reported jog-wheel position to initialize "
"counts to 0.  This means that if the first event is generated by a jog-wheel "
"move, that first move will be lost."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:64
msgid ""
"All HAL pin names are prefixed with `shuttle` followed by the index of the "
"device (the order in which the driver found them), for example `shuttle.0` "
"or `huttle.2`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "_(prefix).button-(number)_ (bit out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "_(prefix).button-(number)-not_ (bit out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:69
msgid ""
"The momentary buttons. \"(number)\" identifies which button corresponds to "
"the HAL pin.  The \"button-(number)\" pins are True when the button is "
"pushed, the \"button-(number)-not\" pins are True when the button is not "
"pushed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "_(prefix).counts_ (s32 out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "_(prefix).spring-wheel-s32_ (s32 out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "_(prefix).spring-wheel-f_ (float out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/shuttle.1.adoc:77
msgid ""
"The current deflection of the spring-wheel (the outer wheel).  It's 0.0 at "
"rest, -1.0 at the counter-clockwise extreme, and +1.0 at the clockwise "
"extreme.  (The Shuttle devices report the spring-wheel position as an "
"integer from -7 to +7, so this pin reports only 15 discrete values in its "
"range.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "sim_pin(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:6
msgid "sim_pin - GUI for displaying and setting one or more HAL inputs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:10
msgid "**sim_pin* _[Options]_ _name1_ [_name2_ [_name3_ ...]]*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:12
msgid "_Options_: *--help* (shows help text) *--title title_string*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:15
msgid ""
"For bit items, the name may include a /mode= specifier: _namei_*/"
"mode=*[*pulse* | *toggle* | *hold*] (default is toggle)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:20
msgid ""
"HAL boolean items (bit) and numerical items (u32, s32, float) are supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:22
msgid "If the named input is a numerical type, the GUI displays:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Entry* Entry widget for value or a valid Tcl expression.\n"
"*Set* Pushbutton to set new value from Entry (or use <RETURN>).\n"
"*Reset* Pushbutton to reset to the value present on initiation If the input is a *bit* type, the GUI shows a single pushbutton that is controlled by radio-button selectors:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"mode=**pulse** Pulse input to 1 for each pushbutton press.\n"
"mode=**toggle** Toggle input for each pushbutton press.\n"
"mode=**hold** Set input to 1 while pushbutton pressed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:35
msgid ""
"If the bit item mode begins with an uppercase letter, the radio buttons for "
"selecting other modes are not shown"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:39
msgid "LinuxCNC or a standalone HAL application must be running"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:42
msgid ""
"A named item can specify a *pin*, *param*, or *signal*. The named item must "
"be writable:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*pin IN or I/O* (and not connected to a signal with a writer)\n"
"*param RW*\n"
"*signal connected to a writable pin*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:51
msgid ""
"*sim_pin* can be used interactively from a shell command line or started "
"automatically from a configuration INI file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:55
msgid "Example for INI file usage:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:59
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[APPLICATIONS] DELAY = 5 APP = *sim_pin* \\\n"
"halui.machine.off/mode=pulse \\\n"
"ini.traj_arc_blend_enable \\\n"
"motion-command-handler-tmax"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
