#, no-wrap
msgid "hal_param_alias(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_param_alias.3.adoc:6
msgid "hal_param_alias - create an alternate name for a param"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_param_alias.3.adoc:10
msgid ""
"int *hal_param_alias*(const char **original_name*, const char **alias*);"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man3/hal_param_alias.3.adoc:13 src/man/man3/hal_pin_alias.3.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "original_name"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_param_alias.3.adoc:15
msgid "The original name of the param"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man3/hal_param_alias.3.adoc:15 src/man/man3/hal_pin_alias.3.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "alias"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_param_alias.3.adoc:17
msgid ""
"The alternate name that may be used to refer to the param, or NULL to remove "
"any alternate name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_param_alias.3.adoc:22
msgid ""
"A param may have two names: the original name (the one that was passed to a "
"*hal_param_new* function) and an alias."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_param_alias.3.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Usually, aliases are for the convenience of users and should be created and "
"destroyed via halcmd.  However, in some cases it is sensible to create "
"aliases directly in a component.  These cases include the case where a param "
"is renamed, to preserve compatibility with old versions."
msgstr ""

