#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "rtapi_mutex(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:6
msgid "rtapi_mutex - Mutex-related functions"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "#include <rtapi_mutex.h>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int rtapi_mutex_try(unsigned long* _mutex_);\n"
"int rtapi_mutex_get(unsigned long* _mutex_);\n"
"int rtapi_mutex_give(unsigned long* _mutex_);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "mutex"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:22
msgid "A pointer to the mutex."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:28
msgid ""
"*rtapi_mutex_try* makes a non-blocking attempt to get the mutex.  If the "
"mutex is available, it returns 0, and the mutex is no longer available.  "
"Otherwise, it returns a nonzero value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:30
msgid "*rtapi_mutex_get* blocks until the mutex is available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:32
msgid ""
"*rtapi_mutex_give* releases a mutex acquired by *rtapi_mutex_try* or "
"*rtapi_mutex_get*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:36
msgid ""
"*rtapi_mutex_give* and *rtapi_mutex_try* may be used from non-realtime, init/"
"cleanup, and realtime code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:38
msgid "*rtapi_mutex_get* may not be used from realtime code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:42
msgid ""
"*rtapi_mutex_try* returns 0 for if the mutex was claimed, and nonzero "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_mutex.3.adoc:43
msgid "*rtapi_mutex_get* and *rtapi_mutex_gif* have no return value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "rtapi_open_as_root(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:6
msgid "rtapi_open_as_root - Open a file with \"root\" privilege"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#include <rtapi.h>\n"
"int rtapi_open_as_root(const char *filename, int flags);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "filename"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:21
msgid ""
"The filename to open, as in *open(2)*.  Note that rtapi has no well-defined "
"\"current directory\", so this should be an absolute path, but this is not "
"enforced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "flags"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:25
msgid ""
"The open flags, as in *open(2)*.  Should never include bits that open or "
"create files (e.g., O_CREAT, O_APPEND, etc)  as this API is not intended for "
"creating or writing files, but this is not enforced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:32
msgid ""
"In \"uspace\" realtime, root privileges are dropped whenever possible.  This "
"API temporarily switches on root privileges to open a file, and switches "
"them off before returning. This can be useful for example when accessing "
"device nodes or memory-mapped I/O."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:35
msgid ""
"In the case of PCI devices on x86 and x86-64 systems, prefer the linux-style "
"PCI interfaces provided in *<rtapi_pci.h>*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:40
msgid ""
"In case of success, the nonnegative file descriptor opened.  If the caller "
"does not close it, it remains open until rtapi_app exits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:42
msgid "In case of failure, a negative errno value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:46
msgid "Call only from realtime initcode in \"uspace\" realtime."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_open_as_root.3.adoc:49
msgid "open(2), rtapi_pci(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_outb.3.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "rtapi_outb(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_outb.3.adoc:8
msgid "rtapi_outb, rtapi_inb - Perform hardware I/O"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_outb.3.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"void rtapi_outb(unsigned char _byte_, unsigned int _port_);\n"
"unsigned char rtapi_inb(unsigned int _port_);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_outb.3.adoc:21
msgid "The address of the I/O port"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_outb.3.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "byte"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_outb.3.adoc:23
msgid "The byte to be written to the port"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_outb.3.adoc:27
msgid ""
"*rtapi_outb* writes a byte to a hardware I/O port. *rtapi_inb* reads a byte "
"from a hardware I/O port."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_outb.3.adoc:36
msgid "*rtapi_inb* returns the byte read from the given I/O port"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_outb.3.adoc:41
msgid ""
"The I/O address should be within a region previously allocated by "
"*rtapi_request_region*.  Otherwise, another real-time module or the Linux "
"kernel might attempt to access the I/O region at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_outb.3.adoc:44 src/man/man3/rtapi_region.3.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "rtapi_region(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "rtapi_parport(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:6
msgid "rtapi_parport - portable access to PC-style parallel ports"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "#include \"rtapi_parport.h\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int rtapi_parport_get(const char* _module_name_, rtapi_parport_t* _port_,\n"
"                      short _base_, unsigned short _base_hi_,\n"
"                      int _modes_);\n"
"void rtapi_parport_release(rtapi_parport_t* _port_);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "module_name"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:23
msgid ""
"By convention, the name of the RTAPI module or HAL component using the "
"parport."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:25
msgid "A pointer to a rtapi_parport_t structure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:28
msgid ""
"The base address of the port (if port >= 16) or the linux port number of the "
"port (if port < 16)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:31
msgid ""
"The \"high\" address of the port (location of the ECP registers), 0 to use a "
"probed high address, or -1 to disable the high address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:37
msgid ""
"Advise the driver of the desired port modes, from <linux/parport.h>.  If a "
"linux-detected port does not provide the requested modes, a warning is "
"printed with rtapi_print_msg. This does not make the port request fail, "
"because unfortunately, many systems that have working EPP parports are not "
"detected as such by Linux."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:45
msgid ""
"*rtapi_parport_get* allocates a parallel port for exclusive use of the named "
"hal component. If successful, access the port with I/O calls such as "
"rtapi_inb at address based at the *base* or *base_hi* addresses. The port "
"must be released with *rtapi_parport_release* before the component exits "
"with *rtapi_exit*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:52
msgid ""
"If the port is a parallel port known to Linux, and Linux detected a high I/O "
"address, this value is used. Otherwise, if base+0x400 is not registered to "
"any device, it is used. Otherwise, no address is used. If no high address is "
"detected, port->base_hi is 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:63
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"typedef struct\n"
"{\n"
"    unsigned short base;\n"
"    unsigned short base_hi;\n"
"    .... // and further unspecified fields\n"
"} rtapi_parport_t;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:71
msgid ""
"*rtapi_parport_get* returns a HAL status code. On success, _port_ is filled "
"out with information about the allocated port.  On failure, the contents of "
"_port_ are undefined except that it is safe (but not required) to pass this "
"port to *rtapi_parport_release*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:73
msgid "*rtapi_parport_release* does not return a value. It always succeeds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_parport.3.adoc:76
msgid "In new code, prefer use of rtapi_parport to rtapi_parport."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_pci.3.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "rtapi_pci(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_pci.3.adoc:6
msgid "rtapi_pci - RTAPI wrappers for linux kernel functionality"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_pci.3.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
