#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "rtapi_print(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:8
msgid "rtapi_print, rtapi_print_msg - print diagnostic messages"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"void rtapi_print(const char* _fmt_, _..._)\n"
"void rtapi_print_msg(int level, const char* _fmt_, _..._)\n"
"typedef void(**rtapi_msg_handler_t*)(msg_level_t _level_, const char* _msg_);\n"
"void rtapi_set_msg_handler(rtapi_msg_handler_t _handler_);\n"
"rtapi_msg_handler_t rtapi_get_msg_handler(void);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:24
msgid ""
"A message level: One of *RTAPI_MSG_ERR*, *RTAPI_MSG_WARN*, *RTAPI_MSG_INFO*, "
"or *RTAPI_MSG_DBG*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "handler"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:27
msgid ""
"A function to call from *rtapi_print* or *rtapi_print_msg* to actually "
"output the message."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "fmt, ..."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:29
msgid "Other arguments are as for _rtapi_vsnprintf(3)_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:36
msgid ""
"*rtapi_print* and *rtapi_print_msg* work like the standard C printf "
"functions, except that a reduced set of formatting operations are "
"supported.  Notably, formatting long-long values is not supported, and "
"formatting floating-point values has different behavior than standard printf."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:42
msgid ""
"Depending on the RTOS, the default may be to print the message to stdout, "
"stderr, a kernel log, etc.  In RTAPI code, the action may be changed by a "
"call to *rtapi_set_msg_handler*.  A *NULL* argument to "
"*rtapi_set_msg_handler* restores the default handler.  "
"*rtapi_msg_get_handler* returns the current handler.  When the message came "
"from *rtapi_print*, _level_ is RTAPI_MSG_ALL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:45
msgid ""
"*rtapi_print_msg* works like rtapi_print but only prints if _level_ is less "
"than or equal to the current message level."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:51
msgid ""
"*rtapi_print* and *rtapi_print_msg* May be called from non-realtime, init/"
"cleanup, and realtime code.  *rtapi_get_msg_handler* and "
"*rtapi_set_msg_handler* may be called from realtime init/cleanup code.  A "
"message handler passed to *rtapi_set_msg_handler* may only call functions "
"that can be called from realtime code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_print.3.adoc:59
msgid "rtapi_set_msg_level(3), rtapi_get_msg_level(3), rtapi_vsnprintf(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "rtapi_prio(3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:8
msgid ""
"rtapi_prio, rtapi_prio_highest, rtapi_prio_lowest, rtapi_prio_next_higher, "
"rtapi_prio_next_lower - thread priority functions"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int rtapi_prio_highest();\n"
"int rtapi_prio_lowest();\n"
"int rtapi_prio_next_higher(int _prio_);\n"
"int rtapi_prio_next_lower(int _prio_);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:21 src/man/man3/rtapi_task_new.3.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "prio"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:23
msgid "A value returned by a prior *rtapi_prio_xxx* call"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:30
msgid ""
"The *rtapi_prio_xxxx* functions provide a portable way to set task priority. "
"The mapping of actual priority to priority number depends on the RTOS. "
"Priorities range from *rtapi_prio_lowest* to *rtapi_prio_highest*, "
"inclusive. To use this API, use one of two methods:"
msgstr ""

#. type: arabic
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:35
msgid ""
"Set your lowest priority task to *rtapi_prio_lowest*, and for each task of "
"the next lowest priority, set their priorities to "
"*rtapi_prio_next_higher*(previous)."
msgstr ""

#. type: arabic
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:38
msgid ""
"Set your highest priority task to *rtapi_prio_highest*, and for each task of "
"the next highest priority, set their priorities to "
"*rtapi_prio_next_lower*(previous)."
msgstr ""

#. type: arabic
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:41
msgid ""
"N.B.: A high priority task will preempt or interrupt a lower priority task.  "
"Linux is always the lowest priority!"
msgstr ""

#. type: arabic
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:45
msgid ""
"Call these functions only from within init/cleanup code, not from realtime "
"tasks."
msgstr ""

#. type: arabic
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:49
msgid "Returns an opaque real-time priority number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_prio.3.adoc:52 src/man/man3/rtapi_task_new.3.adoc:3
