#, no-wrap
msgid "classicladder(9)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:6
msgid "classicladder - realtime software plc based on ladder logic"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:10
msgid ""
"*loadrt classicladder_rt* [**numRungs=**_N_] [**numBits=**_N_] "
"[**numWords=**_N_] [**numTimers=**_N_] [**numMonostables=**_N_] "
"[**numCounters=**_N_] [**numPhysInputs=**_N_] [**numPhysOutputs=**_N_] "
"[**numArithmExpr=**_N_] [**numSections=**_N_] [**numSymbols=**_N_] "
"[**numS32in=**_N_] [**numS32out=**_N_] [**numFloatIn=**_N_] "
"[**numFloatOut=**_N_]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:12
msgid "*loadusr classicladder* _<file name>_ [**--nogui**]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:22
msgid ""
"This component consist of a realtime part and a non-realtime part. The non-"
"realtime part loads the programmable ladder description, while the realtime "
"part provides the pins. The file name of the configuration can be changed "
"using an argument to the non-realtime part. By default the non-realtime part "
"provides a graphical visualisation of the loaded ladder, which can be "
"disabled using the '--nogui' option to the non-realtime part."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:27
msgid ""
"These pins and parameters are created by the realtime *classicladder_rt* "
"module. Each period (minimum 1000000 ns), ClassicLadder reads the inputs, "
"evaluates the ladder logic defined in the GUI, and then writes the outputs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "**classicladder.0.in-**_NN_ IN bit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:32
msgid "These bit signal pins map to **%I**_NN_ variables in ClassicLadder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "**classicladder.0.out-**_NN_ OUT bit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:35
msgid ""
"These bit signal pins map to **%Q**_NN_ variables in ClassicLadder.  Output "
"from ClassicLadder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "**classicladder.0.s32in-**_NN_ IN s32"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:38
msgid ""
"Integer input from ClassicLadder.  These s32 signal pins map to **%IW**_NN_ "
"variables in ClassicLadder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "**classicladder.0.s32out-**_NN_ OUT s32"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:41
msgid ""
"Integer output from ClassicLadder.  These s32 signal pins map to **%QW**_NN_ "
"variables in ClassicLadder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "**classicladder.0.floatin-**_NN_ IN float"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:45
msgid ""
"Integer input from ClassicLadder.  These float signal pins map to "
"**%IF**_NN_ variables in ClassicLadder.  These are truncated to S32 values "
"internally, e.g. 7.5 will be 7."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "**classicladder.0.floatout-**_NN_ OUT float"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:48
msgid ""
"Float output from ClassicLadder.  These float signal pins map to **%QF**_NN_ "
"variables in ClassicLadder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "**classicladder.0.hide_gui** IN bit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:51
msgid ""
"This bit pin hides the ClassicLadder window, while still having the non-"
"realtime code run.  This is usually desirable when modbus is used, as modbus "
"requires the non-realtime code to run."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "*classicladder.0.refresh.time* RO s32"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:56
msgid "Tells you how long the last refresh took."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "*classicladder.0.refresh.tmax* RW s32"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:58
msgid "Tells you how long the longest refresh took."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "*classicladder.0.ladder-state* RO s32"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:60
msgid "Tells you if the program is running or not"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "*classicladder.0.refresh* FP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:67
msgid ""
"The rung update rate.  Add this to the servo thread.  You can added it to a "
"faster thread but it.  Will update no faster than once every 1 millisecond "
"(1000000 ns)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:71
msgid ""
"See https://wiki.linuxcnc.org/cgi-bin/wiki.pl?ClassicLadder_Ver_7.124 for "
"the latest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/classicladder.9.adoc:76
msgid ""
"_ClassicLadder_ chapters in the LinuxCNC documentation for a full "
"description of the *ClassicLadder* syntax and examples."
msgstr ""

