#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:166
msgid ""
"The serial number of the connected drive. This is also shown on the label on "
"the drive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:167
#, no-wrap
msgid "7I64"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:172
msgid ""
"The 7I64 is a 24-input 24-output IO card. 7I64 pins and parameters have "
"names like "
"\"hm2__<BoardType>__.__<BoardNum>__.7i64.__<PortNum>__.__<ChanNum>__.__<Pin>__\", "
"for example `hm2_5i23.0.7i64.1.3.output-01`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:175
#, no-wrap
msgid "7i64.0.0.output-__NN__ (bit, in)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:180
msgid ""
"Writing a 1 or TRUE to this pin will enable output driver _NN_.  Note that "
"the outputs are drivers (switches) rather than voltage outputs.  The LED "
"adjacent to the connector on the board shows the status.  The output can be "
"inverted by setting a parameter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:181
#, no-wrap
msgid "7i64.0.0.input-__NN__ (bit, out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:185
msgid ""
"The value of input _NN_.  Note that the inputs are isolated and both pins of "
"each input must be connected, typically to signal and the ground of the "
"signal.  (This need not be the ground of the board.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:186
#, no-wrap
msgid "7i64.0.0.input-__NN__-not (bit, out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:187
msgid "An inverted copy of the corresponding input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "7i64.0.0.analog0 & 7i64.0.0.analog1 (float, out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:188
msgid "The two analogue inputs (0 to 3.3 V) on the board."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:191
#, no-wrap
msgid "7i64.0.0.output-__NN__-invert (bit, rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:193
msgid ""
"Setting this parameter to 1 / TRUE will invert the output value, such that "
"writing 0 to `.gpio.NN.out` will enable the output and vice-versa."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:194
#, no-wrap
msgid "7I76"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:201
msgid ""
"The 7I76 is not really a smart-serial device.  It serves as a breakout for a "
"number of other Hostmot2 functions.  There are connections for 5 step "
"generators (for which see the main hostmot2 manpage).  The stepgen pins are "
"associated with the 5I25 (`hm2_5i25.0.stepgen.00`....), whereas the smart-"
"serial pins are associated with the 7I76 (`hm2_5i25.0.7i76.0.0.output-00`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:204
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.analog__N__ (modes 1 and 2 only) (float out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:205 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:317
msgid "Analogue input values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:205
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.fieldvoltage (mode 2 only) (float out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:206 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:318
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:344
msgid "Field voltage monitoring pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:206
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.spindir (bit in)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:207 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:248
msgid ""
"This pin provides a means to drive the spindle VFD direction terminals on "
"the 7I76 board."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:207
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.spinena (bit in)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:208 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:249
msgid "This pin drives the spindle-enable terminals on the 7I76 board."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:208
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.spinout (float in)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:210
msgid ""
"This controls the analogue output of the 7I76.  This is intended as a speed "
"control signal for a VFD."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:210
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.output-__NN__ (bit out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:212
msgid ""
"(_NN_ = 0 to 15). 16 digital outputs.  The sense of the signal can be set "
"via a parameter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:212
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.input-__NN__ (bit out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:213 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:245
msgid "(_NN_ = 0 to 31) 32 digital inputs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:213
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.input-__NN__-not (bit in)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:215
msgid ""
"(_NN_ = 0 to 31) An inverted copy of the inputs provided for convenience.  "
"The two complementary pins may be connected to different signal nets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:218
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.nvbaudrate (u32 ro)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:219 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:291
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:324 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:354
msgid "Indicates the vbaud rate. This probably should not be altered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:219
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.nvunitnumber (u32 ro)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:221 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:292
msgid ""
"Indicates the serial number of the device and should match a sticker on the "
"card.  This can be useful for working out which card is which."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:221
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.nvwatchdogtimeout (u32 ro)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:224 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:293
msgid ""
"The sserial remote watchdog timeout.  This is separate from the Anything-IO "
"card timeout.  This is unlikely to need to be changed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:224
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.output-__NN__-invert (bit rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:225 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:256
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:294 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:353
msgid "Invert the sense of the corresponding output pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:225
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.spindir-invert (bit rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:226
msgid "Invert the senseof the spindle direction pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:226
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.spinena-invert (bit rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:227 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:258
msgid "Invert the sense of the spindle-enable pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:227
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.spinout-maxlim (float rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:228 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:259
msgid "The maximum speed request allowable"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:228
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.spinout-minlim (float rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:229 src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:260
msgid "The minimum speed request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:229
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.spinout-scalemax (float rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:233
msgid ""
"The spindle speed scaling.  This is the speed request which would correspond "
"to full-scale output from the spindle control pin.  For example with a 10 V "
"drive voltage and a 10000 RPM scalemax a value of 10,000 RPM on the spinout "
"pin would produce 10 V output.  However, if spinout-maxlim were set to 5000 "
"RPM then no voltage above 5 V would be output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:233
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i76.0.0.swrevision (u32 ro)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:235
msgid ""
"The onboard firmware revision number.  Utilities (man setsserial for "
"details) exist to update and change this firmware."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:236
#, no-wrap
msgid "7I77"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:241
msgid ""
"The 7I77 is an 6-axis servo control card. The analogue outputs are smart-"
"serial devices, but the encoders are conventional hostmot2 encoders and "
"further details of them may be found in the hostmot2 manpage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:244
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i77.0.0.input-__NN__ (bit out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:245
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i77.0.0.input-__NN__-not (bit in)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:246
msgid ""
"(_NN_ = 0 to 31) An inverted copy of the inputs provided for convenience. "
"The two complementary pins may be connected to different signal nets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:246
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i77.0.0.output-__NN__ (bit out)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:247
msgid ""
"(_NN_ = 0 to 15). 16 digital outputs. The sense of the signal can be set via "
"a parameter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:247
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i77.0.0.spindir (bit in)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:248
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i77.0.0.spinena (bit in)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:249
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i77.0.0.spinout (float in)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:250
msgid ""
"This controls the analog output of the 7I77. This is intended as a speed "
"control signal for a VFD."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:250
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i77.0.1.analogena (bit in)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:251
msgid "This pin drives the analog enable terminals on the 7I77 board."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:251
#, no-wrap
msgid ".7i77.0.1.analogout__N__ (float in)"
msgstr ""

