#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:38
msgid "B<blend>\\&.I<N> (requires a floating-point thread)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:43
msgid "B<blend>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<in1> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:45
msgid ""
"First input\\&. If select is equal to 1\\&.0, the output is equal to in1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:48
msgid "B<blend>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<in2> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:50
msgid ""
"Second input\\&. If select is equal to 0\\&.0, the output is equal to in2"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:53
msgid "B<blend>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<select> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:55
msgid ""
"Select input\\&. For values between 0\\&.0 and 1\\&.0, the output changes "
"linearly from in2 to in1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:58
msgid "B<blend>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<out> float out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:60
msgid "Output value\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:64
msgid "B<blend>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<open> bit rw"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/blend.9:66
msgid ""
"If true, select values outside the range 0\\&.0 to 1\\&.0 give values "
"outside the range in2 to in1\\&. If false, outputs are clamped to the the "
"range in2 to in1"
msgstr ""

#. type: TH
#: man/man9/carousel.9:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "CAROUSEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:32
msgid "carousel - Orient a toolchanger carousel using various encoding schemes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:35
msgid ""
"B<loadrt> B<carousel> B<pockets>=I<N>[,I<N>] B<encoding>=I<ssss>[,I<sss>] "
"B<num_sense>=I<N>[,I<N>] B<dir>=I<N>[,I<N>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:37
msgid "B<pockets> The number of pockets in each toolchanger"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:39
msgid ""
"Use up to 8 numbers separated by commas to create multiple carousel "
"components\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:42
msgid "B<encoding>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:53
msgid ""
"The position encoding\\&. One of gray, binary, bcd, index, edge, counts or "
"single\\&. Default = gray\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:56
msgid "B<num_sense>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:58
msgid "The number of position sense pins\\&. Default = 4\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:61
msgid "B<dir>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:63
msgid ""
"Set to 1 for unidirectional or 2 for bidirectional operation\\&. Default = "
"bidirectional"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:66
msgid "B<parity>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:68
msgid ""
"Set to 1 for odd parity, 0 for even parity checking\\&. Default = 0 (even)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:72
msgid ""
"This component is intended to help operate various types of carousel-type "
"toolchangers\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:74
msgid ""
"The component can be configured to operate with binary, binary-coded decimal "
"(BCD) or gray-coded position feedback (I<binary;, \\*(Aqbcd> and I<gray> "
"modes) It can alternatively work with an individual sensor for each tool "
"position (I<single> mode) or with a sensor at each tool position and a "
"separate index (I<index> mode)\\&. Systems using a stepper motor or "
"quadrature encoder are also supported (I<counts> mode)\\&. B<edge> is a "
"special case of index mode for tool changers with pockets on both the rising "
"and falling edges of the position sensor\\&. (Seen on at least one Denford "
"Orac\\&.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:76
msgid ""
"Both unidirectional and bidirectional systems are supported and those that "
"reverse against a stop when in position\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:78
msgid ""
"The number of carousel component instances created depends on the number of "
"entries in the I<pockets> modparam\\&. For example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:80
msgid ""
"B<B loadrt carousel pockets=10,10,8>. Would create 3 carousel instances with "
"10, 10 and 8 pockets\\&. The other parameters are optional\\&. If absent "
"then defaults will be used\\&. Any missing entry will assume the previous "
"value\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:82
msgid ""
"When the enable pin is set to true the component will immediately set the "
"\"active\" pin to true and then (for a bidirectional instance) calculate the "
"shortest path to the requested pocket number\\&. The appropriate motor "
"direction output pins will then be set\\&. Bit outputs for forward and "
"reverse are provided as well as a three-state velocity output for driving a "
"DC motor PWM or a velocity-mode stepgen\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:84
msgid ""
"The component will monitor the carousel position and, when the correct "
"position is reached, set the motor-control pins to 0, set \"active\" to 0 "
"and set \"ready\" to 1\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:86
msgid ""
"In I<index>, I<edge> or I<counts\\(cqmode there is a need to find the "
"initial home position of the carousel\\&. The first time that the \"enable\" "
"pin is set; the carousel will rotate forwards searching for a home "
"signal\\&. In \\*(Aqindex> and I<edge> mode this is when both the index and "
"pulse inputs are true\\&. In I<counts> mode only the index input needs to be "
"set to set home\\&. Additionally in I<counts> mode the usual index-enable "
"logic of the encoder counters is supported\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:88
msgid ""
"With some carousel designs the carousel will not stop immediately\\&. To "
"allow for this set the B<align-dc> pin to a low velocity to be used for a "
"final latching move, and set the B<decel-time> to a suitable value\\&. Once "
"the decel-time has expired the carousel will, if it was moving forwards, "
"reverse back on to the position marker, off of the marker and then back on "
"to the FWD edge\\&. If moving in reverse it will continue off the marker and "
"then reverse slowly on to the FWD edge\\&. This alignment is only possible "
"with a motor-vel controlled bidirectional carousel, Other combinations will "
"be accepted but probably will not have the desired behaviour\\&. Some tuning "
"will be needed of align-dc and decel-time to achieve reliable operation\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:90
msgid ""
"In the unusual case that the index and pulse signals do not align it is "
"possible to use HAL logic to achieve the desired pin switching during "
"homing\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:92
msgid ""
"Setting \"enable\" low does not halt the homing move, so if homing on first "
"tool change is not needed then the enable pin can be toggled by an axis "
"homing pin or a script and the homing process will continue even if that "
"driving signal resets during the carousel homing move\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:94
msgid ""
"To operate the component with an encoder or stepgen use mode \"C\"\\&. The "
"B<scale> pin should be the number of steps or encoder counts between pocket "
"centres\\&. The B<width> pin can be used to stop the motor some distance "
"before the centre of the pocket to allow the motor time to decelerate\\&. In "
"mode \"C\" it is possible to use either the speed/direction control used in "
"other modes or to use direct position mode using the counts-target pin\\&. "
"The internal scaling of the encoder or stepgen should be set to 1\\&.0\\&. A "
"PID hal component will be needed for encoder applications whereas stepgen "
"configurations can use a stepgen in position control mode or in velocity "
"control mode with a PID\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:96
msgid ""
"For tool changers which lock the carousel against a stop the B<rev-pulse> "
"pin can be set to a non-zero value\\&. The motor-rev pin will then be set "
"for this many seconds at the completion of the tool search and at the same "
"time the reverse duty/cycle velocity value will be sent to the motor-vel "
"pin\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:99
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N> (requires a floating-point thread)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:104
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<pocket-number> s32 in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:106
msgid ""
"The pocket to move to when the \\&.enable pin goes high\\&. If the value "
"passed is higher than the number of pockets specified in the \"pockets\" "
"modparam then modulo arithmetic is used\\&. This is intended to allow the "
"use of multiple tools in the same holder, as is sometimes useful with "
"lathes\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:109
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<enable> bit in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:111
msgid ""
"Set this pin high to start movement\\&. Setting it low will stop movement"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:114
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<active> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:116
msgid "indicates that the component is active"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:119
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<ready> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:121
msgid "This pin goes high when the carousel is in-position"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:124
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<strobe> bit in (default: I<1>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:126
msgid ""
"Use this pin to indicate that the position feedback is valid\\&. Often "
"provided by binary encoders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:129
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<parity-> bit in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:131
msgid ""
"Some encoders supply a parity bit, if this is connected then the parity-"
"error output bit will indicate parity errors"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:134
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<sense->I<M> bit in (M=0\\&.\\&.personality)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:138
msgid ""
"Carousel position feedback pins\\&. In I<index> mode there will be only 2 "
"pins\\&. sense-0 is the index and sense-1 is the pocket sensor\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:141
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<rev-pulse> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:143
msgid ""
"The duration in seconds for which a ratchet changer (Boxford, Emco) should "
"pulse the reverse pin to lock the holder"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:146
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<fwd-dc> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:148
msgid "Velocity or duty cycle when forwards rotation is desired"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:151
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<rev-dc> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:153
msgid "Velocity or duty cycle when reverse rotation is desired"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:156
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<hold-dc> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:158
msgid "Duty cycle when carousel is in-position (to hold against stop)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:161
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<align-dc> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:163
msgid ""
"Use this pin to set the speed of a slower alignment move once the changer is "
"in position\\&. Such a system almost certainly needs decel-time setting too"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:166
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<decel-time> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:168
msgid ""
"Time to wait for carousel to stop before final alignment and position check"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:171
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<counts> s32 in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:175
msgid "Connect to the rawcounts of an encoder or a stepgen in I<counts> mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:178
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<scale> s32 in (default: I<100>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:180
msgid "The number of stepgen or encoder counts between successive pockets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:183
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<width> s32 in (default: I<10>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:185
msgid "How far each side of the exact scale to signal a new pocket"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:188
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<home-offset> s32 in (default: I<0>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:190
msgid "The offset (in counts) between the index and pocket 1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:193
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<index-enable> bit io"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:195
msgid "Used to home to an encoder index"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:198
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<jog-fwd> bit in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:200
msgid "Jog the carousel forwards one tool position"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:203
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<jog-rev> bit in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:205
msgid ""
"Jog the carousel in reverse (only if dir = 2)\\&. It is very important that "
"these pins should be debounced and should probably also be interlocked to "
"only operate when the machine is idle\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:208
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<motor-fwd> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:210
msgid "Indicates the motor should run forwards (bigger numbers)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:213
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<motor-rev> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:215
msgid "Indicates the motor should run reverse\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:218
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<parity-error> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:220
msgid "Indicates a parity error"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:223
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<current-position> s32 out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:225
msgid "This pin indicates the current position feedback"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:228
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<motor-vel> float out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:230
msgid "The duty-cycle or velocity to drive a DC motor or stepgen"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:233
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<homed> bit out (default: I<0>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:235
msgid "Shows that homing is complete\\&. Only used in index and edge modes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:238
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<unhome> bit in (default: I<0>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:240
msgid "Should only really be necessary for testing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:243
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<counts-target> float out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:245
msgid "Target position for a stepgen or external PID controller"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:249
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<state> s32 r (default: I<0>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:251
msgid "Current component state"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:254
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<homing> bit r (default: I<0>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:256
msgid "Shows that homing is in progress\\&. Only used for index mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:259
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<timer> float r"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:261
msgid "Shows the value of the internal timer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:264
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<motor-dir> s32 r"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:266
msgid "Internal tag for search direction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:269
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<counts-offset> s32 r"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:271
msgid "Internal offset of index pin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:274
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<debounce> u32 rw"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:276
msgid "How many thread cycles to wait for the position to stabilise"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:279
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<target> s32 r"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:281
msgid "Current target pocket, debug"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:284
msgid "B<carousel>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<base-counts> s32 r (default: I<0>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TH
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHARGE_PUMP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:32
msgid ""
"charge_pump - Create a square-wave for the \\*(Aqcharge pump\\*(Aq input of "
"some controller boards"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:35
msgid "B<loadrt charge_pump>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:38
msgid ""
"The I<Charge Pump> should be added to the base thread function\\&. When "
"enabled the output is on for one period and off for one period\\&. To "
"calculate the frequency of the output 1/(period time in seconds x 2) = "
"Hz\\&. For example if you have a base period of 100,000ns that is 0\\&.0001 "
"seconds and the formula would be 1/(0\\&.0001 x 2) = 5,000 Hz or 5 kHz\\&. "
"Two additional outputs are provided that run a factor of 2 and 4 slower for "
"hardware that requires a lower frequency\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:41
msgid "B<charge-pump>\\&.B<->"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:43
msgid "Toggle the output bit (if enabled)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:47
msgid "B<charge-pump>\\&.B<out> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:53
msgid ""
"Square wave if I<enable> is TRUE or unconnected, low if I<enable> is FALSE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:56
msgid "B<charge-pump>\\&.B<out-2> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:59
msgid "Square wave at half the frequency of I<out>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:62
msgid "B<charge-pump>\\&.B<out-4> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:65
msgid "Square wave at a quarter of the frequency of I<out>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:68
msgid "B<charge-pump>\\&.B<enable> bit in (default: I<TRUE>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/charge_pump.9:72
msgid "If FALSE, forces all I<out> pins to be low"
msgstr ""

#. type: TH
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLARKE2"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:32
msgid "clarke2 - Two input version of Clarke transform"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:35
msgid "B<loadrt clarke2> [B<count>=I<N>|B<names>=I<name1>[,I<name2>\\&...]]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:38
msgid ""
"The Clarke transform can be used to translate a vector quantity from a three "
"phase system (three components 120 degrees apart) to a two phase Cartesian "
"system\\&. B<clarke2> implements a special case of the Clarke transform, "
"which only needs two of the three input phases\\&. In a three wire three "
"phase system, the sum of the three phase currents or voltages must always be "
"zero\\&. As a result only two of the three are needed to completely define "
"the current or voltage\\&. B<clarke2> assumes that the sum is zero, so it "
"only uses phases A and B of the input\\&. Since the H (homopolar) output "
"will always be zero in this case, it is not generated\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:41
msgid "B<clarke2>\\&.I<N> (requires a floating-point thread)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:46
msgid "B<clarke2>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<a> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:50
msgid "B<clarke2>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<b> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:52
msgid "first two phases of three phase input"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:55
msgid "B<clarke2>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<x> float out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:59
msgid "B<clarke2>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<y> float out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/clarke2.9:61 man/man9/clarke3.9:65
