"with fewer than three sides), the current offset will be returned to zero "
"(respecting velocity and acceleration constraints)\\&. After correcting the "
"offending parameter, the B<enable-in> pin must be toggled to resume offset "
"computations\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: TH
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "ESTOP_LATCH"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:32
msgid "estop_latch - Software ESTOP latch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:35
msgid ""
"B<loadrt estop_latch> [B<count>=I<N>|B<names>=I<name1>[,I<name2>\\&...]]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:38
msgid ""
"This component can be used as a part of a simple software ESTOP chain\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:40
msgid "It has two states: \"OK\" and \"Faulted\"\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:42
msgid ""
"The initial state is \"Faulted\"\\&. When faulted, the B<out-ok> output is "
"false, the B<fault-out> output is true, and the B<watchdog> output is "
"unchanging\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:44
msgid ""
"The state changes from \"Faulted\" to \"OK\" when B<all> these conditions "
"are true:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:55
msgid "B<fault-in> is false"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:67
msgid "B<ok-in> is true"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:79
msgid "B<reset> changes from false to true"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:82
msgid ""
"When \"OK\", the B<out-ok> output is true, the B<fault-out> output is false, "
"and the B<watchdog> output is toggling\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:84
msgid ""
"The state changes from \"OK\" to \"Faulted\" when B<any> of the following "
"are true:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:95
msgid "B<fault-in> is true"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:107
msgid "B<ok-in> is false"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:110
msgid ""
"To facilitate using only a single fault source, B<ok-in> and B<fault-en> are "
"both set to the non-fault-causing value when no signal is connected\\&. For "
"estop-latch to ever be able to signal a fault, at least one of these inputs "
"must be connected\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:112
msgid ""
"Typically, an external fault or estop input is connected to B<fault-in>, "
"B<iocontrol\\&.0\\&.user-request-enable> is connected to B<reset>, and B<ok-"
"out> is connected to B<iocontrol\\&.0\\&.emc-enable-in>\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:114
msgid ""
"In more complex systems, it may be more appropriate to use classicladder to "
"manage the software portion of the estop chain\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:117
msgid "B<estop-latch>\\&.I<N>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:122
msgid "B<estop-latch>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<ok-in> bit in (default: I<true>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:126
msgid "B<estop-latch>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<fault-in> bit in (default: I<false>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:130
msgid "B<estop-latch>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<reset> bit in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:134
msgid "B<estop-latch>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<ok-out> bit out (default: I<false>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:138
msgid "B<estop-latch>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<fault-out> bit out (default: I<true>)"
msgstr ""

