#: man/man9/limit3.9:68
msgid "B<limit3>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<max-> float in (default: I<1e20>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/limit3.9:72
msgid "B<limit3>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<maxv> float in (default: I<1e20>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/limit3.9:76
msgid "B<limit3>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<maxa> float in (default: I<1e7>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/limit3.9:78
msgid ""
"Max Acceleration\\&. Note that the component becomes unstable with maxa "
"greater than about 1e7 in a 1kHz thread"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/limit3.9:81
msgid "B<limit3>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<smooth-steps> u32 in (default: I<2>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/limit3.9:83
msgid ""
"Smooth out acceleration this many periods before reaching input or max/min "
"limit\\&. Higher values avoid oscillation, but will accelerate slightly more "
"slowly\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: TH
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "LINCURVE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:32
msgid "lincurve - one-dimensional lookup table"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:35
msgid ""
"B<loadrt lincurve> [B<count>=I<N>|B<names>=I<name1>[,I<name2>\\&...]] "
"[B<personality>=I<P1>[,I<P2>\\&...]]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:38
msgid ""
"This component can be used to map any floating-point input to a floating-"
"point output\\&. Typical uses would include linearisation of thermocouples, "
"defining PID gains that vary with external factors or to substitute for any "
"mathematical function where absolute accuracy is not required\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:40
msgid ""
"The component can be thought of as a 2-dimensional graph of points in (x,y) "
"space joined by straight lines\\&. The input value is located on the x axis, "
"followed up until it touches the line, and the output of the component is "
"set to the corresponding y-value\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:42
msgid ""
"The (x,y) points are defined by the x-val-NN and y-val-NN parameters which "
"need to be set in the HAL file using \"setp\" commands\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:44
msgid "The maximum number if (x,y) points supported is 16\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:46
msgid ""
"For input values less than the x-val-00 breakpoint the y-val-00 is "
"returned\\&. For x greater than the largest x-val-NN the yval corresponding "
"to x-max is returned (ie, no extrapolation is performed\\&.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:48
msgid ""
"Sample usage: loadrt lincurve count=3 personality=4,4,4 for a set of three 4-"
"element graphs\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:51
msgid "B<lincurve>\\&.I<N> (requires a floating-point thread)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lincurve.9:56
msgid "B<lincurve>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<in-> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
