msgid "SIM_PARPORT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:32
msgid ""
"sim_parport - A component to simulate the pins of the hal_parport component"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:35
msgid ""
"B<loadrt sim_parport> [B<count>=I<N>|B<names>=I<name1>[,I<name2>\\&...]]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:38
msgid ""
"Sim_parport is used to replace the pins of a real parport without changing "
"any of the pins names in the rest of the config\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:40
msgid ""
"It has pass-through pins (ending in -fake) that allows connecting to other "
"components\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:42
msgid "eg pin-02-in will follow pin-02-in-fake \\*(Aqs logic\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:44
msgid ""
"pin_01_out-fake will follow pin_01_out (possibly modified by pin_01_out-"
"invert)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:46
msgid ""
"It creates all possible pins of both I<in> and I<out> options of the "
"hal_parport component\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:48
msgid ""
"This allows using other hardware I/O in place of the parport (without having "
"to change the rest of the config)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:50
msgid "or simulating hardware such as limit switches\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:52
msgid "it\\(cqs primary use is in Stepconf for building simulated configs\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:54
msgid "You must use the names= option to have the right pin names\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:56
msgid "eg\\&. names=parport\\&.0,parport\\&.1"
msgstr ""

