#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:32
msgid ""
"spindle - Control a spindle with different acceleration and deceleration and "
"optional gear change scaling"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:35
msgid "B<loadrt spindle> [B<count>=I<N>|B<names>=I<name1>[,I<name2>\\&...]]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:38
msgid ""
"This component will control a spindle with adjustable acceleration and "
"deceleration\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"NOTE: This component is unfortunately named and creates pins with names very much like those created by the motion component\\&.\n"
"In nearly every case this is not the documentation page that you are looking for\\&.\n"
"See http://linuxcnc\\&.org/docs/html/man/man9/motion\\&.9\\&.html instead\\&.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:52
msgid ""
"It is designed for use with non-servo spindle drives that have separate fwd/"
"reverse inputs, such as DC drives and inverters\\&. If a spindle encoder is "
"available it is used to tailor the acceleration and deceleration to the "
"spindle load\\&. If not the spindle speed is simulated\\&. The component "
"allows for gearboxes with up to 16 gears\\&. Each gear has individual "
"control of speeds, acceleration, driver gain and direction\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:55
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N> (requires a floating-point thread)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:60
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<select-gear> u32 in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:62
msgid ""
"Select a gear\\&. Must be in the range 0 → number of available gears -1\\&. "
"If you use this, do not use the select\\&.x input pins\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:65
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<commanded-speed> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:67
msgid "Commanded spindle speed (in RPM)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:70
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<actual-speed> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:72
msgid ""
"Actual spindle speed from a spindle encoder (in RPS)\\&. If you do not have "
"a spindle encoder set the simulate_encoder parameter to 1\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:75
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<simulate-encoder> bit in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:77
msgid "If you do not have an encoder, set this to 1\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:80
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<enable> bit in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:82
msgid ""
"If FALSE, the spindle is stopped at the gear\\(cqs maximum deceleration\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:85
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<spindle-lpf> float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:87
msgid ""
"Smooth the spindle-rpm-abs output when at speed, 0 = disabled\\&. Suitable "
"values are probably between 1 and 20 depending on how stable your spindle "
"is\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:90
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<spindle-rpm> float out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:92
msgid ""
"Current spindle speed in RPM\\&.+ve = forward, -ve = reverse\\&. Uses the "
"encoder input if available\\&. If not, uses a simulated encoder speed\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:95
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<spindle-rpm-abs> float out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:97
msgid "Absolute spindle speed in RPM\\&. Useful for spindle speed displays\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:100
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<output> float out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:102
msgid "Scaled output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:105
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<current-gear> u32 out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:107
msgid "Currently selected gear\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:110
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<at-speed> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:112
msgid "TRUE when the spindle is at speed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:115
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<forward> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:117
msgid "TRUE for forward rotation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:120
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<reverse> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:122
msgid ""
"TRUE for reverse rotation\\&. Both forward and reverse are false when the "
"spindle is stopped\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:125
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<brake> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:127
msgid "TRUE when decelerating"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:130
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<zero-speed> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:132
msgid "TRUE when the spindle is stationary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:135
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<limited> bit out"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:137
msgid "TRUE when the commanded spindle speed is E<gt>max or E<lt>min\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:141
msgid "B<motion>(9)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:144
msgid ""
"The following pins are created depending the I<numgears=> parameter\\&. One "
"of each pin is created for each gear\\&. If no gears are specified then one "
"gear will be created\\&. For instance if you have gears=2 on your command "
"line, you will have two scale pins: B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<scale>\\&.B<0> "
"B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<scale>\\&.B<1>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:146
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<scale>\\&.x float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:148
msgid ""
"Scale the output\\&. For multiple gears you would use a different scale for "
"each gear\\&. If you need to reverse the output for some gears, use a "
"negative scale\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:151
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<min>\\&.x float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:153
msgid ""
"Set the minimum speed allowed (in RPM)\\&. The limit output will be TRUE "
"while the commanded speed is between 0 RPM and the min speed\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:156
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<max>\\&.x float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:158
msgid ""
"Set the maximum speed allowed (in RPM)\\&. The limit output will be TRUE "
"while the commanded speed is above this value\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:161
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<accel>\\&.x float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:163
msgid ""
"Set the maximum acceleration\\&. If you do not have a spindle encoder this "
"is in RPM/second\\&. If you do have an encoder the output is the actual "
"speed plus this value\\&. This way the acceleration can be dependent on the "
"spindle load\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:166
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<decel>\\&.x float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:168
msgid ""
"Set the minimum deceleration\\&. If you do not have a spindle encoder this "
"is in RPM/second\\&. If you do have an encoder the output is the actual "
"speed minus this value\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:171
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<speed-tolerance>\\&.x float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:175
msgid ""
"Tolerance for I<at-speed> signal (in RPM)\\&. Actual spindle speeds within "
"this amount of the commanded speed will cause the at-speed signal to go "
"TRUE\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:178
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<zero-tolerance>\\&.x float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:182
msgid "Tolerance for I<zero-speed> signal (in RPM)\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:185
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<offset>\\&.x float in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:187
msgid "The output command is offset by this amount (in RPM)\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:190
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<select>\\&.x bit in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:192
msgid ""
"Selects this gear\\&. If no select inputs are active, gear 0 is selected\\&. "
"If multiple select inputs are active then the highest is selected\\&."
msgstr ""

