#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:49
msgid "Build and install the component using halcompile:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cd mydir\n"
"$ [sudo] halcompile --install userkins\\&.comp\n"
"# Note:\n"
"#      sudo is required when using a deb install\n"
"#      sudo is *not* required for run-in-place builds\n"
"# $ man halcompile for more info\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:66
msgid "Specify userkins in an ini file as:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[KINS]\n"
"KINEMATICS=userkins\n"
"JOINTS=3\n"
"# the number of JOINTS must agree with the\n"
"# number of joints used in your modified userkins\\&.comp\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:82
msgid "Note: the manpage for userkins is not updated by halcompile --install"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:84
msgid ""
"To use a different component name, rename the file (example mykins\\&.comp) "
"and change all instances of userkins to mykins\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:97
msgid ""
"The B<fpin> pin is included to satisfy the requirements of the halcompile "
"utility but it is not accessible to kinematics functions\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:108
msgid ""
"HAL pins and parameters needed in kinematics functions (kinematicsForward(), "
"kinematicsInverse()) must be setup in a function (B<userkins_setup()>) "
"invoked by the initial motion module call to kinematicsType()\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:112
msgid "B<userkins>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<fdemo> (requires a floating-point thread)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:117
msgid "B<userkins>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<fpin> s32 out (default: I<0>)"
msgstr ""

